      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "1.6. Validators",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s011-1-6-validators.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 1.6. Validators\n\nThe core implementation flow for validators is to locate the C2PA Manifest Store, identify the active manifest, validate the claim and signature, check signer trust and credential status, validate assertions and ingredients, validate the asset’s content binding, and return or display validation results.\n\nExamples of validators in the C2PA ecosystem include photo gallery applications, social media platforms, news publishers, and verification tools.\n\nMust Read to Implement Validation\n\n**[Technical Overview](#_technical_overview)**  \n**Read:** All of this section.  \n**Why:**",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A reading path for validators, whose core flow is to locate the C2PA Manifest Store, identify the active manifest, validate the claim and signature, check signer trust and credential status, validate assertions, ingredients and the content binding, and return or display the results; examples are photo galleries, social media platforms, news publishers and verification tools. Required reading: the Technical Overview; selected Glossary terms; parts of Manifests; hard and soft bindings; hashing and signatures in Cryptography; parts of the Trust Model (validation states, trust lists, X.509 certificates); all of Validation, the core validator section; and the standard assertions the product handles. User Experience is needed only when results are shown to users, so as not to mislead them, and Live Media only for live content. Embedding, Assertions, Claims and URI References are listed as helpful context on the data structures.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
