      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "2.1.2. Claim generator",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s016-2-1-2-claim-generator.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 2.1.2. Claim generator\n\nThe non-human (hardware or software) [actor](#_actor) that generates the [claim](#_claim) about an [asset](#_asset) as well as the [claim signature](#claim-signature-definition), thus leading to the [asset](#_asset)'s associated [C2PA Manifest](#_c2pa_manifest).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The claim generator is a component of a larger system, such as a library, software development kit (SDK), or shared service that a signer relies on to generate and embed claims in assets, but is not the Signer itself and thus does not assume responsibility for the content of the Claim or Asse",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the claim generator as the non-human (hardware or software) actor that generates the claim about an asset and the claim signature, leading to the asset's C2PA Manifest. A note says it is a component of a larger system, such as a library, SDK or shared service that a signer relies on, and is not the signer, so it does not take responsibility for the content of the claim or its assertions.",
        "state": "draft",
