      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "2.2.2. Asset metadata",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s023-2-2-2-asset-metadata.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 2.2.2. Asset metadata\n\nNon-technical information about the [asset](#_asset) and its [digital content](#_digital_content).\n\n<a id=\"_asset\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines asset metadata as non-technical information about an asset and its digital content.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s024-2-2-3-asset",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "2.2.3. Asset",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s024-2-2-3-asset.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 2.2.3. Asset\n\nA file or stream of data containing [digital content](#_digital_content), [asset metadata](#_asset_metadata) and optionally, a [C2PA Manifest](#_c2pa_manifest).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> For the purposes of this definition, we will extend the typical definition of \"file\" to include cloud-native and dynamically generated data.\n\n<a id=\"_derived_asset\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines an asset as a file or stream of data containing digital content, asset metadata and, optionally, a C2PA Manifest. A note extends \"file\" here to include cloud-native and dynamically generated data.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s025-2-2-4-derived-asset",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "2.2.4. Derived asset",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s025-2-2-4-derived-asset.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 2.2.4. Derived asset\n\nA [derived asset](#_derived_asset) is an [asset](#_asset) that is created by starting from an existing [asset](#_asset) and performing [actions](#_action) to it that modify its [digital content](#_digital_content).\n\n**EXAMPLE:** An audio stream that has been shortened or a document where pages have been added.\n\n<a id=\"_asset_rendition\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a derived asset as one created from an existing asset by performing actions that modify its digital content, for example a shortened audio stream or a document with added pages.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s026-2-2-5-asset-rendition",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "2.2.5. Asset rendition",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s026-2-2-5-asset-rendition.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 2.2.5. Asset rendition\n\nA representation of an [asset](#_asset) (either as a part of an [asset](#_asset) or a completely new [asset](#_asset)) where the [digital content](#_digital_content) has had a ['non-editorial transformation'](#editorial-transformation-definition) [action](#_action) (e.g., re-encoding or scaling) applied.\n\n**EXAMPLE:** A video file that is re-encoded for reduced screen resolution or network bandwidth.\n\n<a id=\"_composed_asset\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines an asset rendition as a representation of an asset, either part of it or a wholly new asset, whose digital content has undergone a non-editorial transformation such as re-encoding or scaling; the example is a video re-encoded for a lower screen resolution or bandwidth.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s027-2-2-6-composed-asset",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "2.2.6. Composed asset",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s027-2-2-6-composed-asset.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 2.2.6. Composed asset\n\nA composed asset is an [asset](#_asset) that is created by building up a collection of multiple parts or fragments of [digital content](#_digital_content) (referred to as [ingredients](#ingredient_assertion)) from one or more other [assets](#_asset). When starting from an existing [asset](#_asset), it is a special case of a [derived asset](#_derived_asset) - however a [composed asset](#_derived_asset) can also be one that starts from a \"blank slate\".\n\n**EXAMPLES:**\n\n*   A video created by importing existing video clips and audio segments into a \"blank slate\".\n    \n*",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a composed asset as one built from a collection of parts or fragments of digital content, called ingredients, taken from one or more other assets. When it starts from an existing asset it is a special case of a derived asset, but it can also start from a blank slate. Examples are a video assembled from imported clips and audio segments, and an image with another image superimposed on it.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s028-2-2-7-editorial-transformation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "2.2.7. Editorial transformation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s028-2-2-7-editorial-transformation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 2.2.7. Editorial transformation\n\nA type of transformation that alters either the intent or meaning or both of the [digital content](#_digital_content).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Every editorial transformation is a [perceptible transformation](#perceptible-transformation-definition), but not every [perceptible transformation](#perceptible-transformation-definition) is editorial\n\n<a id=\"perceptible-transformation-definition\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines an editorial transformation as one that alters the intent or the meaning (or both) of the digital content. A note says every editorial transformation is perceptible, but not every perceptible transformation is editorial.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s029-2-2-8-perceptible-transformation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "2.2.8. Perceptible transformation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s029-2-2-8-perceptible-transformation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 2.2.8. Perceptible transformation\n\nA type of transformation that alters how the [digital content](#_digital_content) is perceived by humans under normal conditions.\n\n<a id=\"_core_aspects_of_c2pa\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a perceptible transformation as one that alters how humans perceive the digital content under normal conditions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
    {
