      "narrative": null,
      "content": "## 4\\. Standard Terms\n\nThe key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"NOT RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in [BCP 14](https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/bcp14), [RFC 2119](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2119), and [RFC 8174](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8174) when they appear in any casing (upper, lower or mixed).\n\nCDDL Rules and Type Definitions in the CDDL schemas for C2PA constructs are normative. [Schema validation](#schema-validation) is not necessary, nor it is recomm",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that the key words MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT, RECOMMENDED, NOT RECOMMENDED, MAY and OPTIONAL are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14, RFC 2119 and RFC 8174 when they appear in any casing. States that CDDL rules and type definitions in the C2PA CDDL schemas are normative while comments within them are non-normative, and that schema validation is neither necessary nor recommended. If the CDDL schema conflicts with the normative text of the specification, the normative text takes precedence.",
