      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "5.1. Compatibility",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s057-5-1-compatibility.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 5.1. Compatibility\n\nAs the Content Credentials specification has evolved, constructs such as box labels, assertions (and their fields), claims and time stamps have also evolved. New assertions have been added, and some existing assertions and the claim have newer versions with additional fields. In addition, some constructs have been deprecated. In this specification, when a construct is marked as deprecated, that means that a claim generator shall not write that construct (or value), but that a validator should read it.\n\nTo facilitate testing and diagnosing interoperability issues between",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes how constructs such as box labels, assertions, claims and time stamps have evolved, and defines a deprecated construct as one that a claim generator shall not write but that a validator should read. Recommends that a claim generator declare the specification version it used by providing a specVersion key in the claim_generator_info field, which declares that the active manifest was produced per that version and contains no constructs deprecated in it. Requires a validator to be compatible with at least one specification version and to support all non-deprecated constructs of any version it is compatible with, while allowing it to ignore constructs it does not support (deprecated or unknown) and process the rest of the C2PA Manifest. Also recommends that a claim generator performing ingredient validation add a specVersion key to the validation-results-map to declare the version used for the validation procedure.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
