    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s058-5-2-forward-compatibility",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "5.2. Forward Compatibility",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s058-5-2-forward-compatibility.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 5.2. Forward Compatibility\n\nC2PA aims to ensure that Content Credentials created under newer versions of the specification remains parseable and validatable when processed by implementations conforming to earlier versions, wherever practical. Implementations of the C2PA specification should therefore be designed to:\n\n*   Gracefully handle unknown or unrecognized data (e.g., new fields, structures, or claim types) without causing fatal errors.\n    \n*   Preserve the integrity of a C2PA Manifest even when parts of it cannot be fully interpreted.\n    \n*   Indicate partial interpretation to use",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the C2PA aim that Content Credentials created under newer specification versions remain parseable and validatable by implementations of earlier versions wherever practical. Recommends that implementations gracefully handle unknown or unrecognized data without fatal errors, preserve the integrity of a C2PA Manifest even when parts of it cannot be fully interpreted, and indicate partial interpretation to users or downstream systems rather than rejecting the manifest outright. Notes that breaking changes may occasionally be necessary for significant advances or fundamental security, trust or interoperability concerns, in which case versioning guidance and migration considerations will be explicitly documented.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
