      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 8.1. General\n\nIt is expected that each claim generator, used by actors in the system that creates or processes an asset, will create or assemble one or more assertions about when, where, and how the asset was originated or transformed. An assertion is labelled data, typically (though not required to be) in a CBOR-based structure which represents a declaration about an asset. Some of these assertions will contain human-generated information (e.g., alternate text for accessibility) while others will come from machines (software/hardware) providing the information they generated (e.g., camera",
