      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the expectation that each claim generator creates or assembles one or more assertions about when, where and how an asset was originated or transformed, and defines an assertion as labelled data, typically but not necessarily in a CBOR-based structure, representing a declaration about an asset. Notes that some assertions contain human-generated information and others machine-generated information, with examples including metadata, actions performed on the asset, thumbnails of the asset or its ingredients, and content bindings. States that assertions may be redacted by subsequent claims (Section 8.8 Redaction of Assertions) but cannot be modified once made as part of a claim.",
