      "target": "../sections/s070-8-2-1-namespacing.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 8.2.1. Namespacing\n\nString values in C2PA data structures may be organized into namespaces using a period (`.`) as a separator. The C2PA namespace, `c2pa`, shall be the beginning of any string value defined in this specification. In addition to the `c2pa` namespace, the [C2PA namespace registry](https://github.com/c2pa-org/reserved-namespaces/blob/main/namespaces.yml) lists other top-level namespaces.\n\nEntity-specific namespaces, meaning any namespace other than `c2pa` or those on the registry, shall begin with the Internet domain name for the entity, beginning with a valid [IANA top-leve",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that string values in C2PA data structures may be organized into namespaces using a period as a separator, that any string value defined in the specification shall begin with the c2pa namespace, and that the C2PA namespace registry lists other top-level namespaces. Requires entity-specific namespaces (any other than c2pa or registered ones) to begin with the entity's Internet domain name starting with a valid IANA top-level domain, similar to Java packages (e.g. com.litware), so that labels defined by different entities do not collide. Requires the period-separated components of an entity-specific namespace to follow the POSIX or C locale variable naming convention [a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9_-]*, and gives an ABNF for namespaces.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
