      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "8.2.2. Label Naming",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s071-8-2-2-label-naming.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 8.2.2. Label Naming\n\nEach assertion has a label defined either by the C2PA specifications or an external entity. These labels are strings which are namespaced, as described in the preceding clause or by an entity. The most common labels will be defined in the `c2pa` namespace, but labels may use any namespace that follows the conventions. Labels are also versioned with a simple incrementing integer scheme (e.g., `c2pa.actions.v2`). If no version is provided, it is considered as `v1`. The list of publicly known labels can be found in [Chapter 16, _C2PA Standard Assertions_](#_c2pa_standard",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes assertion labels as namespaced strings defined by the C2PA specifications or an external entity, most commonly in the c2pa namespace, and versioned with a simple incrementing integer such as c2pa.actions.v2, where a missing version is considered v1. Points to Chapter 16 C2PA Standard Assertions for publicly known labels, and notes that namespacing for well-established standards is now done through entity-specific namespaces such as org.iso and org.w3. Gives an ABNF for assertion labels and states that label components follow the POSIX or C locale variable naming convention [a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_-]*, with a repeated underscore (__) reserved for labelling multiple assertions of the same type.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
