    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s072-8-3-versioning",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "8.3. Versioning",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s072-8-3-versioning.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 8.3. Versioning\n\nWhen an assertion’s schema is changed, it should be done in a backwards-compatible manner. This means that new fields may be added and existing ones may be marked as deprecated (i.e., can be read, but never written). Existing fields shall not be removed. The label would then consist of an incremented version number, for example moving from `c2pa.actions` (deprecated) to `c2pa.actions.v2`.\n\nSince the addition of optional fields can be done while maintaining backwards compatibility, such fields may be added to an existing assertion’s schema without a change to the version nu",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that changes to an assertion's schema be backwards compatible, so new fields may be added and existing ones marked deprecated (read but never written), while existing fields shall not be removed and the label takes an incremented version number, e.g. moving from c2pa.actions to c2pa.actions.v2. Optional fields may be added without changing the version number. Requires deprecated fields of C2PA standard assertions to be indicated in Chapter 16 C2PA Standard Assertions and forbids claim generators from inserting data into deprecated fields. Requires a non-backwards-compatible change to give the assertion a new label rather than a higher version number, such as the fictional c2pa.component replacing c2pa.ingredient.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s073-8-4-multiple-instances",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "8.4. Multiple Instances",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s073-8-4-multiple-instances.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 8.4. Multiple Instances\n\nMultiple assertions of the same type can occur in the same manifest, but since assertions are referenced by claims via their label, the assertion labels are required to be unique. This is accomplished by adding a double-underscore and a monotonically increasing index to the label. For example, if a manifest contains a single assertion of type `c2pa.metadata`, then the assertion label will be `c2pa.metadata`. If a manifest contains three assertions of this type, the labels will be `c2pa.metadata`, `c2pa.metadata__1` and `c2pa.metadata__2`.\n\nWhen a label includes a v",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that multiple assertions of the same type in one manifest are given unique labels by appending a double underscore and a monotonically increasing index, e.g. c2pa.metadata, c2pa.metadata__1 and c2pa.metadata__2. When a label includes a version number, the instance number follows the versioned label, e.g. c2pa.ingredient.v2__2.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
