      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "8.6. Assertion Store",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s075-8-6-assertion-store.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 8.6. Assertion Store\n\nThe set of assertions referenced by a [claim](#_claims) in a manifest are collected together into a logical construct that is referred to as the _assertion store_. The assertions and assertion store shall be stored as described in [Section 11.5, “Serialization”](#_serialization); in particular, each assertion referenced in a claim’s `created_assertions` or `gathered_assertions` (but not [`redacted_assertions`](#_redaction_of_assertions)) shall be present in the assertion store located in the same C2PA Manifest as the claim.\n\nIn each manifest, there is a single asserti",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the assertion store as the logical collection of assertions referenced by a claim in a manifest, which shall be stored as described in Section 11.5 Serialization. Requires each assertion referenced in a claim's created_assertions or gathered_assertions (but not redacted_assertions) to be present in the assertion store of the same C2PA Manifest as the claim. Notes that each manifest has a single assertion store but an asset may have several, and recommends that each assertion include a randomly-generated salt in the private c2sh box within its JUMBF Description Box (Section 9.4.2.3 Hashing JUMBF Boxes) so subsequent generators can redact assertions securely.",
        "state": "draft",
