      "target": "../sections/s076-8-7-embedded-vs-externally-stored-data.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 8.7. Embedded vs Externally-Stored Data\n\nSome assertion data, due to its size or an infrequent need for it, may be externally hosted. Such data are not embedded in the assertion store, but instead are referenced by URI. This is accomplished through either a [cloud data](#_cloud_data) assertion for remotely-stored C2PA assertions (JUMBF) or an [external reference](#external_reference_assertion) assertion for either remotely stored assertion or non-assertion data. In both cases, the externally hosted data is not retrieved nor validated as part of manifest validation, and is only retrieved an",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes how assertion data that is large or infrequently needed may be hosted externally and referenced by URI instead of being embedded in the assertion store, using either a cloud data assertion for remotely stored C2PA assertions (JUMBF) or an external reference assertion for remotely stored assertion or non-assertion data. In both cases the externally hosted data is not retrieved or validated as part of manifest validation, and is only retrieved and validated when an application specifically needs it, under the rules in Section 14.10 Validate the Assertions.",
        "state": "draft",
