    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s077-8-8-redaction-of-assertions",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "8.8. Redaction of Assertions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s077-8-8-redaction-of-assertions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 8.8. Redaction of Assertions\n\nAssertions that are present in an asset-embedded manifest may be removed from that asset’s manifest when the asset is [used as an ingredient](#_ingredient_storage). This process is called redaction.\n\nRedaction shall be performed either by removing the entire assertion from the manifest’s assertion store or by replacing its content, as described in [Section 14.10.3, “Redacted Assertion Representation”](#_redacted_assertion_representation).\n\nIn addition, a record that something was removed shall be added to the [claim](#_claims) in the form of a [URI reference](",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines redaction as removing assertions from an asset-embedded manifest when the asset is used as an ingredient, and requires it to be done either by removing the entire assertion from the assertion store or by replacing its content per Section 14.10.3 Redacted Assertion Representation. Requires a URI reference to the redacted assertion in the claim's redacted_assertions field, strongly recommends a c2pa.redacted action with a redacted field, and requires an ingredient manifest to be removed from the C2PA Manifest Store when redacting its ingredient assertion leaves no other references to it; because the URI includes the assertion label, the type of removed information remains known. Recommends documenting a redaction with an update manifest unless it accompanies changes to data covered by content bindings. Forbids claim generators from redacting c2pa.actions or c2pa.actions.v2 assertions, and from redacting the hard binding assertion for the current asset when creating an update manifest; validator handling is described in Section 14.10 Validate the Assertions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
