    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s078-8-9-specifications-of-time-in-assertions",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "8.9. Specifications of time in assertions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s078-8-9-specifications-of-time-in-assertions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 8.9. Specifications of time in assertions\n\nThe default specification for a date/time value in an assertion is the date/time format which is serialized in CBOR as tag number `0` ([RFC 8949](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949), 3.4.1) and represented in CDDL as type `tdate`.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> CBOR Tag 0 is described in [RFC 8949](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949) as \"the date-time production in [RFC 3339](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339), as refined by Section 3.3 of [RFC 4287](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4287), representing the point in time described there\". This means",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that the default date/time value in an assertion is serialized as CBOR tag 0 and represented in CDDL as tdate, which requires an explicit timezone or Z. Distinguishes the evidentiary meanings of standard time values (the signer's claim of the time), a claimed time of signing (signer-claimed and not independently authoritative), and a trusted time stamp (TSA evidence about the data submitted to it). Specifies that claim generator timestamp fields use generator-lower-bound-time-type or generator-upper-bound-time-type, taking a direct tdate or a map with a tdate in value and an optional timeStampType, and that a value without timeStampType shall be interpreted as absolute; lowerBound and upperBound give bounds without guaranteeing the actual time and, on start and end fields, bracket when the process or action occurred. Notes that the claimed time of signing uses CBOR tag 1 (seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00Z), that the time stamp assertion uses standard time-stamping formats, and that the different representations allow the most appropriate standards-based form for each use case.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
