      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "9.1. Uniquely Identifying C2PA Manifests and Assets",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s080-9-1-uniquely-identifying-c2pa-manifests-and-asse.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 9.1. Uniquely Identifying C2PA Manifests and Assets\n\nEvery C2PA Manifest is uniquely identified and referenced by a Uniform Resource Name [RFC 8141, URNs](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8141) from the `c2pa` URN namespace, and a C2PA asset is uniquely identified by the `c2pa` URN value of its active manifest. The ABNF for the C2PA URN is described by [ABNF for C2PA URN](#abnf_for_urn).\n\nA `c2pa` URN shall consist of two mandatory and two optional components, in the following order, with colons (`:`) between each section.\n\n*   URN identifier (`urn:c2pa`): REQUIRED.\n    \n*   UUID v4, in s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that every C2PA Manifest is uniquely identified by a URN from the c2pa URN namespace and that a C2PA asset is identified by the c2pa URN of its active manifest. The URN consists of the required urn:c2pa identifier and UUID v4 string, optionally followed by a Claim Generator identifier (no more than 32 ASCII characters that are not control or graphic characters) and a Version and Reason string (a positive integer, an underscore and another positive integer), separated by colons. When a Version and Reason string is present, a Claim Generator identifier shall also be present but may be empty; an ABNF and examples are given. Notes that earlier versions used a UUID URN with the claim generator identifier first, which did not comply with RFC 9562 or RFC 8141, and that the c2pa URN is used, for example, to identify an asset as an ingredient.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
