      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "9.2. Versioning Manifests Due to Conflicts",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s081-9-2-versioning-manifests-due-to-conflicts.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 9.2. Versioning Manifests Due to Conflicts\n\nSituations may arise where it is necessary to re-label a C2PA Manifest due to a conflict of identifiers. For example, if a claim generator had already added an ingredient manifest into the asset’s C2PA Manifest Store, then later added another ingredient which had a manifest with the same label in its manifest store, but this latter version of the manifest was different due, for example, to a manipulation of one of its assertion values. In such a case, the modified version of the ingredient manifest needs to be copied into the asset’s C2PA Manifes",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes situations where a C2PA Manifest must be re-labelled due to an identifier conflict, such as an ingredient manifest with the same label but different content being added to an asset's C2PA Manifest Store, and requires the modified copy to be re-labelled. To re-label, the claim generator shall append a colon if the URN has no Claim Generator identifier string and then, in all cases, append a colon followed by a monotonically increasing integer starting at 1, an underscore, and a reason code, where 1 means conflict with another C2PA Manifest. For example, a second re-labelling due to conflict appends :2_1.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s082-9-3-identifying-non-c2pa-assets",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
