      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "9.3. Identifying Non-C2PA Assets",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s082-9-3-identifying-non-c2pa-assets.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 9.3. Identifying Non-C2PA Assets\n\nWhen working with assets that do not contain a C2PA Manifest, but the asset contains embedded XMP which include values for `xmpMM:DocumentID` and/or `xmpMM:InstanceID` as defined in [XMP Specification Part 2, 2.2](https://github.com/adobe/xmp-docs/blob/master/XMPNamespaces/XMPDataTypes/ResourceEvent.md), those values shall be used as identifiers for the asset.\n\nWhen working with assets that do not contain a C2PA Manifest and do not contain embedded XMP, the claim generator may use any method of its choosing to provide it with a unique identifier.\n\n<a id=\"_",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that, for assets without a C2PA Manifest but with embedded XMP containing xmpMM:DocumentID and/or xmpMM:InstanceID, those values be used as the asset's identifiers. For assets with neither a C2PA Manifest nor embedded XMP, the claim generator may use any method of its choosing to obtain a unique identifier.",
        "state": "draft",
