      "target": "../sections/s084-9-4-1-standard-uris.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 9.4.1. Standard URIs\n\nAll references to information in the manifest, whether stored internally to the asset (i.e., embedded) or stored externally to the asset (e.g., in the cloud), shall be referenced via JUMBF URI references as defined in ISO 19566-5:2023, C.2. These URIs are normally used either as part of a `hashed_uri` or `hashed_ext_uri` data structure.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> [Section 16.4.1.4.6, “Unique Identifiers for Actions”](#unique-identifiers-for-actions) describes an extension to standard JUMBF URIs to allow for the referencing of individual fields within a CBOR Content Type Box. Thi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires all references to information in the manifest, whether embedded or stored externally, to use JUMBF URI references as defined in ISO 19566-5:2023, C.2, normally within a hashed_uri or hashed_ext_uri structure, and notes that the field-referencing extension in Section 16.4.1.4.6 Unique Identifiers for Actions applies only in that context. For a compressed manifest, the URI shall be formed as if the manifest were not compressed, including the label of the c2ma or c2um box but not the c2cm box, and shall not include the label of the brob box. A validator shall treat an internal JUMBF URI reference as unresolved if any label in its path is ambiguous because multiple child boxes share that label.",
