      "title": "9.4.2.1. Embedded",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s086-9-4-2-1-embedded.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 9.4.2.1. Embedded\n\nA `hashed_uri` is used when the URI is for something embedded in the same C2PA Manifest Store.\n\nThis specification provides an equivalent `hashed-uri-map` data structure for schemas using a [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.3.1, “Hashed URI”](#cddl_annex_hashed_uri) for the complete normative schema):\n\nCDDL for hashed URI\n\n```cddl\n; The data structure used to store a reference to a URL within the same JUMBF\n; and its hash. We use a socket/plug here to allow hashed-uri-map to be used in\n; individual files without having the map de",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that a hashed_uri is used when the URI refers to something embedded in the same C2PA Manifest Store, and gives the CDDL hashed-uri-map with a url (JUMBF URI), an optional alg, and a hash byte string. If alg is absent the algorithm is taken from an enclosing structure, the field in this structure is used if both are present, and the structure is invalid if neither supplies one. Because assertion stores shall be in the same C2PA Manifest box as the claim, only self#jumbf URIs are permitted; these may be relative to the entire C2PA Manifest Store (starting with a slash) or to the current manifest, and shall not contain the two-period sequence (..). Examples of both URI forms are given.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
