    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s087-9-4-2-2-external",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "9.4.2.2. External",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s087-9-4-2-2-external.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 9.4.2.2. External\n\nWhen referring to a resource that exists externally to the C2PA Manifest Store, a `hashed-ext-uri-map` data structure is used. It is a variation on the `hashed-uri`, in that it references an external URI instead of a `self#jumbf`. The `hashed-ext-uri` data structure is defined by the `hashed-ext-uri-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.3.2, “Hashed External URI”](#cddl_annex_hashed_ext_uri) for the complete normative schema):\n\nCDDL for hashed external URI\n\n```cddl\n; The data structure used to store a refer",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the hashed-ext-uri-map structure for referencing resources external to the C2PA Manifest Store, a variation of hashed-uri with an http/https url, a mandatory alg, a hash, and optional dc:format, size and data_types fields. Recommends the https scheme to protect privacy in transit but also permits http because data integrity is protected by the hash field, leaving manifest authors to choose. When present, dc:format provides an alternative to the Content-Type header and shall be used as the required format during content negotiation, and data_types may give one or more asset types for more clarity. The optional size field gives the size of the data to be retrieved and may serve validators as a hint alongside the hash, for example about whether to download, validate or both.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s088-9-4-2-3-hashing-jumbf-boxes",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "9.4.2.3. Hashing JUMBF Boxes",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s088-9-4-2-3-hashing-jumbf-boxes.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 9.4.2.3. Hashing JUMBF Boxes\n\nWhen creating a URI reference to any JUMBF box (e.g., [assertions](#_assertions) and [data boxes](#_data_boxes)), the hash shall be performed over the contents of the structure’s JUMBF superbox, which includes both the JUMBF Description Box and all content boxes therein (but does not include the structure’s JUMBF superbox header).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> More details on hashing can be found at [Section 12.1, “Hashing”](#_hashing).\n\nAs described in the latest version of JUMBF (ISO 19566-5:2023), and shown in [Figure 5, “Example `c2pa.actions` assertion”](#example-acti",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires the hash for a URI reference to any JUMBF box, such as assertions and data boxes, to be computed over the contents of the structure's JUMBF superbox, including the JUMBF Description Box and all content boxes but not the superbox header (with more detail in Section 12.1 Hashing). Defines the C2PA salt as a Private field of a JUMBF Description box whose value is a standard box with a 4-byte big-endian length, a box type of c2sh, and a payload of 16 or 32 bytes of randomly generated data. Figure 5 shows an example c2pa.actions assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
