    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s090-10-1-overview",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "10.1. Overview",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s090-10-1-overview.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 10.1. Overview\n\nA **claim** gathers together all the assertions about an asset at a given time including the set of assertions for [binding to the content](#_binding_to_content). The claim is then cryptographically hashed and signed as described in [Section 10.3.2.4, “Signing a Claim”](#_signing_a_claim). A claim is encoded as a JUMBF superbox with the label `c2pa.claim.v2` and a CBOR payload, which shall comply with the Core Deterministic Encoding Requirements of CBOR (see [RFC 8949](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949), clause 4.2.1).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Previous versions supported the use",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a claim as gathering all the assertions about an asset at a given time, including those for binding to content, which is then cryptographically hashed and signed as described in Section 10.3.2.4 Signing a Claim. Specifies that a claim is encoded as a JUMBF superbox labelled c2pa.claim.v2 with a CBOR payload that shall comply with the CBOR Core Deterministic Encoding Requirements. Notes that assertion metadata on claims is deprecated, and that the earlier c2pa.claim label and claim-map are deprecated: validators should still accept them, but claim generators shall not produce them.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
