    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s092-10-2-1-schema",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "10.2.1. Schema",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s092-10-2-1-schema.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 10.2.1. Schema\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `claim-map-v2` and `claim-map` rules in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) for claims with labels `c2pa.claim.v2` and `c2pa.claim`, respectively (see [Section G.2.1, “Claim”](#cddl_annex_claim) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; CDDL schema for a claim map in C2PA\nclaim-map-v2 = {\n  ; uniquely identifies a specific version of an asset\n  \"instanceID\": tstr .size (1..max-tstr-length),\n\n  ; the claim generator of this claim\n  \"claim_generator_info\": generator-info-map,\n\n  ; JUMBF URI r",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL schema for claims: claim-map-v2 for the c2pa.claim.v2 label and the deprecated claim-map for c2pa.claim, with the complete normative schema in Section G.2.1 Claim. claim-map-v2 requires instanceID, claim_generator_info, signature and created_assertions, and optionally allows gathered_assertions, dc:title, redacted_assertions, alg, alg_soft, and the deprecated specVersion and metadata fields; the deprecated claim-map instead carries claim_generator, a claim_generator_info array, an assertions list and dc:format. It also defines generator-info-map with a required name and optional version, icon, operating_system, specVersion and any additional fields. An example claim-map-v2 is given in CBOR diagnostic notation.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
