    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s093-10-2-2-fields",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "10.2.2. Fields",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s093-10-2-2-fields.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 10.2.2. Fields\n\nThe `alg` field shall contain the hash algorithm used to compute the hash for any hashed-uri, hard binding assertion, or hash assertion that does not explicitly define it. The value of this field, if present, shall be a string that is one of the allowed hash algorithms as defined in [Section 12.1, “Hashing”](#_hashing). If the `alg` field is not present, then each hashed-uri, each hard binding assertion, and each hash assertion shall explicitly declare which hashing algorithm is to be used.\n\nIf present, the value of `dc:title` shall be a human-readable name for the asset.",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the claim's fields. The alg field, if present, shall be an allowed hash algorithm from Section 12.1 Hashing and applies to any hashed-uri, hard binding assertion or hash assertion that does not define its own, and if alg is absent each of those shall declare its algorithm explicitly. dc:title, if present, shall be a human-readable name for the asset, though claim generators should instead create a metadata assertion with dc:title; instanceID should be the asset's xmpMM:InstanceID when XMP is present, and otherwise some other unique identifier shall be used. The signature field shall be present with an absolute URI reference to the claim signature in the same C2PA Manifest, and created_assertions shall be present with one or more references to assertions made by the claim, attributed to the signer and including at least a hard binding assertion in a standard manifest. When present, gathered_assertions references assertions provided by other workflow components that are not attributed to the signer, and redacted_assertions references redacted assertions; the notes add that dc:format is no longer in c2pa.claim.v2, that XMP-derived field names do not require XMP, and that the claim-level specVersion is deprecated in favour of the one in claim_generator_info.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
