    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s096-10-2-3-2-generator-info-map",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "10.2.3.2. Generator Info Map",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s096-10-2-3-2-generator-info-map.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 10.2.3.2. Generator Info Map\n\nWhen adding a `claim_generator_info` field, its value is a `generator-info-map` object which shall contain a `name` field. It may also contain either a `version` field or an `icon` field or both. In addition, any other field is permitted, using the standard entity-specific namespacing described in [Section 8.2.1, “Namespacing”](#_namespacing). The data in this object shall represent the non-human (hardware or software) actor that actually generated the claim (aka the claim generator itself).\n\nA claim generator may desire to provide a graphical representation",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that a claim_generator_info value is a generator-info-map that shall contain a name field and may contain version, icon, or both, plus any other fields using entity-specific namespacing, and that it shall represent the non-human (hardware or software) actor that generated the claim. If present, icon shall be a hashed URI to an embedded data assertion labelled c2pa.icon that follows the multiple-instance label rules, with its hash algorithm taken from the hashed URI's alg or else the claim's alg, and Manifest Consumers should also support the data box approach of earlier versions. A specVersion field should be present and, if so, shall contain the SemVer version of the specification the claim generator used to create the manifest (e.g. 2.4.0), which validators should treat as purely informational without changing their validation logic. A JSON example is included.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
