      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "10.3.2.2. Adding Ingredients",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s101-10-3-2-2-adding-ingredients.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 10.3.2.2. Adding Ingredients\n\nIn many authoring scenarios, an actor does not create an entirely new asset but instead brings in other existing assets on which to create their work - either as a derived asset, a composed asset or an asset rendition. These existing assets are called ingredients and their use is documented in the provenance data through the use of an [ingredient assertion](#ingredient_assertion).\n\nWhen an ingredient contains one or more C2PA manifests, those manifests should be inserted into this asset’s C2PA Manifest Store to help ensure that the provenance data is kept in",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes ingredients as existing assets an actor brings in to create a derived asset, composed asset or asset rendition, documented in the provenance data through ingredient assertions. Recommends inserting an ingredient's C2PA Manifests into the asset's C2PA Manifest Store, as described in Section 11.4 Ingredient Storage. If a manifest with the same unique identifier is already present, the two shall be compared: an identical new manifest shall be ignored, while a different one shall be added after its identifier is changed per Chapter 9 Unique Identifiers. If an ingredient's remote manifest cannot be retrieved, the claim generator should use the error code manifest.inaccessible.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
