      "target": "../sections/s102-10-3-2-3-connecting-the-signature.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 10.3.2.3. Connecting the Signature\n\nThe signature cannot be part of the signed payload, but since its label is pre-defined, then the full URI reference is also known. As such, we can include that in the claim by setting the value of the `signature` field of the claim to that URI reference.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This provides the explicit binding of the claim to its signature.\n\n<a id=\"_signing_a_claim\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that although the signature cannot be part of the signed payload, its label is predefined, so its full URI reference is known and is set as the value of the claim's signature field. This provides the explicit binding of the claim to its signature.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
