      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "10.3.2.5.2. Choosing the Payload",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s106-10-3-2-5-2-choosing-the-payload.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 10.3.2.5.2. Choosing the Payload\n\nA previous version of this specification used the same value for the `payload` field in the time stamp as was used in the `Sig_signature` as described in [Section 10.3.2.4, “Signing a Claim”](#_signing_a_claim). This payload is henceforth referred to as a \"v1 payload\" in a \"v1 time stamp\" and is considered deprecated. A claim generator shall not create one, but a validator shall process one if present.\n\nThe \"v2 payload\", of the \"v2 time stamp\", is the value of the `signature` field of the `COSE_Sign1_Tagged` structure created as part of [Section 10.3.2.",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the deprecated v1 payload (in a v1 time stamp) as the same payload value used in the Sig_signature for signing the claim, which a claim generator shall not create but a validator shall process if present. Defines the v2 payload (in a v2 time stamp) as the value of the signature field of the COSE_Sign1_Tagged structure created when signing the claim, including the entire serialized bstr with its major type and length bytes, and requires claim generators to use it when time stamping.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
