    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s107-10-3-2-5-3-obtaining-the-time-stamp",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "10.3.2.5.3. Obtaining the time stamp",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s107-10-3-2-5-3-obtaining-the-time-stamp.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 10.3.2.5.3. Obtaining the time stamp\n\nAll time stamps shall be obtained as described in [RFC 3161](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3161) with the following additional requirements:\n\n*   The `MessageImprint` of the `TimeStampReq` structure ([RFC 3161](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3161), section 2.4.1) shall be computed by creating the `ToBeSigned` value in [RFC 9052](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9052), section 4.4, with the following values for elements of `Sig_structure`:\n    \n    *   The `context` element shall be `CounterSignature`.\n        \n    *   The `payload` element s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires all time stamps to be obtained per RFC 3161 with additional requirements. The MessageImprint of the TimeStampReq shall be computed from the RFC 9052 ToBeSigned value, using a Sig_structure whose context is CounterSignature, whose payload is as described in Section 10.3.2.5.2 Choosing the Payload, and whose other elements follow Section 12.3.3 Computing the Signature. The ToBeSigned value is hashed with an algorithm from the allowed list in Section 12.1 Hashing that the TSA supports (a TSA supporting none cannot be used), preferably the same algorithm as the claim's digital signature. The certReq boolean shall be asserted so that the TSA's certificate chain is provided in the response.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s108-10-3-2-5-4-storing-the-time-stamp",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "10.3.2.5.4. Storing the time stamp",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s108-10-3-2-5-4-storing-the-time-stamp.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 10.3.2.5.4. Storing the time stamp\n\nv1 time stamps (deprecated) are stored in a COSE unprotected header whose label is the string `sigTst`. If present, the value of this header shall be a `tstContainer` defined by [Section G.2.2, “Timestamp Container”](#cddl_annex_tst_container). The content of the `TimeStampResp` structure received in reply from the TSA shall be stored as the value of the `val` property of an element of `tstTokens`.\n\nv2 time stamps shall be stored in a COSE unprotected header whose label is the string `sigTst2`. When present, the value of this header shall be a `tstCon",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that deprecated v1 time stamps are stored in a COSE unprotected header labelled sigTst whose value shall be a tstContainer, with the content of the TSA's TimeStampResp stored as the val of a tstTokens element. v2 time stamps shall be stored in a COSE unprotected header labelled sigTst2 as a tstContainer, with the timeStampToken from the TimeStampResp stored as val and formatted as a DER-encoded RFC 3161 TimeStampToken in a CBOR byte string; a note equates this to the CTT model of the IETF COSE time-stamp header draft, serving as a countersignature over the complete signature structure. If no time stamps are included, neither sigTst nor sigTst2 shall be present. The tstContainer CDDL is given and noted to be a CBOR adaptation of a subset of the JAdES schema, with val as a byte string rather than Base64.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s109-10-3-2-6-credential-revocation-information",
