    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s121-11-5-serialization",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.5. Serialization",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s121-11-5-serialization.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 11.5. Serialization\n\nThe C2PA Manifest Store and individual C2PA Manifests are serialized using the JPEG Universal Metadata Box Format (ISO 19566-5:2023, JUMBF). This serialized format shall be used also in formats that do not natively support JUMBF, or when C2PA Manifest Stores are stored separately from the asset, such as in a separate file or URI location. The following type, label, and content requirements shall apply:\n\n**Table 2. C2PA JUMBF boxes**\n\n| Item | JUMBF type UUID | JUMBF Label | Contents |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| C2PA Manifest Store | `63327061-0011-0010-8000-00AA00389B",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that C2PA Manifest Stores and C2PA Manifests are serialized using JUMBF (ISO 19566-5:2023), and that this format shall also be used in formats without native JUMBF support or when stores are kept separately from the asset. Table 2 gives the JUMBF type UUID, label and contents for the Manifest Store (c2pa), standard manifest (c2ma), update manifest (c2um), compressed manifest (c2cm), deprecated standard manifest type (c2md), Assertion Store (c2as, label c2pa.assertions), Claim (c2cl, label c2pa.claim.v2) and Claim Signature (c2cs, label c2pa.signature). These boxes shall satisfy Section 11.5.3.2 Toggles and Section 11.5.3.3 Labels, and Manifest Consumers shall accept c2md superboxes as standard manifests while claim generators shall not create them.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s122-11-5-1-assertion-store-contents",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.5.1. Assertion Store Contents",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s122-11-5-1-assertion-store-contents.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 11.5.1. Assertion Store Contents\n\nThe [C2PA Assertion Store](#assertion-store-arch) is a JUMBF superbox that shall have the label and type given in [Table 2, “C2PA JUMBF boxes”](#table_c2pa_jumbf_boxes). It shall contain one or more JUMBF superboxes (called C2PA Assertion boxes) whose JUMBF type defines the type of the sub-boxes that contain the assertion data (ISO 19566-5:2023, Annex B). These superboxes shall each have a label as defined in [Standard Assertions](#_c2pa_standard_assertions) and shall contain a JUMBF Description Box, one or more JUMBF Content Boxes and possibly a Padding",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that the C2PA Assertion Store is a JUMBF superbox with the label and type given in Table 2, containing one or more C2PA Assertion superboxes whose JUMBF type defines the type of their content sub-boxes. Each assertion superbox shall have a label as defined in Standard Assertions and contain a JUMBF Description Box, one or more JUMBF Content Boxes and possibly a Padding Box. Recommends CBOR, JSON, Embedded File (bfdb and bidb) or UUID content types while permitting any JUMBF content type and a JUMBF Protection Box per ISO 19566-4:2020, and notes that custom formats such as encrypted data are supported through a UUID Content Box.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s123-11-5-2-compressed-manifests",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.5.2. Compressed Manifests",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s123-11-5-2-compressed-manifests.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 11.5.2. Compressed Manifests\n\nBoth [standard](#_standard_manifests) and [update](#_update_manifests) C2PA Manifests can be compressed, in their entirety. To support this, C2PA defines a new `brob` JUMBF content box, based on a similar box in JPEG-XL (ISO/IEC 18181-2:2024). The `brob` box shall have box ID of `0x62726F62` (`brob`).\n\nFor either type of manifest, the value of the `TYPE` field shall be `c2cm`, the value of the [label field](#jumbf_labels) shall be identical to the label of the compressed manifest superbox, and the contents of the `brob` content box shall be the [RFC 7932](htt",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that standard and update C2PA Manifests can be compressed in their entirety using a new brob JUMBF content box with box ID 0x62726F62, based on a similar JPEG-XL box. A compressed manifest shall have a TYPE of c2cm, a label identical to that of the compressed manifest superbox, and brob contents that are the Brotli-compressed (RFC 7932) bytes of the entire manifest superbox, as shown in Figure 10. Hashing a compressed box follows Section 9.4.2.3 Hashing JUMBF Boxes, covering the Description Box and the brob box with its compressed payload without decompressing it first. Anywhere the specification references a standard or update manifest, a compressed one is also valid.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s124-11-5-3-general-c2pa-jumbf-requirements",
