    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s125-11-5-3-1-processing-rules",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.5.3.1. Processing Rules",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s125-11-5-3-1-processing-rules.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 11.5.3.1. Processing Rules\n\nA C2PA Manifest Consumer shall never process an assertion, assertion store, claim, claim signature or C2PA Manifest that is not contained inside of a C2PA Manifest Store. Additionally, when a C2PA Manifest Consumer encounters a JUMBF box or superbox whose JUMBF type UUID it does not recognize, it shall skip over (and ignore) its contents.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This means that the C2PA Manifest Consumer can process private boxes that it knows about, but ignore ones of which it is unaware.\n\n<a id=\"_toggles\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that a C2PA Manifest Consumer never process an assertion, assertion store, claim, claim signature or C2PA Manifest that is not contained in a C2PA Manifest Store, and that it skip over and ignore the contents of any JUMBF box or superbox whose type UUID it does not recognize. Notes that this lets a consumer process private boxes it knows about while ignoring unknown ones.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s126-11-5-3-2-toggles",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.5.3.2. Toggles",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s126-11-5-3-2-toggles.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 11.5.3.2. Toggles\n\nAll JUMBF Description boxes (ISO 19566-5:2023, A.3) used in a C2PA Manifest require a label and so the _Label Present_ toggle (`xxxxxx1x`) shall be set. In addition, because JUMBF URIs are used to refer to boxes throughout the system (e.g., listing assertions, references to ingredients, etc.), the _Requestable_ toggle (`xxxxxx11`) shall be set.\n\nWhen including a salt in a _PRIVATE_ box as described in [Section 9.4.2.3, “Hashing JUMBF Boxes”](#_hashing_jumbf_boxes), the _Private_ toggle (`xxx1xxxx`) shall also be set.\n\n<a id=\"jumbf_labels\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires the Label Present toggle (xxxxxx1x) and the Requestable toggle (xxxxxx11) to be set on all JUMBF Description boxes used in a C2PA Manifest, because labels are required and boxes are referred to by JUMBF URIs. When a salt is included in a PRIVATE box as described in Section 9.4.2.3 Hashing JUMBF Boxes, the Private toggle (xxx1xxxx) shall also be set.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s127-11-5-3-3-labels",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.5.3.3. Labels",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s127-11-5-3-3-labels.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 11.5.3.3. Labels\n\nAs described in the JUMBF specification (ISO 19566-5:2023, A.3), a label shall be stored as Unicode characters in the UTF-8 encoding and shall be null-terminated. Characters in the ranges U+0000 to U+001F inclusive and U+007F to U+009F inclusive, as well as the specific characters '/', ';', '?', and '#', are not permitted in the label.\n\nBecause labels are used as part of JUMBF URIs, the characters U+FEFF, U+FFFF, and U+D800-U+DFFF shall also not be used.\n\n<a id=\"_unrecognized_boxes\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires JUMBF labels to be stored as null-terminated Unicode characters in UTF-8, per ISO 19566-5:2023, A.3. Labels may not contain characters in the ranges U+0000 to U+001F or U+007F to U+009F, or the characters '/', ';', '?' and '#', and because labels are used in JUMBF URIs, U+FEFF, U+FFFF and U+D800-U+DFFF shall also not be used.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s128-11-5-3-4-unrecognized-boxes",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.5.3.4. Unrecognized Boxes",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s128-11-5-3-4-unrecognized-boxes.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 11.5.3.4. Unrecognized Boxes\n\nThe C2PA Manifest Store (`c2pa`) and C2PA Manifest (`c2ma`, `c2um`, `c2cm`, and `c2md`) may also contain JUMBF boxes and superboxes that satisfy the requirements in [Section 11.5.3.2, “Toggles”](#_toggles) and [Section 11.5.3.3, “Labels”](#jumbf_labels) and whose JUMBF type UUIDs are not defined in this specification.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Allowing other boxes and superboxes enables custom extensions to C2PA as well as enabling the addition of new boxes in future versions of this specification without breaking compatibility.\n\nIf the _Requestable_ and _Label Present",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Allows the C2PA Manifest Store (c2pa) and C2PA Manifests (c2ma, c2um, c2cm and c2md) to contain JUMBF boxes and superboxes whose type UUIDs are not defined in the specification, provided they satisfy Section 11.5.3.2 Toggles and Section 11.5.3.3 Labels, enabling custom extensions and future additions without breaking compatibility. Requires any box or superbox with both the Requestable and Label Present toggles set to be maintained in any updated C2PA Manifest Store, since such boxes are intended to be referenced via JUMBF URIs and removing them could cause downstream workflows to fail.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s129-11-5-4-jumbf-rationale",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.5.4. JUMBF Rationale",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s129-11-5-4-jumbf-rationale.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 11.5.4. JUMBF Rationale\n\nIn order to support many of the requirements of C2PA, C2PA Manifests needed to be stored (serialized) into a structured binary data store that enables some specific functionality including:\n\n*   Ability to store multiple manifests (e.g., parents and ingredients) in a single container.\n    \n*   Ability to refer to individual elements (both within and across manifests) via URIs.\n    \n*   Ability to clearly identify the parts of an element to be hashed.\n    \n*   Ability to store pre-defined data types used by C2PA (e.g., JSON and CBOR).\n    \n*   Ability to store arbi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains why JUMBF (ISO 19566-5:2023) was chosen to serialize C2PA Manifests: it can store multiple manifests in one container, refer to elements within and across manifests via URIs, clearly identify the parts of an element to be hashed, and store both C2PA's predefined data types (e.g. JSON and CBOR) and arbitrary data formats. It is also natively supported by the JPEG family and compatible with the ISO BMFF box model, letting it work with classic image formats such as JPEG/JFIF and PNG as well as 3D and document formats such as PDF. A note explains that using CBOR for the entire manifest was considered but not chosen because CBOR is not a container format, and re-implementing JUMBF's features in CBOR would be a lot of work and would not fully remove the need for a JUMBF/BMFF parser.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s130-11-6-embedding",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.6. Embedding",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s130-11-6-embedding.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 11.6. Embedding\n\nA C2PA Manifest Store can be embedded into a variety of file formats covering media types including images, videos, audio, fonts, and documents. [Appendix A, _Embedding manifests_](#embedding_annex) provides the technical details on how to embed C2PA Manifests into each specifically supported file format.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Many classic image formats such as BMP do not support the embedding of arbitrary data, so the use of an [external manifest](#_external_manifests) is required.\n\n<a id=\"_multiple_step_processing\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States that a C2PA Manifest Store can be embedded into a variety of file formats covering images, video, audio, fonts and documents, with technical details for each supported format in Appendix A Embedding manifests. Notes that many classic image formats such as BMP do not support embedding arbitrary data, so an external manifest is required for them.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s131-11-7-multiple-step-processing",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.7. Multiple Step Processing",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s131-11-7-multiple-step-processing.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 11.7. Multiple Step Processing\n\nSome asset file formats require file offsets of the C2PA Manifest Store and asset content to be fixed before the manifest is signed, so that content bindings will correctly align with the content they authenticate. Unfortunately, the size of a manifest and its signature cannot be precisely known until after signing, which could cause file offsets to change.\n\nAs an example, in [JPEG 1](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPEG) files, the entire C2PA Manifest Store is required to appear in the file before the image data, and so its size will affect the file offsets",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that some file formats require the file offsets of the C2PA Manifest Store and asset content to be fixed before signing so content bindings align, yet the size of the manifest and its signature cannot be precisely known until after signing, citing JPEG 1, where the entire Manifest Store must appear before the image data. Requires a multiple step approach, similar to how PDF signatures are done, to accomplish this.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s132-11-7-1-create-content-bindings",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.7.1. Create content bindings",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s132-11-7-1-create-content-bindings.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 11.7.1. Create content bindings\n\nWhen creating a [standard manifest](#_standard_manifests), its claim shall include one or more content binding assertions in its list of assertions to ensure that the asset is tamper-evident.\n\nCreate the data hash assertion and add it to the assertion store taking into account the following considerations.\n\nIn many cases, such as with JPEG 1, it is not possible to hash the asset in its entirety because the manifest will be embedded in the middle of the file, so the size or location of manifest data will not be known at the time the asset hash is computed.",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a standard manifest's claim to include one or more content binding assertions so that the asset is tamper-evident, and describes creating the data hash assertion using exclusion ranges, where a single hash covers only the asset ranges outside the exclusions (e.g. the claim creator may exclude the APP11 segments holding a manifest in a JPEG 1 file). To prevent insertion attacks a single exclusion range is desirable; when the manifest's size or location is unknown, start and length shall both be zero and pad should be large enough for the values written in the second pass, with at least 16 bytes recommended and pad consisting of all 0x00 bytes. Claim generators shall ensure that changes to pad data or other excluded data cannot change how the asset is interpreted; for JPEG 1, a note says this can be achieved by eliminating padding or by including all APP11 segment headers and 2-byte length fields in the data-hash-map.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s133-11-7-2-create-a-temporary-claim-and-signature",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.7.2. Create a temporary Claim and Signature",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s133-11-7-2-create-a-temporary-claim-and-signature.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 11.7.2. Create a temporary Claim and Signature\n\nAdd the newly created data hash assertion reference to the claim’s assertion list providing a temporary hash value, such as empty spaces.\n\nAt this point, the temporary claim is complete and can be added to the C2PA Manifest being created.\n\nSince the claim is only temporary at this time, it is not possible to sign it. To ensure the claim signature box contains a valid CBOR structure, create a temporary `COSE_Sign1_Tagged` structure as described in {8152}, section 4.2. The `COSE_Sign1_Tagged` is a tag byte followed by a `COSE_Sign1` structure,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes adding the data hash assertion reference to the claim's assertion list with a temporary hash value, such as empty spaces, after which the temporary claim can be added to the C2PA Manifest. Because the temporary claim cannot be signed yet, it describes building a temporary COSE_Sign1_Tagged structure so the claim signature box holds valid CBOR. The four-element array consists of an empty protected header bucket (a zero-length bstr), an unprotected header map with one pad entry holding a zero-filled bstr of the desired padding size (25 kilobytes is recommended initially), a nil payload, and a zero-length bstr signature.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s134-11-7-3-complete-the-c2pa-manifest",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.7.3. Complete the C2PA Manifest",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s134-11-7-3-complete-the-c2pa-manifest.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 11.7.3. Complete the C2PA Manifest\n\nAt this point all of the boxes that comprise the entire C2PA Manifest for the asset are completed and can be (if not already) constructed into its final form. The asset’s C2PA Manifest, along with the manifests of any ingredients, are combined together to form the complete C2PA Manifest Store. The active manifest is required to be the last C2PA Manifest superbox in the C2PA Manifest Store superbox. The C2PA Manifest Store can then be embedded into the asset as discussed in [Appendix A, _Embedding manifests_](#embedding_annex).\n\n<a id=\"_going_back_and_fi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes completing the C2PA Manifest by assembling all its boxes into final form and combining the asset's manifest with the manifests of any ingredients into the complete C2PA Manifest Store. Requires the active manifest to be the last C2PA Manifest superbox in the C2PA Manifest Store superbox, after which the store can be embedded into the asset as discussed in Appendix A, Embedding manifests.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s135-11-7-4-going-back-and-filling-in",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.7.4. Going back and filling in",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s135-11-7-4-going-back-and-filling-in.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 11.7.4. Going back and filling in\n\nNow that the C2PA Manifest Store has been embedded into the asset, the starting offset and the length of the active manifest can be updated in its data hash assertion. It is necessary that when doing so, you do not change the size of the assertion’s box, only its data. This is done by adjusting the value of the `pad` field to be the necessary length to \"fill up\" the remaining bytes.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Preferred/deterministic CBOR serialization of `pad` uses a variable length integer to specify the length of the encoded binary data. When the length goes from",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes updating the data hash assertion with the active manifest's starting offset and length after embedding, without changing the assertion box's size, by adjusting the pad field; a note explains that some padding sizes cannot be expressed in pad alone and can be split between pad and pad2. The updated assertion is then hashed into the reserved space, and the claim is hashed and signed per Section 10.3.2.4, Signing a Claim, with the unprotected pad header shrunk so the claim signature box keeps its size. Requires repeating the multiple step processing with larger padding chosen in Section 11.7.2 if the serialized COSE_Sign1_Tagged exceeds the reserved size, noting that still-valid revocation information should be reusable but a new time stamp will be required. Recommends that claim generators use padding before assertion creation when assertions defined outside this specification may depend on file layout.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s136-11-8-external-manifests",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.8. External Manifests",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s136-11-8-external-manifests.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 11.8. External Manifests\n\nIn some cases, it may not be possible (or practical) to embed a C2PA Manifest Store in an asset. In those cases, keeping the C2PA Manifests externally to the asset is an acceptable model for providing provenance to assets. The C2PA Manifest should be stored in a location, referred to as a manifest repository, that is easily locatable by a Manifest Consumer working with the asset, such as [by reference or URI](#manifests-by-reference). As the C2PA Manifest Store is a JUMBF box, it shall be served with the Media Type for C2PA Manifest Stores, `application/c2pa`.\n\n>",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes keeping C2PA Manifests external to the asset, in a manifest repository easily locatable by a Manifest Consumer (such as by reference or URI), when embedding is not possible or practical. Requires the C2PA Manifest Store to be served with the media type application/c2pa, noting that application/x-c2pa-manifest-store is deprecated. Lists common reasons for external manifests: embedding may be technically impossible, impractical when the manifest store is larger than the asset's digital content, or inappropriate when the asset cannot be modified.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s137-11-8-1-embedding-a-reference-to-an-external-mani",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "11.8.1. Embedding a Reference to an external Manifest",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s137-11-8-1-embedding-a-reference-to-an-external-mani.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 11.8.1. Embedding a Reference to an external Manifest\n\nIf the asset has embedded XMP, and the C2PA Manifest Store will be stored externally, it is recommended that the claim generator add a [`dcterms:provenance`](https://www.dublincore.org/specifications/dublin-core/dcmi-terms/#http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance) key to the XMP, the value (a URI reference) being where to locate the C2PA Manifest Store.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> A previous version of this specification also recommended using this method for references to embedded manifests. Now this mechanism is only for external manifests.\n\nSince f",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that, when an asset has embedded XMP and its C2PA Manifest Store is stored externally, the claim generator add a dcterms:provenance key to the XMP whose value is a URI reference to the manifest store. Notes that this mechanism is now only for external manifests, and that fonts, which do not support XMP, use an equivalent method described in the clause on fonts.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s138-12-cryptography",
