    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s139-12-1-hashing",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.1. Hashing",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s139-12-1-hashing.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 12.1. Hashing\n\nAll cryptographic hashes used in the creation and validation of C2PA Manifests (and their contents) as per the technical requirements of this specification shall be generated using one of the hash algorithms as described in this section. This section defines both:\n\n*   A list of hash algorithms that generators should use for generating hashes of new content and that validators shall support for validating hashes of existing content (the allowed list);\n    \n*   A list of hash algorithms that validators should support for validating hashes of existing content but that generato",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires all cryptographic hashes used in creating and validating C2PA Manifests to use algorithms from an allowed list (generators should use, validators shall support) or a deprecated list (validators should support, generators shall not produce), excluding soft bindings and custom assertions. Requires that an algorithm appear in at most one list, that each output length be listed separately, and that unlisted algorithms be forbidden and not supported optionally. Requires hash outputs to be stored as CBOR byte strings with an algorithm identifier (alg) in the same structure, an enclosing structure, or the claim-map or claim-map-v2, with the nearest identifier taking precedence and the claim-map alg used as the fallback. The allowed list is SHA2-256 (sha256), SHA2-384 (sha384) and SHA2-512 (sha512); SHA-3 is excluded for consistency with the signature algorithm list, and the deprecated list is empty.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s140-12-2-binding-to-content",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.2. Binding to Content",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s140-12-2-binding-to-content.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 12.2. Binding to Content\n\n<a id=\"_overview_4\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Heading that opens section 12.2 Binding to Content; it carries no text of its own.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s141-12-2-1-overview",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.2.1. Overview",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s141-12-2-1-overview.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 12.2.1. Overview\n\nA key aspect to the [standard C2PA manifest](#_standard_manifests) is the presence of one or more data structures, called content bindings, that can uniquely identify portions of the asset. There are two types of bindings that are supported by C2PA - hard bindings and soft bindings. A hard binding (also known as a cryptographic binding) enables the validator to ensure that (a) this manifest belongs with this asset and (b) that the asset has not been modified, by determining values that can match only this asset and no other, not even other assets derived from it or rendi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes content bindings in a standard C2PA manifest, distinguishing hard (cryptographic) bindings, which let a validator confirm the manifest belongs to this asset and that the asset is unmodified, from soft bindings, which are computed from the digital content and help identify derived assets and renditions. Requires that a single manifest contain no more than one hard binding assertion, while allowing zero or more soft binding assertions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s142-12-2-2-hard-bindings",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.2.2. Hard Bindings",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s142-12-2-2-hard-bindings.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 12.2.2. Hard Bindings\n\nEvery hard binding assertion is built from the hash algorithms defined in [Section 12.1, “Hashing”](#_hashing). The specific hard binding assertion used depends on the format and structure of the asset, as described below.\n\n<a id=\"_hashing_using_byte_ranges\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States that every hard binding assertion is built from the hash algorithms defined in Section 12.1, Hashing, and that the specific hard binding assertion used depends on the asset's format and structure, as described in the following subsections.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s143-12-2-2-1-hashing-using-byte-ranges",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.2.2.1. Hashing using byte ranges",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s143-12-2-2-1-hashing-using-byte-ranges.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 12.2.2.1. Hashing using byte ranges\n\nThe simplest type of hard binding that can be used to detect tampering is a cryptographic hashing algorithm, as described in [Section 12.1, “Hashing”](#_hashing), over some or all of the bytes of an asset. This approach can be used on any type of asset, but should only be considered for formats that don’t support one of the forms of box-based hashing.\n\nWhen using this form of hard binding, a [data hash assertion](#_data_hash) is used to define the range of bytes that are hashed (and those that are not). Because a data hash assertion defines a byte ran",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the simplest hard binding as a cryptographic hash over some or all bytes of an asset, usable on any asset type but recommended only for formats that do not support box-based hashing. Specifies that a data hash assertion defines which byte ranges are hashed, works for single binaries or multi-chunk assets, and binds a C2PA Manifest to the codec configuration of live media over Enhanced RTMP (V2), as described in Section 15.5.3.3, Initialization data binding.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s144-12-2-2-2-hashing-using-a-general-box-hash",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.2.2.2. Hashing using a general box hash",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s144-12-2-2-2-hashing-using-a-general-box-hash.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 12.2.2.2. Hashing using a general box hash\n\nWhen an asset’s format is a non-BMFF-based box format, such as JPEG 1, PNG, GIF or others listed [here](#_handling_for_specific_formats), then a [general box hash](#_general_box_hash) assertion should be used. This assertion consists of an array of structures, each one listing one or more boxes (by their name/identifier) and a hash that covers that data of those boxes (and any possible data that may be present in the file between them), along with the algorithm used for [hashing](#_hashing).\n\n<a id=\"_hashing_a_bmff_formatted_asset\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends using a general box hash assertion for non-BMFF box-based formats such as JPEG 1, PNG and GIF. Describes the assertion as an array of structures, each listing one or more boxes by name or identifier with a hash covering those boxes (and any data between them) and the hashing algorithm used.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s145-12-2-2-3-hashing-a-bmff-formatted-asset",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.2.2.3. Hashing a BMFF-formatted asset",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s145-12-2-2-3-hashing-a-bmff-formatted-asset.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 12.2.2.3. Hashing a BMFF-formatted asset\n\nIf the asset is based on [ISO/IEC 14496-12, ISO BMFF](https://www.iso.org/standard/83102.html) then a hard binding optimized for the box-based format (called [BMFF-based hash assertions](#_bmff_based_hash)) may be used instead.\n\nFor a monolithic MP4 file asset where the `mdat` box is validated as a unit, the assertion is validated nearly identically to a data hash assertion. It simply uses a box exclusion list instead of byte ranges to define the range of bytes that are hashed (and those that are not).\n\nFor fragmented MP4 (fMP4) files, the assert",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Permits ISO BMFF-based assets to use BMFF-based hash assertions instead, which for a monolithic MP4 with mdat validated as a unit work nearly like a data hash assertion but use a box exclusion list rather than byte ranges. Requires that, for fragmented MP4 files, the assertion be combined with chunk-specific hashing information located as specified in Section A.5, Embedding manifests into BMFF-based assets, and points to the live media section for hashing individual segments.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s146-12-2-2-4-hashing-unstructured-text-assets",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.2.2.4. Hashing unstructured text assets",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s146-12-2-2-4-hashing-unstructured-text-assets.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 12.2.2.4. Hashing unstructured text assets\n\nFor unstructured text assets that have a C2PA Manifest embedded using Unicode Variation Selectors as described in [Section A.8, “Embedding Manifests into Unstructured Text”](#embedding_manifests_into_unstructured_text), a [data hash assertions](#_data_hash) shall be used. This assertion provides a hard binding mechanism specifically designed for text content where the C2PA Manifest is embedded as a sequence of non-rendering Unicode characters, and its hashing follows the text-specific normalization rules defined in [Validating a text data hash]",
