      "title": "12.2.2.9. Binding Non-C2PA Asset Metadata",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s151-12-2-2-9-binding-non-c2pa-asset-metadata.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 12.2.2.9. Binding Non-C2PA Asset Metadata\n\nOne of the capabilities of a hard binding is that it can exclude parts of an asset, for various reasons. However, a Claim Generator should, where possible, include asset metadata (i.e., metadata outside a C2PA Manifest such as EXIF or XMP) in the hard binding, in order to protect its integrity throughout the asset’s lifecycle.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Only signed C2PA created\\_assertions are attributed to the signer. Any asset metadata outside of this specific mechanism, whether included in hard bindings or not, is not attributed to the signer by this spe",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that a Claim Generator, where possible, include asset metadata outside the C2PA Manifest, such as EXIF or XMP, in the hard binding to protect its integrity. A note clarifies that only signed C2PA created_assertions are attributed to the signer, so metadata covered only by a hard binding is not, whereas serializing it into a c2pa.metadata assertion in created_assertions explicitly signals that the signer asserts it. Recommends copying asset metadata values supported by the common metadata assertion, as described in Appendix C, into such an assertion when the signer can assert them.",
        "state": "draft",
