    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s153-12-2-3-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "12.2.3.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s153-12-2-3-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 12.2.3.1. General\n\nSoft bindings are described using [soft binding assertions](#soft_binding_assertion) such as a fingerprint computed from the [digital content](#_digital_content) or an invisible watermark embedded within the digital content. These soft bindings enable digital content to be matched even if the underlying bits differ.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> For example, an asset rendition in a different resolution or encoding format.\n\nAdditionally, if a C2PA manifest is removed from an asset, but a copy of that manifest remains in a provenance store elsewhere, the manifest and asset may be match",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes soft bindings, expressed through soft binding assertions such as a fingerprint of the digital content or an invisible watermark, as enabling digital content to be matched even when the underlying bits differ, for example in another resolution or encoding. Notes that if a manifest is removed from an asset but a copy remains in a provenance store, soft bindings may be used to match the two. Requires that a soft binding not be used as a hard binding.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
