    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s165-13-2-identity-of-signers",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.2. Identity of Signers",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s165-13-2-identity-of-signers.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 13.2. Identity of Signers\n\nIdentity in the trust model is the means by which a cryptographic signing key (aka credential) is associated with the signer for the basis of making trust decisions based on the claim signature or any structure (including, but not limited to, assertions and claims) signed with that key.\n\nThe credential shall be listed in the COSE protected headers of the `COSE_Sign1_Tagged` structure used for digital signatures in all C2PA manifests. Exactly one instance of an identity credential shall appear in the union of the protected and unprotected headers. `COSE_Sign1_Tagg",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines identity in the trust model as the means of associating a signing key (credential) with the signer for trust decisions about anything signed with that key. Requires the credential to be listed in the COSE protected headers of the COSE_Sign1_Tagged structure, with exactly one credential across protected and unprotected headers, and requires rejecting structures with none or with two or more, including repeats of the same credential. An exception treats the same X.509 chain under both the x5chain string label and integer label 33 as a single credential, with further details in Section 13.5, X.509 Certificates.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s166-13-3-validation-states",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.3. Validation states",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s166-13-3-validation-states.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 13.3. Validation states\n\n<a id=\"_general_4\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Heading that opens section 13.3 Validation states; it carries no text of its own.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
