    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s167-13-3-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.3.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s167-13-3-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.3.1. General\n\nA validator is a Manifest Consumer that will make some [validation](#validation-clause) statements about that asset and its associated active manifest. The process for retrieving these statements is described in the [validation section](#validation-clause). The actor consuming the asset, usually through their user agent and its user interface, then has to interpret those statements to arrive at a set of conclusions of their own about the provenance of the asset they are consuming. These conclusions will be drawn from those statements and the contents of the asset itself.",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes a validator as a Manifest Consumer that makes validation statements about an asset and its active manifest, following the process in the validation section. The actor consuming the asset, usually through a user agent, then interprets those statements and the asset's contents to reach their own conclusions about its provenance.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s168-13-3-2-manifest-states",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.3.2. Manifest States",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s168-13-3-2-manifest-states.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.3.2. Manifest States\n\nBased on these statements, a C2PA Manifest may be one of the following:\n\n*   [Well-Formed](#_well_formed_manifest)\n    \n*   [Valid](#_valid_manifest)\n    \n*   [Trusted](#_trusted_manifest)\n    \n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Any Trusted manifest is also Valid, and any Valid manifest is also Well-Formed.\n\n<a id=\"_asset_states\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists the states a C2PA Manifest may have based on validation statements: Well-Formed, Valid and Trusted. Notes that any Trusted manifest is also Valid, and any Valid manifest is also Well-Formed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s169-13-3-3-asset-states",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.3.3. Asset States",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s169-13-3-3-asset-states.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.3.3. Asset States\n\nIf a validator reports that the portions of the asset that are covered by content bindings have not been modified since the active manifest was produced \\[[Section 14.12, “Validate the Asset’s Content”](#_validate_the_assets_content)\\], and its active manifest is either [Valid](#_valid_manifest) or [Trusted](#_trusted_manifest), then the asset itself is a Valid asset.\n\n<a id=\"_well_formed_manifest\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a Valid asset as one whose content-binding-covered portions a validator reports as unmodified since the active manifest was produced (per Section 14.12, Validate the Asset's Content) and whose active manifest is Valid or Trusted.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s170-13-3-4-well-formed-manifest",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.3.4. Well-Formed Manifest",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s170-13-3-4-well-formed-manifest.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.3.4. Well-Formed Manifest\n\nA C2PA Manifest is Well-Formed if validation determines that each of the following is true:\n\n*   The manifest’s contents abide by the normative requirements of this specification, that are validated via the [validation process](#_validation_process).\n    \n*   Only those assertions allowed for the [specific type](#_types_of_manifests) of the manifest are present \\[[Section 14.10.1, “Validate the correct assertions for the type of manifest”](#_validate_the_correct_assertions_for_the_type_of_manifest)\\].\n    \n*   The assertions of the manifest meet all the requi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a Well-Formed C2PA Manifest as one where validation determines that its contents meet the normative requirements checked by the validation process, only assertions allowed for its manifest type are present (Section 14.10.1), its assertions meet all assertion requirements (Section 14.10.4), and any ingredients meet all ingredient requirements (Section 14.11).",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s171-13-3-5-valid-manifest",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.3.5. Valid Manifest",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s171-13-3-5-valid-manifest.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.3.5. Valid Manifest\n\nA C2PA Manifest is Valid if validation determines that each of the following is true:\n\n*   The manifest is Well-Formed \\[[Section 13.3.4, “Well-Formed Manifest”](#_well_formed_manifest)\\].\n    \n*   The manifest has not been modified since the manifest was signed \\[[Section 12.3.6, “Cryptographic validation”](#_cryptographic_validation)\\].\n    \n*   The claim signature receives a success code of `claimSignature.validated` \\[[Section 14.7, “Validate the Signature”](#_validate_the_signature)\\].\n    \n*   Validation of the claim signature validity period receives the suc",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a Valid C2PA Manifest as one that is Well-Formed, unmodified since signing, has a claim signature with success code claimSignature.validated, receives claimSignature.insideValidity for the signature validity period, and whose signer credential is not rejected with signingCredential.ocsp.revoked. States that a Valid manifest's claim can be attributed to the claim generator identified by the claim's claim_generator_info field.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s172-13-3-6-trusted-manifest",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.3.6. Trusted Manifest",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s172-13-3-6-trusted-manifest.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.3.6. Trusted Manifest\n\nA C2PA Manifest is Trusted if validation determines that each of the following is true:\n\n*   The manifest is Valid \\[[Section 13.3.5, “Valid Manifest”](#_valid_manifest)\\].\n    \n*   The signing credential of the C2PA Manifest receives the success code of `signingCredential.trusted` \\[[Section 14.7, “Validate the Signature”](#_validate_the_signature)\\].\n    \n\n<a id=\"_trust_lists\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a Trusted C2PA Manifest as one that is Valid and whose signing credential receives the success code signingCredential.trusted under Section 14.7, Validate the Signature.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s173-13-4-trust-lists",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.4. Trust Lists",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s173-13-4-trust-lists.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 13.4. Trust Lists\n\n<a id=\"_c2pa_signers\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Heading that opens section 13.4 Trust Lists; it carries no text of its own.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s174-13-4-1-c2pa-signers",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.4.1. C2PA Signers",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s174-13-4-1-c2pa-signers.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.4.1. C2PA Signers\n\nA validator shall maintain the following information for evaluating C2PA signers:\n\n*   A list of accepted Extended Key Usage (EKU) values.\n    \n*   For each accepted EKU value, a list of \"trust anchor configurations\".\n    \n\nAn individual trust anchor configuration shall include the X.509 certificate for that trust anchor. Additionally, the configuration should include a \"notBefore\" date/time, before which there is no trust for that trust anchor configuration. If the trust for that trust anchor configuration has ended, it should also include a \"notAfter\" date/time, af",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a validator to maintain a list of accepted Extended Key Usage (EKU) values and, for each, a list of trust anchor configurations, each including the trust anchor's X.509 certificate and recommended to include notBefore and (when trust has ended) notAfter date/times. Requires that a configuration not be used for claim signatures whose timestamp, or the current time if none, falls before notBefore or after notAfter. Requires the list for the c2pa-kp-claimSigning EKU to include the C2PA Trust List, and recommends letting users configure additional anchors for that or other EKUs and offering default or externally maintained lists. Notes that including id-kp-emailProtection or id-kp-documentSigning alongside c2pa-kp-claimSigning can improve compatibility with older validators.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s175-13-4-2-time-stamping-authorities",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.4.2. Time Stamping Authorities",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s175-13-4-2-time-stamping-authorities.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.4.2. Time Stamping Authorities\n\nA validator shall maintain a list of trust anchor configurations for Time Stamping Authorities (TSAs), which shall be separate from the lists [for C2PA signers](#_c2pa_signers).\n\nAn individual TSA trust anchor configuration shall include the X.509 certificate for that trust anchor. Additionally, the configuration should include a \"notBefore\" date/time, before which there is no trust for that trust anchor configuration. If the trust for that trust anchor configuration has ended, it should also include a \"notAfter\" date/time, after which there is no trust",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a validator to maintain trust anchor configurations for Time Stamping Authorities (TSAs) separately from the C2PA signer lists, each including the X.509 certificate and recommended to include notBefore and notAfter date/times. Requires that a configuration not be used for time-stamps asserting times outside those bounds, and that the list include the C2PA TSA Trust List. Recommends allowing users to configure additional TSA trust anchor stores, and permits offering default or externally maintained lists.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s176-13-4-3-private-credential-storage",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.4.3. Private Credential Storage",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s176-13-4-3-private-credential-storage.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 13.4.3. Private Credential Storage\n\nA validator may also allow the user to create and maintain a private credential store of signing credentials. This store is intended as an \"address book\" of credentials they have chosen to trust based on an out-of-band relationship. If present, the private credential store shall only apply to validating signed C2PA manifests, and shall not apply to validating time stamps. If present, the private credential store shall only allow trust in signer credentials directly; entries in the private credential store cannot issue credentials and shall not be includ",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Permits a validator to let users maintain a private credential store, an address book of signing credentials trusted through out-of-band relationships. Requires that the store apply only to validating signed C2PA manifests (not time stamps), trust only signer credentials directly, and never act as trust anchors. Requires that the store not be pre-configured and that entries be added or removed only at the user's request.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s177-13-5-x-509-certificates",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "13.5. X.509 Certificates",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s177-13-5-x-509-certificates.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 13.5. X.509 Certificates\n\nX.509 Certificates are stored as defined by [RFC 9360](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9360) (_CBOR Object Signing and Encryption (COSE): Header Parameters for Carrying and Referencing X.509 Certificates_). For convenience, the definition of `x5chain` is copied below.\n\n> **IMPORTANT:**\n> This specification adds additional requirements beyond those of [RFC 9360](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9360), which are listed after the quoted text. In particular, this specification requires all intermediate certificate authorities' certificates of the signer’s certifica",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that X.509 certificates are stored per RFC 9360, quoting its x5chain definition, and adds requirements beyond it. Requires claim generators to include the signer's certificate and all intermediate CA certificates in x5chain, recommends omitting the root certificate, and notes that the first certificate's public key validates the signature. Requires claim generators to use only integer label 33 (the string label x5chain is deprecated) and to place the header only in the protected bucket. Requires validators to accept either label from either bucket, treat both labels together as one credential using label 33, and reject the signature as malformed if the same label appears in both buckets.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
