      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.1.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s184-14-1-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.1.1. Description\n\nValidation of a C2PA Manifest is a multi-step process that involves validating the assertions, claim & associated claim signature contained within it along with (for active manifests, only) validation of any associated hard bindings. This validation process is performed by a validator, which is a hardware or software actor that implements the validation algorithms described in this clause.\n\n<a id=\"_phases_of_validation\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes validation of a C2PA Manifest as a multi-step process covering its assertions, claim and claim signature, plus any associated hard bindings for active manifests only. Defines a validator as a hardware or software actor that implements the validation algorithms in this clause.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
