    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s189-14-2-2-validation-structures",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.2.2. Validation Structures",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s189-14-2-2-validation-structures.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.2.2. Validation Structures\n\nThe following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) schema defines the data structures used for validation results (see [Section G.7.3, “Validation Result Structures”](#cddl_annex_validation_result_structs) for the complete normative schema):\n\nCDDL for Validation Results\n\n```cddl\n; custom status codes\n$status-code /= tstr .regexp \"([\\\\da-zA-Z_-]+\\\\.)+[\\\\da-zA-Z_-]+\"\n\nstatus-map = {\n  \"code\": $status-code,         ; A label-formatted string that describes the status\n\n  ; At most one of \"url\" and \"resourceUrl\" may be present.\n  ; \"url\": JUM",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines, in CDDL, the data structures for validation results, with a complete normative schema in Section G.7.3. These include status-map (a code, at most one of url or resourceUrl, an optional explanation, and a deprecated success flag), status-codes-map with success, informational and failure arrays, and trust-list-uri-map with uri, type and optional identifier. Also defines validation-results-map with optional activeManifest, ingredientDeltas, specVersion, and either trustListUri (deprecated) or trustListUris, and ingredient-delta-validation-result-map with ingredientAssertionURI and validationDeltas.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s190-14-3-displaying-manifest-information",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.3. Displaying Manifest Information",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s190-14-3-displaying-manifest-information.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 14.3. Displaying Manifest Information\n\nManifest Consumers should not display data from manifests which are not [Valid](#_valid_manifest) nor from assets which are not [Valid](#_asset_states). If the Manifest Consumer chooses to display such data, it shall include as part of the display:\n\n*   a warning about the lack of validity,\n    \n*   a warning that the data shall not be attributed to the manifest’s signer, and in the case of an ingredient manifest, additional not to the asset’s manifest’s signer.\n    \n\n> **NOTE:**\n> In authoring scenarios, it is desirable to more prominently raise warn",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that Manifest Consumers not display data from manifests or assets that are not Valid. Requires that, if such data is displayed anyway, the display include a warning about the lack of validity and a warning that the data shall not be attributed to the manifest's signer (or, for an ingredient manifest, to the asset's manifest's signer). A note says authoring scenarios should raise warnings more prominently.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
