      "title": "14.4.3. For Hashed Ext URIs",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s194-14-4-3-for-hashed-ext-uris.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.4.3. For Hashed Ext URIs\n\nSome parts of a C2PA Manifest utilize a `hashed_ext_uri` structure for encapsulating an external URI, its hash and the algorithm used to compute the hash. If there is an `alg` field in the `hashed_ext_uri` structure, it shall be used as the hashing algorithm. If the `alg` field is not present in the `hashed_ext_uri` structure, the failure code of `algorithm.unsupported` shall be used.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The `alg` field is mandatory in `hashed_ext_uri`, so no recursive procedure to determine the hash algorithm is necessary.\n\n<a id=\"_algorithm_validation\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires the alg field of a hashed_ext_uri structure, which encapsulates an external URI and its hash, to be used as its hashing algorithm, and requires the failure code algorithm.unsupported if it is absent. Notes that alg is mandatory in hashed_ext_uri, so no recursive lookup is needed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
