      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.5.2.2. Special Considerations for PDF",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s200-14-5-2-2-special-considerations-for-pdf.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.5.2.2. Special Considerations for PDF\n\nPDF files support a technology called \"incremental update\", where information is appended to the end of the document instead of modifying the original. This requires that PDF files support multiple C2PA Manifest Stores - though there shall only be one per update section.\n\nIf there are multiple C2PA Manifest Stores present in a single update section, they shall all be considered as invalid and the validation should treat this as if no manifests were located. However, any C2PA Manifest Stores present in early updates of the PDF or of the original P",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes how PDF incremental updates require support for multiple C2PA Manifest Stores, but only one per update section. Requires multiple stores in a single update section to be considered invalid (treated as if no manifests were located), while stores in earlier updates or the original PDF remain valid and are processed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s201-14-5-2-3-special-considerations-for-html",
      "types": [
