      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.5.2.4. Special Considerations for Structured Text",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s202-14-5-2-4-special-considerations-for-structured-t.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.5.2.4. Special Considerations for Structured Text\n\nFor assets consisting of structured text, the C2PA Manifest Store shall be located by following the procedure defined in [Section A.9, “Embedding Manifests into Structured Text”](#embedding_manifests_into_structured_text). The validator shall read the file in binary mode and search for the `-----BEGIN C2PA MANIFEST-----` and `-----END C2PA MANIFEST-----` delimiters. If the delimiters are not found, only one delimiter is found, or more than one manifest block is found, the asset shall be treated as if no manifests were located.\n\nIf a m",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires locating the C2PA Manifest Store for structured text per Section A.9 by reading the file in binary mode and searching for the -----BEGIN C2PA MANIFEST----- and -----END C2PA MANIFEST----- delimiters, treating the asset as having no manifests if delimiters are missing, unpaired or there is more than one block. Requires extracting and whitespace-trimming the reference between delimiters. Specifies resolving a data: URI only if it has media type application/c2pa and base64 encoding, resolving other URIs per Section 14.5.3 (retrieval is optional; if not retrieved, no manifests are treated as located), and otherwise treating the asset as having no manifests.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s203-14-5-2-5-special-considerations-for-append-only-",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.5.2.5. Special Considerations for Append-Only Text Files",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s203-14-5-2-5-special-considerations-for-append-only-.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.5.2.5. Special Considerations for Append-Only Text Files\n\nFor append-only plain-text files and JSONL streams, the C2PA Manifest Store shall be located by following the procedure defined in [Section A.3.17, “Embedding manifests into append-only text files”](#_embedding_manifests_into_append_only_text_files). The validator shall:\n\n1.  Read the file in binary mode and scan from the end, line by line, for the last complete sentinel line. For plain-text files, this is a line beginning with `-----BEGIN C2PA CHECKPOINT-----` and ending with `-----END C2PA CHECKPOINT-----`; for JSONL files, a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires locating the C2PA Manifest Store for append-only plain-text files and JSONL streams per Section A.3.17 by scanning in binary mode from the end for the last complete sentinel line (a BEGIN/END C2PA CHECKPOINT line for plain text, or a JSON object with a c2pa:checkpoint member for JSONL). Requires treating the asset as having no manifests and reporting manifest.appendOnlyText.noSentinel if no such line is found or it is malformed. Specifies extracting and trimming the reference, decoding valid application/c2pa base64 data: URIs (otherwise reporting manifest.appendOnlyText.noSentinel) and resolving other URIs per Section 14.5.3, reporting manifest.inaccessible if retrieval fails. The located store is that of the active checkpoint, with earlier checkpoints found by following the chain described in Section 14.12.6.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
