      "title": "14.5.3.1. By Reference",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s208-14-5-3-1-by-reference.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.5.3.1. By Reference\n\nIf there is no embedded C2PA Manifest Store, the following attempts should be made to locate one at a remote location. Once a C2PA Manifest Store is located, the validation process should proceed with that manifest as the active manifest (and therefore not continue looking for additional manifests). The following attempts should be made in order:\n\n*   If the asset was retrieved via an HTTP connection, the [Link Header](#_by_link_header) clause below describes how to find a manifest via the `Link` header.\n    \n*   If the asset has any XMP in the standard asset loca",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that, when no store is embedded, a validator attempt in order to locate a remote C2PA Manifest Store via an HTTP Link header, an XMP dcterms:provenance URI, a font C2PA table with non-zero activeManifestUriLength, sidecar files named with an added or replacement .c2pa extension, or a similarly named entry in the same archive, stopping at the first found. Permits looking in other places if these fail. Requires the manifest.inaccessible error code when a documented remote manifest is missing or unreachable, and rejection with manifest.inaccessible.encrypted or manifest.inaccessible.malformed when a retrieved store is unreadable due to encryption or cannot be interpreted as valid.",
        "state": "draft",
