      "target": "../sections/s209-14-5-3-2-by-link-header.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.5.3.2. By `Link` header\n\nIf the asset was retrieved via an HTTP connection, the validator should look in the header of the HTTP response for a `Link` header, as defined in [RFC 8288](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8288), containing a parameter of `rel=c2pa-manifest`. If present, a C2PA Manifest Store can be retrieved from that URI reference. The URI will be a standard `http` or `https` URI, such as https://c2pa.org/image.c2pa.\n\nIt is also possible to use the link relation to refer to the C2PA Manifest Store that is embedded inside an asset through the use of a [JUMBF URI](#_uri_ref",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that, for assets retrieved over HTTP, a validator look for a Link header (per RFC 8288) with rel=c2pa-manifest, from whose http or https URI the C2PA Manifest Store can be retrieved. Describes that the link may also refer to an embedded store using a JUMBF URI fragment to the C2PA Manifest Store superbox, and requires validators to ignore any childlabel portion since references to specific manifests are not permitted. Notes that HTTP refers to the protocol in RFC 9110, not only the http:// scheme.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s210-14-5-4-decompression",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.5.4. Decompression",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s210-14-5-4-decompression.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.5.4. Decompression\n\nAs described [previously](#_compressed_manifests), both standard and update manifests can be compressed. When a compressed manifest is encountered, a validator shall decompress it before proceeding with the standard validation process. If the data contained in the `brob` box of a compressed manifest is not either a standard or update manifest or if the decompression fails, the validator shall reject the manifest with a failure code of `manifest.compressed.invalid`.\n\n<a id=\"_validating_a_match\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a validator to decompress compressed standard or update manifests before standard validation. Requires rejection with manifest.compressed.invalid if decompression fails or the brob box data is not a standard or update manifest.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s211-14-5-5-validating-a-match",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.5.5. Validating a Match",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s211-14-5-5-validating-a-match.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.5.5. Validating a Match\n\nA validator may wish to validate that the located C2PA Manifest Store is indeed the one associated with asset.\n\nIf the C2PA Manifest Store was located then the hard binding assertion present in its active manifest shall be used to validate that it is the matching manifest and whether the asset has been modified without manifest updates. If the hard binding does not match, it is unknown if that is because of (a) modification of the asset or (b) the wrong C2PA Manifest Store was located. Accordingly, the validator shall treat this as a non-matching hard binding a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes that a validator may wish to confirm that the located C2PA Manifest Store belongs to the asset. Requires using the active manifest's hard binding assertion for this, and, since a mismatch could mean either modification or the wrong store, requires treating it as a non-matching hard binding and rejecting with assertion.dataHash.mismatch, assertion.boxesHash.mismatch, assertion.collectionHash.mismatch, assertion.segmentHash.mismatch or assertion.bmffHash.mismatch depending on the assertion type.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s212-14-6-locating-and-validating-the-claim",
