    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s213-14-6-1-locating",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.6.1. Locating",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s213-14-6-1-locating.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.6.1. Locating\n\nOnce the manifest to be validated has been located (hereafter referred to as the \"current manifest\"), the claim is found by locating, within the current manifest, the JUMBF Superbox with a label of `c2pa.claim.v2` (or `c2pa.claim` for files with older claim structures) and a JUMBF type UUID of `6332636C-0011-0010-8000-00AA00389B71` (`c2cl`). Note that the JUMBF type UUID is the same for both the new (with `c2pa.claim.v2` label) and old (with `c2pa.claim` label) claim formats. There shall only be one such box in the current manifest. If more than one is located, the C2PA",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies locating the claim within the current manifest as the JUMBF superbox labelled c2pa.claim.v2 (or c2pa.claim for older claims) with JUMBF type UUID 6332636C-0011-0010-8000-00AA00389B71 (c2cl), which is the same for both formats. Requires exactly one such box, rejecting the manifest with claim.multiple if more than one is found.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s214-14-6-2-validating",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.6.2. Validating",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s214-14-6-2-validating.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.6.2. Validating\n\nIf the content of the claim is not well-formed CBOR, the claim shall be rejected with a failure code of `claim.cbor.invalid`.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Well-formed CBOR is defined in [RFC 8949](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949), Appendix C.\n\nFor a \"c2pa.claim.v2\", the following fields are expected to be present in the CBOR object. If any are absent, then the claim shall be rejected with a failure code of `claim.malformed`.\n\n*   `instanceID`\n    \n*   `signature`\n    \n*   `created_assertions`\n    \n*   `claim_generator_info`\n    \n\nIf the `claim_generator_info` field does not c",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a claim whose content is not well-formed CBOR to be rejected with claim.cbor.invalid. Requires a c2pa.claim.v2 to contain instanceID, signature, created_assertions and claim_generator_info, and requires rejection with claim.malformed if any is missing or if claim_generator_info lacks a name field. Requires any icon field in the generator-info-map to be validated as described in Section 14.10.4.3, Validation of References.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s215-14-7-validate-the-signature",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.7. Validate the Signature",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s215-14-7-validate-the-signature.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 14.7. Validate the Signature\n\nThe validator shall retrieve the URI reference for the signature from the value of the claim’s `signature` field and resolve the URI reference to obtain the COSE signature. If the `signature` field is not present, or the URI cannot be resolved, or the URI does not resolve to a location within the same C2PA Manifest box (as the claim), then the claim shall be rejected with a failure code of `claimSignature.missing`.\n\nFor all types of C2PA Manifests, the validation of the credential used in the signature shall be performed according to [Chapter 13, _Trust Model_",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires the validator to resolve the claim's signature field to the COSE signature, rejecting with claimSignature.missing if it is absent, unresolvable or outside the same C2PA Manifest box. Requires credential validation per Chapter 13, rejecting with signingCredential.invalid for unacceptable credentials and algorithm.unsupported for algorithms not on the allowed or deprecated lists. Requires checking for a valid time stamp first, then recommends verifying a chain of trust to a trust anchor configuration while honouring notBefore and notAfter, assigning signingCredential.trusted or rejecting with signingCredential.untrusted. Requires then verifying the signature per Section 12.3, assigning claimSignature.validated or rejecting with claimSignature.mismatch, and states that headers in the rest of the chapter mean the union of protected and unprotected headers.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s216-14-8-validate-the-time-stamp",
