    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s218-14-8-1-1-embedded-in-the-claim-signature",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.8.1.1. Embedded in the Claim Signature",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s218-14-8-1-1-embedded-in-the-claim-signature.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.8.1.1. Embedded in the Claim Signature\n\nIf either the `sigTst` or `sigTst2` header is present, then the `tstTokens` array is expected to contain a single `tstToken`. If the header contains more than one `tstToken`, the validator shall issue a `timeStamp.malformed` informational code and ignore the time stamps.\n\nA validator that supports `sigTst` shall perform the following procedures to validate the time stamp response:\n\n*   Retrieve the `val` property from the `tstToken`, which shall be an RFC3161-compliant `TimeStampResp` (time stamp response).\n    \n*   Check the value of the `statu",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that when a sigTst or sigTst2 header is present its tstTokens array is expected to hold a single tstToken, and requires issuing timeStamp.malformed and ignoring the time stamps if there is more than one. Requires a validator supporting sigTst to take the val property as an RFC 3161 TimeStampResp, issue timeStamp.malformed and ignore it if the PKIStatusInfo status is not 0 (granted) or 1 (grantedWithMods), and otherwise use its timeStampToken. Requires a validator for sigTst2 to take the val property as an RFC 3161 timeStampToken.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s219-14-8-1-2-referenced-by-a-time-stamp-assertion",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.8.1.2. Referenced by a time stamp assertion",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s219-14-8-1-2-referenced-by-a-time-stamp-assertion.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.8.1.2. Referenced by a time stamp assertion\n\nIf a validator has already located a TimeStampToken in a `sigTst` or `sigTst2` header, that passes validation (as per [Section 14.8.2, “Validating the TimeStampToken”](#_validating_the_timestamptoken)), then it shall skip this step. When no such header exists or the TimeStampToken located there did not pass validation, this step shall be followed.\n\nIf a validator had previously located any [time stamp assertions](#timestamp_assertion), which were then maintained in a mapping of C2PA Manifest identifiers to TimeStampTokens, then the validato",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a validator to skip this step if a TimeStampToken from a sigTst or sigTst2 header has already passed validation, and to follow it otherwise. Requires that, if time stamp assertions were previously mapped from C2PA Manifest identifiers to TimeStampTokens, the validator use the token mapped to the current manifest's identifier, trying each one if several exist until one passes. States that no error is raised when the identifier is absent from the mapping.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s220-14-8-2-validating-the-timestamptoken",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.8.2. Validating the TimeStampToken",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s220-14-8-2-validating-the-timestamptoken.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.8.2. Validating the TimeStampToken\n\nAll validators shall continue the process as follows:\n\n*   If the signature algorithm in the `timeStampToken` is not on the allowed or deprecated list in [Section 12.3, “Digital Signatures”](#_digital_signatures), then the validator shall issue a `timeStamp.untrusted` informational code and ignore the time stamp.\n    \n*   Validate the signature in the `timeStampToken`, as described in [RFC 5652](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5652), Section 5.6. If the signature is not valid, then the validator shall issue a `timeStamp.mismatch` informational code",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires validators to check the timeStampToken's signature algorithm, signature, messageImprint presence, imprint hash algorithm, imprint match against the claim (sigTst) or COSE signature field (sigTst2), TSA certificate trust chain, and that genTime falls within the TSA and CA certificates' validity, issuing informational codes such as timeStamp.untrusted, timeStamp.mismatch, timeStamp.malformed or timeStamp.outsideValidity and ignoring the time stamp on failure. Requires issuing timeStamp.trusted and timeStamp.validated when all checks pass, then checking genTime against the claim signing certificate chain to return claimSignature.insideValidity or reject with claimSignature.outsideValidity. Notes that a failed time stamp does not by itself reject the manifest, that time stamps stay valid after the TSA credential expires, and that TSA revocation status is not required. Requires validators to use the attested time when a trusted, validated time stamp is present, and otherwise to use the current time to return claimSignature.insideValidity or reject with claimSignature.outsideValidity.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s221-14-8-3-validating-the-claimed-time-of-signing",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.8.3. Validating the \"claimed time of signing\"",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s221-14-8-3-validating-the-claimed-time-of-signing.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.8.3. Validating the \"claimed time of signing\"\n\nA validator may choose to validate the \"claimed time of signing\" as attested by the value present in the `iat` protected header. If the `iat` header is present, the validator may validate that the attested time falls within the validity period of the signer’s certificate and all CA certificates up to the trust anchor, and not later than the time attested by any associated trusted time stamp. If the validator does the validation of this value, and it falls inside the validity period, the validator shall return the `timeOfSigning.insideValid",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Permits a validator to check that the claimed time of signing in the iat protected header falls within the validity period of the signer's certificate and CA certificates and is no later than any trusted time stamp. Requires that a validator performing this check return the informational code timeOfSigning.insideValidity or timeOfSigning.outsideValidity accordingly.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s222-14-9-validate-the-credential-revocation-informat",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.9. Validate the Credential Revocation Information",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s222-14-9-validate-the-credential-revocation-informat.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 14.9. Validate the Credential Revocation Information\n\nDiscovery of the revocation status of the signer’s certificate and all CA certificates that are part of the trust chain is important to determining whether a given certificate is considered valid and trusted.\n\nFor CA certificates, the validator should determine revocation status as indicated in the Authority Information Access (AIA) extension as described in [RFC 5280](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5280), section 4.2.2.1. The validator should make use of relevant OCSP responses included in the C2PA Manifest if the AIA extension indi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes determining the revocation status of the signer's certificate and CA certificates in the trust chain as important to deciding validity and trust. Recommends determining CA certificate status via the AIA extension and any included OCSP responses, and requires rejection with signingCredential.untrusted if a CA certificate was revoked at the trusted time stamp time or current time. For the signer's certificate, requires treating it as not revoked when revocation status is unsupported, and validating stapled rVals OCSP responses and any certificate status assertions in other manifests per Section 14.9.1, trying each until one passes. Recommends that an online validator query the OCSP responder per Section 14.9.2 if no revocation information is found in the C2PA Manifest Store.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s223-14-9-1-determining-revocation-through-ocsp-respo",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.9.1. Determining revocation through OCSP responses in the C2PA Manifest Store",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s223-14-9-1-determining-revocation-through-ocsp-respo.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.9.1. Determining revocation through OCSP responses in the C2PA Manifest Store\n\nA validator shall decode OCSP responses per the requirements of [RFC 6960](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6960), in particular requirements 1 through 4 of section 3.2. If an OCSP response is accepted, and if all of the following requirements are met, then this establishes that the relevant certificate was not revoked at the time of signing.\n\n*   The claim signature has an attested time provided by a valid signed time stamp.\n    \n*   There exists a `SingleResponse` in the `responses` array of the `tbsRespo",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a validator to decode OCSP responses per RFC 6960, including requirements 1 through 4 of section 3.2. Specifies that an accepted response establishes the certificate was not revoked at signing when the claim signature has a valid time stamp, a SingleResponse has status good with the current time no earlier than thisUpdate and the attested time before thisUpdate or within the (thisUpdate,nextUpdate) or (thisUpdate,producedAt + 24 hours) interval, and the signer is an authorized responder. Requires the validator then to issue signingCredential.ocsp.notRevoked or perform an online OCSP check, and to reject with signingCredential.ocsp.revoked if a response meets all conditions except that certStatus is revoked.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s224-14-9-2-determining-revocation-from-online-ocsp-r",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.9.2. Determining revocation from online OCSP response",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s224-14-9-2-determining-revocation-from-online-ocsp-r.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.9.2. Determining revocation from online OCSP response\n\nIf, for a given certificate, no OCSP response in the C2PA Manifest Store satisfies the conditions in [Section 14.9.1, “Determining revocation through OCSP responses in the C2PA Manifest Store”](#ocsp_stapled), or if the claim signature does not have a time stamp, the validator may choose to query the OCSP responder, per [RFC 6960](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6960), with the responder `accessLocation` found via [RFC 6960](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6960), section 3.1.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Querying the credential status method",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Permits a validator to query the OCSP responder online when no stored response satisfies Section 14.9.1 or the claim signature lacks a time stamp, noting that such queries can reveal the asset being validated. Requires signingCredential.ocsp.skipped if the check is not performed and signingCredential.ocsp.inaccessible if no response is received. Specifies that an accepted response establishes non-revocation when the time stamp time (or current time if no valid time stamp) falls within (thisUpdate,nextUpdate), certStatus is good or revoked with removeFromCRL, and the signer is an authorized responder, or when a revoked status with another reason has a revocationTime after a valid attested time stamp falling within that interval. Requires signingCredential.ocsp.notRevoked in those cases, otherwise signingCredential.ocsp.unknown for an unknown status or rejection with signingCredential.ocsp.revoked.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
