    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s228-14-10-1-2-standard-manifest-assertions",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.1.2. Standard Manifest Assertions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s228-14-10-1-2-standard-manifest-assertions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.10.1.2. Standard Manifest Assertions\n\nIf it is a [standard manifest](#_standard_manifests):\n\n1.  Validate that there is exactly one [hard binding to content](#_binding_to_content) assertion - either a `c2pa.hash.data`, a `c2pa.hash.boxes`, a `c2pa.hash.collection.data`, a `c2pa.hash.segment`, `c2pa.hash.bmff.v2` (deprecated), or a `c2pa.hash.bmff.v3`. If no such assertion is present, the manifest shall be rejected with a failure code of `claim.hardBindings.missing`. If there is more than one such assertion, the manifest shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.multipleHardB",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the assertion checks for a standard manifest: there shall be exactly one hard binding assertion (c2pa.hash.data, c2pa.hash.boxes, c2pa.hash.collection.data, c2pa.hash.segment, the deprecated c2pa.hash.bmff.v2, or c2pa.hash.bmff.v3), otherwise rejection with claim.hardBindings.missing or assertion.multipleHardBindings. It also requires at most one c2pa.ingredient assertion with relationship parentOf (else manifest.multipleParents) and at least one actions assertion in created_assertions or gathered_assertions (else claim.actions.missing). Finally, a c2pa.created or c2pa.opened action must appear in the first actions assertion of exactly one of those two lists, else the manifest is rejected with assertion.action.malformed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s229-14-10-1-3-update-manifest-assertions",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.1.3. Update Manifest Assertions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s229-14-10-1-3-update-manifest-assertions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.10.1.3. Update Manifest Assertions\n\nIf it is an [update manifest](#_update_manifests):\n\n1.  Validate that exactly one ingredient assertion is present and that its `relationship` is `parentOf`. If there is not (i.e., either it is missing, there are more than one, or the value of `relationship` is not `parentOf`), the manifest shall be rejected with a failure code of `manifest.update.wrongParents`.\n    \n2.  Validate that there are no `c2pa.hash.data`, `c2pa.hash.boxes`, `c2pa.hash.collection.data`, `c2pa.hash.segment`, `c2pa.hash.bmff.v2` (deprecated), `c2pa.hash.bmff.v3`, or [thumbnail",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the assertion checks for an update manifest: exactly one ingredient assertion with relationship parentOf must be present, otherwise rejection with manifest.update.wrongParents. The manifest shall be rejected with manifest.update.invalid if it contains any hard binding assertions (c2pa.hash.data, c2pa.hash.boxes, c2pa.hash.collection.data, c2pa.hash.segment, c2pa.hash.bmff.v2, c2pa.hash.bmff.v3), thumbnail assertions, or c2pa.hash.multi-asset assertions. Any action in c2pa.actions or c2pa.actions.v2 assertions must use one of the values supported for update manifests, else the same failure code applies.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
