    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s230-14-10-2-preparing-the-list-of-redacted-assertion",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.2. Preparing the list of redacted assertions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s230-14-10-2-preparing-the-list-of-redacted-assertion.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.10.2. Preparing the list of redacted assertions\n\nA validator, when processing a claim, shall gather the set of redacted assertions for each ingredient’s manifest (if present) based on each JUMBF URI listed in its `redacted_assertions` field. A claim’s `redacted_assertions` field shall never include a JUMBF URI to any of its own assertions.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Assertions can be redacted from ingredient assets at any point in the final asset’s provenance history, and not necessarily by the claim generator that first uses an ingredient asset as an ingredient.\n\nFor more details, refer to the [S",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a validator processing a claim to gather the set of redacted assertions for each ingredient's manifest from the JUMBF URIs in its redacted_assertions field, and forbids a claim's redacted_assertions from referencing any of its own assertions. A note explains that assertions can be redacted at any point in the asset's provenance history, not only by the claim generator that first used the ingredient; further detail is in section 14.11.3.2 Performing explicit validation.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s231-14-10-3-redacted-assertion-representation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.3. Redacted Assertion Representation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s231-14-10-3-redacted-assertion-representation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.10.3. Redacted Assertion Representation\n\nA redacted assertion may be represented in the assertion store either by being removed entirely, or by having its labelled assertion container retained with the JUMBF Content boxes within it replaced by a single UUID Content box whose `ID` field has a value of `CAA98EEE-9D4D-F80E-86AD-4DFFCA263973` (called the C2PA Redaction UUID) and whose `DATA` field contains only zeros (binary `0x00` values).\n\nA validator shall accept either representation as a validly redacted assertion, as described in [Section 14.10.4, “Assertion Validation”](#_assertion_",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that a redacted assertion may either be removed entirely from the assertion store or keep its labelled assertion container with its content boxes replaced by a single UUID Content box carrying the C2PA Redaction UUID (CAA98EEE-9D4D-F80E-86AD-4DFFCA263973) and a DATA field of only zeros. A validator shall accept either representation as validly redacted.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
