    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s233-14-10-4-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.4.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s233-14-10-4-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.10.4.1. General\n\nEach assertion in the `created_assertions` and `gathered_assertions` fields of the claim (and in the `assertions` field of a v1 claim) is a `hashed_uri` structure. For each assertion, the validator shall first determine if the URI reference in the `url` field is in the [list of redacted assertions](#_preparing_the_list_of_redacted_assertions).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Even though the assertions listed in the `gathered_assertions` field were not created by the claim generator, they are still part of the Claim and are therefore also validated according to this validation algorith",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the general validation procedure for each hashed_uri in a claim's created_assertions and gathered_assertions (or a v1 claim's assertions). Redacted assertions are treated as valid unless labelled c2pa.actions or c2pa.actions.v2 (rejected with assertion.action.redacted); other assertions must resolve within the same manifest (else assertion.outsideManifest or assertion.missing) and their computed hash must match (else assertion.hashedURI.mismatch, otherwise assertion.hashedURI.match is recorded). The claim shall also be rejected for malformed CBOR or non-conforming JSON (assertion.cbor.invalid or assertion.json.invalid), for assertions in the store that the claim does not reference (assertion.undeclared), and for redacted_assertions URIs pointing into the claim's own manifest (assertion.selfRedacted). Assertion metadata is not validated except that processStart must not be later than processEnd, else assertion.metadata.malformed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s234-14-10-4-2-specific-assertion-validation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.4.2. Specific Assertion Validation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s234-14-10-4-2-specific-assertion-validation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.10.4.2. Specific Assertion Validation\n\nFor each assertion, the validator shall check the assertion’s label and if it is listed below, the validator shall perform the specific validation steps for that assertion type. If the assertion’s label is not listed below, then that type of assertion does not require any additional validation steps beyond those already described.\n\n*   `c2pa.cloud-data`, [Section 14.10.4.2.1, “`c2pa.cloud-data` validation”](#_c2pa_cloud_data_validation)\n    \n*   `c2pa.external-reference`, [Section 14.10.4.2.2, “`c2pa.external-reference` validation”](#_c2pa_extern",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires the validator to check each assertion's label and perform the specific validation steps for listed types: c2pa.cloud-data, c2pa.external-reference, c2pa.actions or c2pa.actions.v2, c2pa.linked-resource-integrity, c2pa.metadata, c2pa.session-keys, c2pa.time-stamp and c2pa.alternative-content-representation; unlisted types need no further steps. A note says ingredient assertions are validated separately under section 14.11 Validate the Ingredients. Any hashed_uri or hashed_ext_uri field in a standard assertion shall be validated per section 14.10.4.3 Validation of References, except the activeManifest field of c2pa.ingredient.v3 and the externalResources entries of c2pa.linked-resource-integrity, which have their own procedures.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s235-14-10-4-2-1-c2pa-cloud-data-validation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.4.2.1. `c2pa.cloud-data` validation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s235-14-10-4-2-1-c2pa-cloud-data-validation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 14.10.4.2.1. `c2pa.cloud-data` validation\n\nIf the assertion’s label is `c2pa.cloud-data`:\n\n1.  Check that the assertion contains the following fields: `label`, `size`, and `location`. If any of those fields are missing, the claim shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.cloud-data.malformed`.\n    \n2.  If the `label` field of the external assertion is any of the following values, the claim shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.cloud-data.hardBinding`.\n    \n    1.  `c2pa.hash.bmff.v2` (deprecated)\n        \n    2.  `c2pa.hash.bmff.v3`\n        \n    3.  `c2pa.hash.bo",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies validation of c2pa.cloud-data assertions: the label, size and location fields must be present, otherwise rejection with assertion.cloud-data.malformed. The claim shall be rejected with assertion.cloud-data.hardBinding if the external label is a hard binding or multi-asset hash label, with assertion.cloud-data.actions if an update manifest references an actions label, and with assertion.cloud-data.malformed if the label is an actions, cloud-data or ingredient label. The location field is validated per section 14.10.5.2 Validation of External References, and if retrieved, the JUMBF box label must match the label field or the claim is rejected with assertion.cloud-data.labelMismatch.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
