    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s237-14-10-4-2-3-c2pa-linked-resource-integrity-valid",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.4.2.3. `c2pa.linked-resource-integrity` validation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s237-14-10-4-2-3-c2pa-linked-resource-integrity-valid.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 14.10.4.2.3. `c2pa.linked-resource-integrity` validation\n\nIf the assertion’s label is `c2pa.linked-resource-integrity`:\n\n1.  Check that the assertion appears in the claim’s `created_assertions` array. If it does not, the claim shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.linkedResourceIntegrity.notCreated`.\n    \n2.  Check that the assertion’s `resources` field is an object containing either a non-empty `externalResources` array, or a non-empty `relativeResources` array together with an `alg` field. If the `resources` field is missing or matches neither of these shapes, the claim",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies validation of c2pa.linked-resource-integrity assertions: the assertion must be in created_assertions (else assertion.linkedResourceIntegrity.notCreated) and its resources field must hold a non-empty externalResources array or a non-empty relativeResources array with an alg field (else assertion.linkedResourceIntegrity.malformed). Each well-formed entry receives exactly one terminal code, including a resourceUrl field: skipped if not retrieved, or match, inaccessible, sizeMismatch, formatMismatch or hashMismatch, none of which cause rejection. External entries need url, alg and hash and follow section 14.10.5.2 Validation of External References with the mismatch codes remapped to informational ones. Relative entries need uri and hash, the shared alg is checked per section 14.4.4 Algorithm validation, and a decoded uri containing a path segment of exactly .. causes rejection with assertion.linkedResourceIntegrity.invalidURI before retrieved data is checked for size, format and hash.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
