      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 14.10.4.2.4. `c2pa.actions` validation\n\nIf the assertion’s label is `c2pa.actions` or `c2pa.actions.v2`:\n\nThe `when`, `whenStart`, and `whenEnd` fields are claim generator provided timestamps annotate the time within which an action occurred. Validators shall apply the syntax and internal-consistency checks below but shall not compare these fields with an external time source.\n\n1.  Ensure that it has an `actions` field. If not, the claim shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.action.malformed`.\n    \n2.  For each action in the `actions` list:\n    \n    1.  If the assertion’s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies validation of c2pa.actions and c2pa.actions.v2 assertions, noting that when, whenStart and whenEnd get syntax and consistency checks but shall not be compared to an external time source. An actions field is required, and in v2 when may not appear with whenStart or whenEnd and whenStart must not be later than whenEnd (else assertion.action.malformed); c2pa.created or c2pa.opened is only allowed as the first action of the first actions assertion. Actions c2pa.opened, c2pa.placed, c2pa.removed, c2pa.deleted, c2pa.transcoded and c2pa.repackaged must reference ingredient assertions with the expected relationship and manifest location, otherwise assertion.action.ingredientMismatch (with an informational assertion.action.ingredientLocationMismatch for a v2 claim whose ingredient is listed in a different field). It further covers c2pa.redacted needing a resolvable JUMBF URI (else assertion.action.redactionMismatch), validation of icon fields and relatedAssertions entries, and the requirement that c2pa.watermarked or c2pa.watermarked.bound actions be accompanied by a c2pa.soft-binding assertion (else assertion.action.softBindingMissing).",
