      "target": "../sections/s245-14-10-5-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.10.5.1. General\n\nA [cloud data](#_cloud_data) assertion or a hashed [external reference](#external_reference_assertion) assertion contains URI references to (and hashes of) externally hosted data. Those references are not retrieved and validated as part of standard validation. A validator shall first successfully validate a claim before attempting to retrieve the external data referenced. A validator shall not attempt to retrieve external data from a rejected claim. As the retrieval of external data is optional, the inability to retrieve or validate external data shall not cause a cla",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States that externally hosted data referenced by cloud data or hashed external reference assertions is not retrieved during standard validation; a validator shall first successfully validate the claim and shall not retrieve external data from a rejected claim. Because retrieval is optional, failure to retrieve or validate external data shall not cause rejection. A validator that does retrieve such data shall follow section 14.10.5.2 Validation of External References, may apply the countermeasures of section 14.10.5.3 Retrieval Security, and shall validate retrieved labelled assertions as if they were embedded.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
