      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.5.2. Validation of External References",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s246-14-10-5-2-validation-of-external-references.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.10.5.2. Validation of External References\n\nThe following procedure shall be used to validate the external data referenced in a cloud data or hashed external reference assertion. Network retrieval performed as part of this procedure may apply the countermeasures described in [Section 14.10.5.3, “Retrieval Security”](#_retrieval_security).\n\n1.  Resolve the URI reference in the `url` field and retrieve its data. If the `url` field is not present, the validator aborts the attempt by applying a countermeasure described in [Section 14.10.5.3, “Retrieval Security”](#_retrieval_security), or",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the procedure for validating external data from cloud data or hashed external reference assertions. The validator resolves the url and aborts if it is missing, a countermeasure is applied, or retrieval fails; it then returns assertion.hashedURI.mismatch without providing the data if the retrieved representation's length differs from size or its Content-Type differs from the declared content type (from dc:format, defaulting to application/jumbf for cloud data, with content_type ignored). For a hashed_ext_uri, the hash is computed with the algorithm determined per section 14.4.3 For Hashed Ext URIs; a missing or mismatched hash yields assertion.hashedURI.mismatch, otherwise assertion.hashedURI.match is recorded and the data is provided to the application.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
