    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s247-14-10-5-3-retrieval-security",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.5.3. Retrieval Security",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s247-14-10-5-3-retrieval-security.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.10.5.3. Retrieval Security\n\nA validator performing network retrieval under [Section 14.10.5.2, “Validation of External References”](#_validation_of_external_references) (or any other clause that references this section) may apply the countermeasures described in this section before and during each retrieval attempt, regardless of which assertion type initiated the retrieval.\n\nWhere network retrieval is performed on the validator’s behalf by a platform that the validator does not control, and the validator is therefore unable to apply one or more of the countermeasures described in thi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Permits a validator performing network retrieval to apply the countermeasures in this section before and during each retrieval attempt, regardless of which assertion type triggered it. If retrieval is done by a platform the validator does not control and cannot apply the countermeasures, the validator may route retrieval through a component that can, such as a server-side service, or may decline to retrieve. A note gives a browser-based validator as an example and recalls that skipping optional retrieval does not cause a claim to be rejected.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
