      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.10.5.3.1. Permitted schemes and identifiers",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s248-14-10-5-3-1-permitted-schemes-and-identifiers.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 14.10.5.3.1. Permitted schemes and identifiers\n\nA validator may limit automated retrieval performed under this procedure to the `https` URI scheme, and may decline to dereference other schemes (such as `file` or `ftp`) and non-network identifiers.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Unencrypted `http` is discouraged by standard industry practice.\n\nA validator may reject a URI whose authority component contains a `userinfo` subcomponent (i.e. `user:password@host`) before a retrieval attempt is made.\n\n<a id=\"_credential_handling\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Permits a validator to limit automated retrieval to the https URI scheme and to decline other schemes such as file or ftp and non-network identifiers, noting that unencrypted http is discouraged by industry practice. A validator may also reject a URI whose authority contains a userinfo subcomponent before attempting retrieval.",
        "state": "draft",
