      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s251-14-10-5-3-4-redirect-handling.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 14.10.5.3.4. Redirect handling\n\nA validator may limit the number of HTTP redirects it will follow for a single validation operation (see [Section 14.10.5.3.6, “Resource limits”](#_resource_limits)), and may refuse to follow a redirect from an HTTPS URI to an HTTP URI. If the redirect limit is exceeded or a downgrade redirect is encountered, the validator may abort the retrieval.\n\nBefore a redirected request is sent, a validator may apply the countermeasures in [Section 14.10.5.3.1, “Permitted schemes and identifiers”](#_permitted_schemes_and_identifiers), [Section 14.10.5.3.2, “Credenti",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Permits a validator to limit the number of HTTP redirects it follows per validation operation and to refuse HTTPS-to-HTTP redirects, aborting retrieval if either occurs. Before sending a redirected request, a validator may apply the scheme, credential and address countermeasures of sections 14.10.5.3.1 to 14.10.5.3.3 to the redirect target exactly as for the initial request.",
        "state": "draft",
