      "target": "../sections/s253-14-10-5-3-6-resource-limits.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 14.10.5.3.6. Resource limits\n\nFor the purposes of this section, a _retrieval attempt_ is a single request-response exchange, including a request made to a redirect target, and a _validation operation_ is the complete process of resolving, retrieving, decoding, and validating the data referenced by one `hashed_ext_uri`, `unhashed_ext_uri`, or cloud data `location`, including all redirects followed for that reference.\n\nA validator may enforce, for each validation operation:\n\n*   a maximum number of redirects, as described in [Section 14.10.5.3.4, “Redirect handling”](#_redirect_handling);",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a retrieval attempt as a single request-response exchange and a validation operation as the full process of resolving, retrieving, decoding and validating the data for one hashed_ext_uri, unhashed_ext_uri or cloud data location, including redirects. Permits a validator to enforce per-operation limits on redirects, encoded bytes read, decoded representation bytes, decompression nesting depth and an overall deadline, and per-claim limits on total retrieval attempts and concurrent operations. If an enforced limit is exceeded, the validator may abort and discard partial data; a note says the size field gives an a priori bound on decoded bytes usable as a read limit.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
