      "target": "../sections/s255-14-11-1-explanation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.11.1. Explanation\n\nA validator shall perform the [validation steps](#_validation_process) for the asset being presented and its active manifest. If any of the steps conclude the active manifest is invalid, that manifest shall be rejected with the indicated failure code.\n\nAn asset’s active manifest may list one or more ingredients, through the use of [ingredient assertions](#ingredient_assertion). Some of those ingredients may have their own manifests associated with them, and some of those manifests may themselves have ingredients and ingredient manifests.\n\n<a id=\"_processing_ingredien",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a validator to perform the validation steps for the presented asset and its active manifest, rejecting the manifest with the indicated failure code if any step finds it invalid. Explains that an active manifest may list ingredients via ingredient assertions, some of which may have their own manifests with further ingredients.",
