    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s262-14-11-3-2-performing-explicit-validation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.11.3.2. Performing explicit validation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s262-14-11-3-2-performing-explicit-validation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.11.3.2. Performing explicit validation\n\nIf the `relationship` field is not present in an ingredient assertion, the assertion shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.ingredient.malformed`.\n\nThe value of the `relationship` field shall be one of the following: `parentOf`, `inputTo`, or `componentOf`. If the value of the `relationship` field is not one of these, the assertion shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.ingredient.malformed`.\n\nIf both an `activeManifest` and a `digitalSourceType` field are present, the assertion shall be rejected with a failure code of",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies explicit checks on ingredient assertions, each failing with assertion.ingredient.malformed: the relationship field must be present and be parentOf, inputTo or componentOf, and activeManifest and digitalSourceType must not both be present. If relatedAssertions is present it must be a non-empty array whose hashed URIs validate per section 14.10.4.3 and resolve to assertions in the same manifest that are not ingredient or actions assertions and whose label ends with .ingredient, ignoring any multiple-instance suffix. A referenced assertion that has been redacted causes the informational code assertion.redacted to be recorded.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s263-14-11-3-3-performing-recursive-validation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.11.3.3. Performing recursive validation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s263-14-11-3-3-performing-recursive-validation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.11.3.3. Performing recursive validation\n\nThe validator shall recursively validate all ingredient manifests in the asset, for example using a depth-first search as described below. A validator need not implement the algorithm exactly as described, but the results of the validation shall be equivalent to the results of this algorithm.\n\n1.  Create two empty lists:\n    \n    1.  A list to hold the `hashed_uri` values of all ingredient manifests used in the asset, anywhere in its lineage.\n        \n    2.  A list to hold the JUMBF URIs of all redacted assertions in the asset, anywhere in its",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires the validator to recursively validate all ingredient manifests, with results equivalent to the described depth-first algorithm. The algorithm collects lists of ingredient manifest hashed_uri tuples (activeManifest or c2pa_manifest plus claimSignature) and redacted assertion JUMBF URIs across the lineage, rejecting with claim.missing or assertion.selfRedacted where appropriate, skipping unresolvable, mismatched or zeroed ingredient assertions and returning any validationResults status codes. Each ingredient manifest with matching redacted assertions is then validated by the claim signature hash method, otherwise by either that method or the manifest hash method, with validationResults entries reconciled against the validation output. A v3 ingredient with activeManifest but no validationResults yields assertion.ingredient.malformed, and validators should ignore other manifests in the store that are not in the ingredient list, for compatibility with custom and future constructs.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
