    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s264-14-11-3-3-1-claim-signature-hash-validation-meth",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.11.3.3.1. Claim Signature Hash Validation Method",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s264-14-11-3-3-1-claim-signature-hash-validation-meth.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 14.11.3.3.1. Claim Signature Hash Validation Method\n\nThis method includes a full validation of the ingredient’s claim, like that performed for the active manifest, except that content bindings are not evaluated:\n\n1.  Resolve the URI reference in the `url` value of the `claimSignature` field to obtain the ingredient’s claim signature box. If the URI reference cannot be resolved, or the `claimSignature` field is not present, the ingredient claim is rejected with a failure code of `ingredient.claimSignature.missing`.\n    \n2.  Determine the hash algorithm identifier (or possible failure cod",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the claim signature hash validation method, a full validation of the ingredient's claim without evaluating content bindings. The claimSignature url is resolved (else ingredient.claimSignature.missing) and its hash compared with the hash field, rejecting with ingredient.claimSignature.mismatch if absent or unequal; on a match, ingredient.claimSignature.validated is issued and the signature, time stamp and revocation information are validated per sections 14.7 to 14.9. Redacted assertions with a matching manifest label that contain anything other than zero bytes cause rejection with assertion.notRedacted, and non-redacted assertions other than hard bindings are validated per section 14.10. Under this method the validator shall not record hash mismatch codes for activeManifest, and notes explain that only c2pa.ingredient.v3 has a claimSignature field, so redactions in manifests referenced by deprecated ingredient assertions cause validation to fail.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s265-14-11-3-3-2-manifest-hash-validation-method",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.11.3.3.2. Manifest Hash Validation Method",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s265-14-11-3-3-2-manifest-hash-validation-method.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 14.11.3.3.2. Manifest Hash Validation Method\n\nAn ingredient manifest that has not been changed due to redaction can be validated faster if the current validator trusts the previous claim generator’s validation results:\n\n1.  Resolve the URI reference in the `url` value of the `activeManifest` field to obtain the ingredient’s manifest box. If the `url` field is not present or the URI reference cannot be resolved, the ingredient claim is rejected with a failure code of `ingredient.manifest.missing`.\n    \n2.  Determine the hash algorithm identifier (or possible failure code) by following th",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the manifest hash validation method, a faster option for an ingredient manifest unchanged by redaction when the validator trusts the previous claim generator's results. The activeManifest url is resolved (else ingredient.manifest.missing), its hash computed per section 14.4 and section 9.4.2.3, and compared with the hash field; a missing or unequal hash causes rejection with ingredient.manifest.mismatch, while a match fully validates the ingredient and issues ingredient.manifest.validated.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s266-14-12-validate-the-asset-s-content",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
