      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.12.1.1. General\n\nOnce a standard manifest (and its bindings) has been located, the exclusion range(s) shall be extracted from the `c2pa.hash.data` assertion.\n\nIf the ending byte offset of one exclusion range (`start` + `length`) is greater than the starting byte offset of the next exclusion range in the array, or a `start` or `length` value is negative, then the manifest shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.dataHash.malformed`.\n\nIf any update manifests were encountered then the `length` value of the exclusion range whose `start` value is the offset of the start of the e",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies validation of a c2pa.hash.data assertion: overlapping or negative exclusion ranges cause rejection with assertion.dataHash.malformed, and when update manifests are present the C2PA Manifest Store exclusion length and later range starts are adjusted for the store's current length. The hash is computed over the asset bytes outside the exclusion ranges; an exclusion running past the end of the asset, a missing hash field, or non-permitted data within the manifest store exclusion causes rejection with assertion.dataHash.mismatch, and an unlisted alg causes algorithm.unsupported. Additional exclusions beyond the manifest store and padding produce the informational code assertion.dataHash.additionalExclusionsPresent, pad and pad2 fields are ignored, and success yields assertion.dataHash.match. If the hash does not match, a multi-asset hash assertion is validated if present, otherwise the manifest is rejected with assertion.dataHash.mismatch.",
