      "target": "../sections/s284-14-12-4-validating-a-multi-asset-hash.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 14.12.4. Validating a multi-asset hash\n\nIf the standard validation of the hard binding in the standard manifest fails, and the standard manifest contains a multi-asset hash assertion in `created_assertions`, then the validator shall proceed to validate the multi-asset hash assertion. If more than one multi-asset hash assertion is present, then the manifest shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.multiAssetHash.malformed`.\n\nValidation of the multi-asset hash assertion (`c2pa.hash.multi-asset`) shall be performed by iterating over the array of `parts` in the `multi-asset-hash-ma",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that if standard hard binding validation fails and a multi-asset hash assertion is in created_assertions, the validator shall validate it; more than one such assertion, a missing or empty parts array, or a part lacking a valid locator and hashAssertion causes rejection with assertion.multiAssetHash.malformed. Byte-offset locators need non-negative byteOffset and length, and bmffBox locators must reference a present box. A missing non-optional part causes assertion.multiAssetHash.missingPart while optional parts are skipped, and overlapping parts or parts not covering every byte cause assertion.multiAssetHash.malformed. Each part is hashed with its referenced method using offsets relative to the part start, with truncation or mismatch causing assertion.multiAssetHash.mismatch; if all parts validate, assertion.multiAssetHash.match is recorded and no hard binding failure codes are recorded.",
        "state": "draft",
