      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.12.5.1. General\n\nValidation of a collection data hash assertion (`c2pa.hash.collection.data`) that has been located in a standard manifest shall be performed by iterating over the array of `uris` in the `collection-data-hash-map`. If there is no `uris` field present, then the manifest shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.collectionHash.malformed`.\n\nFollow the procedure in [Section 14.4, “Determining the hashing algorithm”](#_determining_the_hashing_algorithm) to determine the hash algorithm and any possible failure codes. Once determined, hashing shall be processed as s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies validation of a c2pa.hash.collection.data assertion by iterating over its uris array, rejecting with assertion.collectionHash.malformed if uris is missing or any entry lacks uri or hash. Each uri shall be checked before use and rejected with assertion.collectionHash.invalidURI if it contains . or ..; each retrieved asset is hashed over all its bytes, with a mismatch causing assertion.collectionHash.mismatch and a match adding assertion.collectionHash.match. Any listed file not found causes rejection with assertion.collectionHash.incorrectFileCount.",
        "state": "draft",
