      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.12.5.3. Hashing of WARC files",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s288-14-12-5-3-hashing-of-warc-files.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.12.5.3. Hashing of WARC files\n\nFor WARC files, the collection data hash covers every record other than the C2PA manifest record, and each record’s hash is computed over its uncompressed bytes, as described in [Section A.10.3, “Hashing”](#warc_hashing).\n\nA WARC file has no central directory that fixes the complete set of records present, so the collection data hash on its own binds only the records it lists. A validator shall reject the manifest with a failure code of `assertion.collectionHash.mismatch` if any two records in the file, other than the C2PA manifest record, share the same",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that for WARC files the collection data hash covers every record except the C2PA manifest record, each hashed over its uncompressed bytes. Because WARC has no central directory, a validator shall reject with assertion.collectionHash.mismatch if any two non-manifest records share a WARC-Record-ID, and shall verify that records and uris entries correspond one-to-one by matching uri to WARC-Record-ID, rejecting with the same code otherwise, so that appended or duplicated records cannot leave the manifest valid. Compressed records shall be decompressed under an implementation-defined maximum size and rejected with assertion.collectionHash.mismatch if they exceed it or if the decompressed length differs from Content-Length, which a note explains bounds work from maliciously crafted records.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
