      "target": "../sections/s290-14-12-6-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.12.6.1. General\n\nValidation of a segment hash assertion (`c2pa.hash.segment`) that has been located in a standard manifest, as described in [Section 14.5.2.5, “Special Considerations for Append-Only Text Files”](#_locating_append_only_text), shall be performed over the file read in binary mode.\n\nIf the `version` field is absent, or contains a value that the validator does not recognise, then the manifest shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.segmentHash.malformed`. If the `hash`, `segmentStart` or `segmentEnd` field is absent, or `segmentEnd` is less than `segmentStart`,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies validation of a c2pa.hash.segment assertion over the file read in binary mode. The manifest is rejected with assertion.segmentHash.malformed if version is missing or unrecognised, if hash, segmentStart or segmentEnd is missing or segmentEnd is less than segmentStart, if predecessorSentinel lacks start, length or hash, or if sentinelLength presence does not match whether the sentinel line references the store externally (required) or inline (forbidden). The sentinel line must begin at segmentEnd, and the hash over bytes [segmentStart, segmentEnd) must match, otherwise assertion.segmentHash.mismatch; on success assertion.segmentHash.match is added.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
