    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s291-14-12-6-2-coverage-of-the-asset",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "14.12.6.2. Coverage of the asset",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s291-14-12-6-2-coverage-of-the-asset.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 14.12.6.2. Coverage of the asset\n\nThe checkpoints present in a file shall together cover every byte of it, so that content cannot be added, removed or replaced without a covering checkpoint.\n\nFor the active checkpoint only, the validator shall verify that the sentinel line carrying its manifest ends at the end of the file, so that no content has been appended without a covering checkpoint. The end boundary shall be determined as follows:\n\n*   If the `sentinelLength` field is present, the end boundary is `segmentEnd` plus `sentinelLength`.\n    \n*   If the `sentinelLength` field is absent,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that the checkpoints in a file together cover every byte. For the active checkpoint, the end boundary (segmentEnd plus sentinelLength, or plus the actual sentinel line length including its line ending) must equal the file length, the first checkpoint without predecessorSentinel must have segmentStart of 0, and every other checkpoint's segmentStart must equal predecessorSentinel.start plus predecessorSentinel.length; any failure causes rejection with assertion.segmentHash.partialCoverage. A note says these checks ensure every byte up to the active sentinel line falls in exactly one segment or sentinel line, with no gaps.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
