    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s294-15-1-introduction",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.1. Introduction",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s294-15-1-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 15.1. Introduction\n\nThe C2PA Live Media specification is designed to support the unique requirements of live media workflows, streaming workflows and dynamic packaging, where content is created and distributed in real-time, or packaged in a just-in-time manner. This specification outlines how to manage assertions related to tracks (video, audio, subtitles, etc) in live sessions, ensuring the integrity and authenticity of the content as it is produced and shared.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Live Media workflows can include both live streaming scenarios (e.g., live sports events, news broadcasts) and dyn",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the C2PA Live Media specification as supporting live, streaming and dynamic packaging workflows where content is created or packaged in real time, and outlining how to manage assertions for tracks in live sessions to ensure integrity and authenticity. Notes clarify that it covers live streaming and dynamic packaging and is not limited to video, provided the packaging is BMFF or delivery uses Enhanced RTMP (V2). States that this version applies to ISO BMFF content, ISO/IEC 23000-19 content, and Enhanced RTMP (V2) contributions via section 15.5 Verifiable Segment Info method, while being agnostic of manifest and delivery protocols, and does not support MPEG-2 Transport Streams.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
