    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s297-15-3-1-c2pa-manifest-transport",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.3.1. C2PA Manifest transport",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s297-15-3-1-c2pa-manifest-transport.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.3.1. C2PA Manifest transport\n\nThe live media architecture builds upon this specification’s support for BMFF-based asset embedding, adding mechanisms to support real-time content validation. The two key parts of that are (1) any hashing of content shall be done using a standard `bmff-hash-map` (where the target of the hash is a segment) or, for content contributed over [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html), as described in [Section 15.5.3, “Carriage over Enhanced RTMP (E-RTMP)”](#rtmp_verifiable_segment_info), and (2) anytime that a C2PA Manifest",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes live media manifest transport as building on BMFF embedding with two key requirements: content hashing shall use a standard bmff-hash-map targeting a segment (or the method of section 15.5.3 for Enhanced RTMP (V2)), and any C2PA Manifest Store in a live stream shall be in a uuid box per section A.5.1, or for Enhanced RTMP (V2) in a c2paManifest pair in a VideoPacketType.Metadata or AudioPacketType.Metadata message. The uuid box holding a manifest store may appear in any segment and is called the C2PA Manifest Box. Defines dynamically packaged content as prepared just-in-time on request, treats live media and dynamically packaged content as interchangeable terms, and notes that live streams are always dynamically packaged but not vice versa.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
