    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s298-15-3-2-segment-based-validation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.3.2. Segment-based validation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s298-15-3-2-segment-based-validation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.3.2. Segment-based validation\n\nLive media, or dynamically packaged, streams require the validation of each segment of the stream independently of other segments. As such, the hash of each segment’s content needs to be provided as part of that segment. Two different methods for signing that information are described, enabling a given claim generator to choose the most appropriate one for its needs. Either method can be used, and validators are not required to support both.\n\nThese methods are:\n\n*   \"[Section 15.4, “Per-segment C2PA Manifest Box method”](#using_c2pa_manifest_box)\" which u",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States that live or dynamically packaged streams require each segment to be validated independently, so each segment must carry its own content hash. Describes two signing methods, either of which can be used and validators need not support both: section 15.4 Per-segment C2PA Manifest Box method and section 15.5 Verifiable Segment Info method, the latter using a verifiable-segment-info in an emsg box or E-RTMP Metadata message together with session keys. Other C2PA-defined live media binding schemes may be used provided they compute segment hashes with a standard bmff-hash-map and embed or reference the manifest store via a uuid box per section A.5.1.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s299-15-3-3-c2pa-manifest-binding-in-an-initializatio",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.3.3. C2PA Manifest binding in an initialization segment",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s299-15-3-3-c2pa-manifest-binding-in-an-initializatio.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.3.3. C2PA Manifest binding in an initialization segment\n\nFor those use cases that require (or desire) the presence of an initialization segment, it shall contain a `uuid` box, whose `bmff-hash-map` includes the `moov` box to establish a cryptographic relationship between the initialization segment and the media segments. For the subset of live media streams that are in a broadcast 'push' streaming scenario (e.g., over-the-air broadcast television without a pull mechanism), the initialization segment may be repeated periodically, and the `uuid` box need not be included in each initializ",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that, where an initialization segment is used, it contain a uuid box whose bmff-hash-map includes the moov box, cryptographically linking it to the media segments. In broadcast push scenarios the initialization segment may be repeated periodically and the uuid box need not be in every copy. A note explains the binding ensures the manifest corresponds to the specific media, preventing replay attacks and content substitution.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
