    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s301-15-4-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.4.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s301-15-4-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.4.1. Description\n\nA live media stream may use per-segment C2PA Manifest Boxes to provide per-segment validation. When using this approach, each media segment shall contain a C2PA Manifest Box carried in a `uuid` box as defined in [Section A.5.1, “The `'uuid'` Box for C2PA”](#uuid_box). The active C2PA Manifest for each segment shall contain a BMFF hash assertion (`c2pa.hash.bmff.v3`) with a `hash` field that covers the bytes of that segment and with no `merkle` field, a [Section 15.4.2, “Live Media Segment Assertion”](#livevideo_segment), and may also contain any other assertions relev",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the per-segment C2PA Manifest Box method, which a live media stream may use: each media segment shall contain a C2PA Manifest Box in a uuid box per section A.5.1, whose active manifest shall contain a c2pa.hash.bmff.v3 assertion with a hash covering the segment and no merkle field, plus a live media segment assertion, and may contain other relevant assertions. Claim generators may embed additional per-segment validation values derived from segment hashes, such as anchor-point chaining values. A note says this method does not need session keys, verifiable-segment-info-map or emsg boxes and can be used independently of the Verifiable Segment Info method.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
