    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s302-15-4-2-live-media-segment-assertion",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.4.2. Live Media Segment Assertion",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s302-15-4-2-live-media-segment-assertion.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.4.2. Live Media Segment Assertion\n\nWhen using the per-segment C2PA Manifest Box method, a live media segment assertion shall be included in the C2PA Manifest of each segment. This assertion, which provides metadata about the segment and its relationship to the live media stream, shall have a label of `c2pa.livevideo.segment`.\n\nThe live media segment assertion shall contain a `sequenceNumber` field that provides a unique identifier for the segment. It shall also contain a `streamId` field that provides a unique identifier for the entire live media stream.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The value of `st",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a live media segment assertion labelled c2pa.livevideo.segment in each segment's manifest when using the per-segment C2PA Manifest Box method, containing a sequenceNumber identifying the segment and a streamId identifying the whole stream (any unique string, such as a UUID or URL). It shall also contain a continuityMethod field indicating how cryptographic continuity between segments is ensured; the only defined value is c2pa.manifestId, which requires a previousManifestId field holding the previous segment's manifest identifier. Implementers may define other continuity methods and fields, named using labels as described in section 8.2 Labels.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
