    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s303-15-4-2-1-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.4.2.1. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s303-15-4-2-1-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 15.4.2.1. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `livevideo-segment-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.8.1, “Live Media Segment”](#cddl_annex_livevideo_segment) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; assertion used to carry live media segment information\n; this assertion shares `sequenceNumber` semantics with\n; `verifiable-segment-info-map`\n\nlivevideo-segment-map = {\n    ; monotonically increasing sequence number for each segment\n    \"sequenceNumber\" => uint,\n    \"streamId\" => tstr, ; A uniq",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL schema for the live media segment assertion via the livevideo-segment-map rule, with sequenceNumber, streamId, continuityMethod and optional additional fields, and the livevideo-segment-map-manifestId rule adding previousManifestId when continuityMethod is c2pa.manifestId; the complete normative schema is in section G.8.1 Live Media Segment. Also provides a CBOR diagnostic notation example of such an assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
