    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s305-15-5-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s305-15-5-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.5.1. Description\n\nThe Verifiable Segment Info Map (`verifiable-segment-info`) is a structure designed to provide concise per-segment information for a live media stream allowing for each segment to be validated independently. It enables the validation of each segment’s integrity and authenticity during playback, ensuring that the content has not been tampered with. It is used in workflows which are using [Section 15.5.5, “Session Keys”](#session_keys) to sign the segment information.\n\nA `verifiable-segment-info` is a `COSE_Sign1_Tagged` structure where the payload field is the CBOR ser",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the verifiable-segment-info as a COSE_Sign1_Tagged structure giving concise per-segment information so each live media segment can be validated independently, used in workflows that sign segment information with session keys. Its payload is a CBOR-serialized segment-info-map that shall be present and not detached, signed by a private session key, with alg (and optionally iat) in the protected header and the session key kid in the unprotected header. The segment-info-map shall contain sequenceNumber (matching mfhd.sequence_number or the ISO/IEC 23009-9 indexing rules, and matching the live media segment assertion when both methods are used), manifestId identifying the current or still-active manifest, and bmffHash, a bmff-hash-map of the segment with no merkle field and an exclusion for /emsg boxes with value urn:c2pa:verifiable-segment-info. It may also contain an optional manifestUri hashed-ext-uri from which a manifest can be retrieved.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s306-15-5-2-use-in-an-emsg-box",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.2. Use in an `emsg` box",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s306-15-5-2-use-in-an-emsg-box.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.5.2. Use in an `emsg` box\n\nWhen using the `verifiable-segment-info` in a live media workflow, a `verifiable-segment-info` shall be present in the `emsg` box of each segment of a live media stream to verify the integrity of the content during playback.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This requirement applies only to workflows that chose the `verifiable-segment-info` method and does not apply to workflows that rely solely on C2PA Manifest Boxes embedded in each segment.\n\nThe C2PA `emsg` box fields shall have:\n\n*   `version` set to `0`\n    \n*   `scheme_id_uri` set to `urn:c2pa:verifiable-segment-info`",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that, in workflows using the verifiable-segment-info method, a verifiable-segment-info be present in the emsg box of each segment, noting this does not apply to workflows relying only on per-segment C2PA Manifest Boxes. Specifies the emsg field values: version 0, scheme_id_uri urn:c2pa:verifiable-segment-info, value fseg, presentation_time_delta 0, timescale and event_duration covering the segment, a session-unique id, and message_data holding the encoded verifiable-segment-info. Gives the CDDL schema for verifiable-segment-info and segment-info-map, with the complete normative schema in section G.8.2 Verifiable Segment Info.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s307-15-5-3-carriage-over-enhanced-rtmp-e-rtmp",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.3. Carriage over Enhanced RTMP (E-RTMP)",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s307-15-5-3-carriage-over-enhanced-rtmp-e-rtmp.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.5.3. Carriage over Enhanced RTMP (E-RTMP)\n\n[Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html) is a message-based, continuously multiplexed streaming protocol commonly used for live contribution (\"first mile\") streaming, and does not package content using ISO BMFF. For content contributed over [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html), `rtmp-verifiable-segment-info` is carried in an E-RTMP `VideoPacketType.Metadata` message (for the video track) or `AudioPacketType.Metadata` message (for an audio track) instead of an `emsg`",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes carriage over Enhanced RTMP (V2), a message-based streaming protocol used for live contribution that does not use ISO BMFF packaging. For such content, rtmp-verifiable-segment-info is carried in a VideoPacketType.Metadata or AudioPacketType.Metadata message instead of an emsg box, with an rtmp-segment-info-map payload whose sequenceNumber and manifestId have the same meaning as before and whose segmentHash, an rtmp-hash-map, replaces bmffHash. A note says AudioPacketType.Metadata is not yet defined by Enhanced RTMP (V2) and its use assumes it will be added.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s308-15-5-3-1-logical-segment",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.3.1. Logical segment",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s308-15-5-3-1-logical-segment.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 15.5.3.1. Logical segment\n\nContent contributed over [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html) may include multiple tracks of the same media type (for example, multiple audio tracks), identified by `trackId` when [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html) multitrack support is used. For the purposes of this clause, a track is identified by its media type together with its `trackId`; audio and video `trackId` values are independent of each other, and an audio or video message that does not use [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a logical segment for Enhanced RTMP (V2) content: tracks are identified by media type and trackId (non-multitrack messages belong to track 0, and an absent trackId equals 0), and a segment is scoped to one track, with the carrying Metadata message required to belong to that track. A video or audio segment shall begin at the tag header of the first frame after the previous segment and consist of complete frames followed by one or more Metadata messages carrying rtmp-verifiable-segment-info. Publishers shall send Metadata messages on the same chunk stream as the track's coded frames, with a timestamp equal to the segment's last frame, which a note says guarantees unambiguous ordering. Consecutive Metadata messages belong to the segment they close, boundaries shall not split frames, sequenceNumber shall increase by 1 per segment per track, and each session key shall sign for only one track.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s309-15-5-3-2-segment-hash-computation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.3.2. Segment hash computation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s309-15-5-3-2-segment-hash-computation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 15.5.3.2. Segment hash computation\n\nThe `segmentHash` field of an `rtmp-segment-info-map` shall be computed, using the algorithm identified in its `alg` field, over the concatenation, in transmission order, of the following fields of each coded-frame packet of the segment:\n\n1.  the RTMP message timestamp of the message carrying the packet, as a 32-bit unsigned big-endian integer;\n    \n2.  the composition time offset of the packet, as a 24-bit signed big-endian integer, or 0 if the packet carries none (for example, a `CodedFramesX` packet or an audio packet);\n    \n3.  the coded media data",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that segmentHash in an rtmp-segment-info-map shall be computed with the alg algorithm over the concatenation, in transmission order, of each coded-frame packet's RTMP message timestamp (32-bit unsigned big-endian), composition time offset (24-bit signed big-endian, or 0 if absent) and coded media data. Only the segment's track packet from a Multitrack message is included, Aggregate Message contents are treated as individually transmitted with normalized timestamps, and no other bytes are included. Notes clarify that control messages, data messages, codec configuration packets and all Metadata messages do not contribute, that rewriting timestamps or composition offsets invalidates the hash, and that the TimestampOffsetNano ModEx data is not covered and so cannot be relied upon by a validator.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s310-15-5-3-3-initialization-data-binding",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.3.3. Initialization data binding",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s310-15-5-3-3-initialization-data-binding.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 15.5.3.3. Initialization data binding\n\nA C2PA Manifest delivered in a `c2paManifest` \\[name, value\\] pair shall contain, as its hard binding, a [data hash assertion](#_data_hash) without an `exclusions` field, whose hash is computed over the E-RTMP initialization data. The E-RTMP initialization data is the concatenation of the codec configuration payloads (for example, `[AVCDecoderConfigurationRecord]`, `[HEVCDecoderConfigurationRecord]` or `[AacSequenceHeader]`, as defined by [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html)) carried in the most recent `Seque",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a manifest delivered in a c2paManifest pair to use as its hard binding a data hash assertion without exclusions, computed over the E-RTMP initialization data, defined as the concatenated codec configuration payloads from each track's most recent SequenceStart packet (or legacy sequence header), video tracks before audio and by ascending trackId. Publishers shall send each track's codec configuration on that track's chunk stream and before the binding c2paManifest, sending a new c2paManifest before dependent frames if configuration changes. A validator shall validate this hard binding when it validates the first segment whose manifestId identifies that manifest, against the configuration most recently received before that segment's closing c2paSegmentInfo. Notes explain this mirrors binding to the moov box, that onMetaData is excluded because intermediaries rewrite it, and that multiple message streams on one connection share one manifest and so must not reuse a media type and trackId combination.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s311-15-5-3-4-amf-carriage",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.3.4. AMF carriage",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s311-15-5-3-4-amf-carriage.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 15.5.3.4. AMF carriage\n\nWithin a `VideoPacketType.Metadata` or `AudioPacketType.Metadata` message, AMF3 object encoding shall be used, and the value of each of the following \\[name, value\\] pairs, when present, shall be carried as a native AMF3 `ByteArray`:\n\n`c2paSegmentInfo`\n\nThe binary-encoded `rtmp-verifiable-segment-info`, whose payload is an `rtmp-segment-info-map`, present in the `Metadata` message(s) that close each segment of the track carrying it. More than one `c2paSegmentInfo` may be present consecutively for the same segment (for example, signed with different session keys du",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires AMF3 object encoding in VideoPacketType.Metadata and AudioPacketType.Metadata messages, with the c2paSegmentInfo and c2paManifest values carried as native AMF3 ByteArray. c2paSegmentInfo holds the binary rtmp-verifiable-segment-info in the Metadata messages closing each segment; several may appear for one segment, for example during key rotation, and the segment is valid if at least one validates. c2paManifest holds a binary C2PA Manifest Store that shall include a c2pa.session-keys assertion, sent for the first manifest and whenever the active manifest changes, and should be on the video track unless an audio track needs its own manifest. Gives the CDDL schema for rtmp-segment-info-map (normative schema in section G.8.3 Enhanced RTMP Segment Info) and a CBOR diagnostic example.",
