      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.3.5. Capability negotiation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s312-15-5-3-5-capability-negotiation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 15.5.3.5. Capability negotiation\n\nBecause E-RTMP is also used by endpoints that do not support this specification, support for C2PA Manifests shall be negotiated during the connection handshake using the `C2PA` bit (`0x10`) of `CapsExMask`, as defined by [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html). A client that supports C2PA Manifests shall set this bit in the `capsEx` property of the Command Object of its `connect` command, and shall set the `objectEncoding` property of that same Command Object to 3. A server that supports C2PA Manifests shall set this",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires C2PA Manifest support over E-RTMP to be negotiated in the connection handshake using the C2PA bit (0x10) of CapsExMask: a supporting client shall set it in the capsEx property of its connect Command Object and set objectEncoding to 3, and a supporting server shall set it in the Info Object of its _result. An endpoint shall not send c2paSegmentInfo or c2paManifest unless both sides signaled support, and a non-signaling endpoint should not expect them. Receivers shall ignore unrecognized pairs in Metadata messages and continue processing the rest; a note says negotiation avoids depending on legacy endpoint behaviour.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
