    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s313-15-5-3-6-reconnection",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.3.6. Reconnection",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s313-15-5-3-6-reconnection.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 15.5.3.6. Reconnection\n\nThe C2PA state of a stream (the active C2PA Manifest, its session keys and the `sequenceNumber` of each track) is not affected by an [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html) reconnection (for example, in response to a `NetConnection.Connect.ReconnectRequest`): segments sent on the new connection shall continue the `sequenceNumber` of each track. After reconnecting, a publisher shall send the active C2PA Manifest again in a `c2paManifest` \\[name, value\\] pair, after the codec configuration of each track and before the first code",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States that an Enhanced RTMP (V2) reconnection does not affect a stream's C2PA state (active manifest, session keys and per-track sequenceNumber), so segments on the new connection shall continue each track's sequenceNumber. After reconnecting, a publisher shall resend the active manifest in a c2paManifest pair after each track's codec configuration and before the first coded frame. Notes explain that this supports moving to a different server instance, and that segments cannot span a reconnection, so a publisher can send each track's current c2paSegmentInfo before disconnecting to avoid unvalidatable frames.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
