      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.5.4. C2PA Manifest Updates\n\nWhen different assertions are required for a new segment (for example, to indicate different provenance or replace expiring session keys), a new C2PA Manifest Store shall be provided, either embedded in the segment via a C2PA Manifest Box or linked externally, or for E-RTMP-delivered segments, via a `c2paManifest` \\[name, value\\] pair in a `VideoPacketType.Metadata` or `AudioPacketType.Metadata` message. The new manifest shall be used for all subsequent segments until another manifest is provided.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This allows for dynamic updates to the C2PA Ma",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that when a new segment needs different assertions, such as changed provenance or replacement of expiring session keys, a new C2PA Manifest Store be provided, embedded in a C2PA Manifest Box, linked externally, or for E-RTMP via a c2paManifest pair in a Metadata message. The new manifest shall apply to all subsequent segments until another is provided, which a note says allows dynamic updates while maintaining integrity and authenticity.",
