      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.5.5.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s316-15-5-5-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 15.5.5.1. Description\n\nSession keys are asymmetric key pairs. Any of the cryptographic algorithms allowed for [claim generator X.509 certificates](#certificate-requirements) may be used.\n\nWhen using session-specific keys, they shall be generated at the start of a live media session, but may also be generated and delivered via updated manifests in later segments (either initialization or other segments). Each session key is used for a limited period, which enables key rotation. Session-specific keys should be updated when the provenance changes.\n\nThe public halves of the session keys are",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes session keys as asymmetric key pairs that may use any algorithm allowed for claim generator X.509 certificates; they shall be generated at the start of a live media session, may also be delivered in later manifests, are each used for a limited period to enable rotation, and should be updated when provenance changes. Public keys are delivered in a C2PA Manifest, with the initial set in the initialization segment's manifest or, for E-RTMP, in a c2paManifest sent before the referencing c2paSegmentInfo. For an unknown session key, a receiver should check the segment's C2PA Manifest Box, then the manifestUri, and shall fall back to the initialization segment's manifest; for E-RTMP it shall use the c2paManifest matching manifestId and should try manifestUri if needed. The receiver shall ensure the retrieved manifest's identifier matches manifestId, and an externally hosted manifest needs to remain at its URI for as long as the content is provided.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
