    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s321-15-7-2-verifiable-segment-info-method",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.7.2. Verifiable Segment Info method",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s321-15-7-2-verifiable-segment-info-method.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.7.2. Verifiable Segment Info method\n\nWhen using the Verifiable Segment Info method, there are two main steps involved in generating the live media stream.\n\nSession Key Generation\n\nAt the start of a live media session, one or more session keys are generated, each with its own `createdAt`, `validityPeriod`, and `minSequenceNumber`. These session keys are included in the C2PA Manifest in the C2PA Manifest Box that shall be present in the initialization segment(s), or in an E-RTMP `VideoPacketType.Metadata` or `AudioPacketType.Metadata` message. The `minSequenceNumber` for each key indicat",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the two steps of generating a live media stream with the Verifiable Segment Info method. In session key generation, one or more session keys, each with its own createdAt, validityPeriod and minSequenceNumber, are included in the C2PA Manifest in the C2PA Manifest Box that shall be present in the initialization segment(s), or in an E-RTMP VideoPacketType.Metadata or AudioPacketType.Metadata message; minSequenceNumber indicates the earliest segment that should be signed with that key, supporting overlap for key rotation. In signing the box hash, each BMFF/CMAF segment shall have an emsg box containing the verifiable-segment-info, a segment-info-map signed by a session key that carries a sequenceNumber against out-of-order attacks and a bmff-hash-map hashing the segment, and an updated manifest may be included in the segment or referenced via manifestUri. Notes explain that over Enhanced RTMP (V2) each track uses its own session key and an rtmp-verifiable-segment-info with an rtmp-segment-info-map is carried in Metadata messages, and that longer streams rotate session keys through subsequent initialization segments.",
        "state": "draft",
