    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s325-15-8-3-verifiable-segment-info-validation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "15.8.3. Verifiable Segment Info Validation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s325-15-8-3-verifiable-segment-info-validation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.8.3. Verifiable Segment Info Validation\n\nIf the C2PA Manifest present in the C2PA Manifest Box contains a session keys assertion, the public session keys shall be extracted and stored for use in validating subsequent segments. If any public session key does not conform to the requirements described in [Session Keys Assertion](#session_keys_assertion), the validation of that segment shall fail with a failure code of `livevideo.sessionkey.invalid`. Similarly, if signature validation (`signerBinding`) of any public session key structure fails, that session key is invalid and shall not be",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies how a validator processes the Verifiable Segment Info method: public session keys from a session keys assertion are extracted and stored, and a key that does not conform or whose signerBinding signature fails is invalid and causes livevideo.sessionkey.invalid. A non-initialization segment with a conforming emsg box but no valid session keys fails with livevideo.segment.invalid; otherwise the validator uses the kid from the unprotected header to find the key, retrieving the manifest via manifestUri if needed, and fails with livevideo.segment.invalid if the key is missing or the signature does not verify. The segment-info-map check also fails with livevideo.segment.invalid if the sequenceNumber does not increase, is below the key's minSequenceNumber, the BMFF/CMAF presentation time is outside the key's validity period, or the hash does not match bmffHash. The validator should also check that the certificate that signed the manifest providing the current session key is still valid, failing with livevideo.sessionkey.invalid if it is not.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s326-15-8-4-verifiable-segment-info-validation-over-e",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
