      "target": "../sections/s326-15-8-4-verifiable-segment-info-validation-over-e.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 15.8.4. Verifiable Segment Info Validation over Enhanced RTMP\n\nFor content contributed over [Enhanced RTMP (V2)](https://veovera.org/docs/enhanced/enhanced-rtmp-v2.html), the validation steps described in [Verifiable Segment Info Validation](#_verifiable_segment_info_validation) apply, with the `VideoPacketType.Metadata` or `AudioPacketType.Metadata` message carrying `c2paSegmentInfo` used in place of the `emsg` box, and the ``rtmp-segment-info-map’s `segmentHash`` field (see [Section 15.5.3, “Carriage over Enhanced RTMP (E-RTMP)”](#rtmp_verifiable_segment_info)) used in place of `bmffHas",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that for content contributed over Enhanced RTMP (V2) the Verifiable Segment Info validation steps apply, with the Metadata message carrying c2paSegmentInfo used in place of the emsg box and the rtmp-segment-info-map segmentHash field used in place of bmffHash, and session keys delivered in c2pa.session-keys in a c2paManifest metadata message. Lists the errors that cause livevideo.segment.invalid when parsing the rtmp-segment-info-map: a non-increasing sequenceNumber within a track, a sequenceNumber below the key's minSequenceNumber, validation time outside the key's createdAt plus validityPeriod window, a hash mismatch with segmentHash, a key identified by kid already used for a different track, or a Metadata message that does not belong to the track identified by its mediaType and trackId.",
