      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.1. Introduction",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s328-16-1-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 16.1. Introduction\n\nThis section of the document lists the standard set of assertions for use by C2PA implementations, describing their syntax, usage, etc. To keep things simple, all example JUMBF URIs have been shortened for illustrative purposes - full URIs are necessary in the actual data.\n\nAll assertions shall have a label as described in [Section 8.2, “Labels”](#assertion_labels) and shall be versioned as described in [Chapter 5, _Versioning_](#_versioning).\n\nAll C2PA standardized assertions use the JSON JUMBF content type, the CBOR JUMBF content type, or the Embedded File content typ",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the standard set of assertions for C2PA implementations, noting that example JUMBF URIs are shortened for illustration. Requires all assertions to have a label per Section 8.2, Labels, and to be versioned per Chapter 5, Versioning; standardized assertions use the JSON, CBOR or Embedded File JUMBF content types from ISO 19566-5:2023, entity-specific assertions may use others, and the Codestream content type shall not be used. Unless otherwise stated, standard assertions shall be serialized as CBOR complying with the Core Deterministic Encoding Requirements of RFC 8949 with CDDL schemas, while JSON assertions use JSON Schema. Explains that the assertions are grouped into functional clusters, and that Metadata About Assertions and Regions of Interest are supporting structures used by assertions rather than assertions themselves.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
