      "target": "../sections/s329-16-2-standard-c2pa-assertion-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 16.2. Standard C2PA Assertion Summary\n\nThe standard C2PA assertions are listed in [Table 3, “Standard C2PA assertions”](#standard-assertions), grouped by their function.\n\n**Table 3. Standard C2PA assertions**\n\n| Function | Type | Assertion | Schema | Serialization |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Content binding & integrity | [BMFF-based Hash](#_bmff_based_hash) | c2pa.hash.bmff (removed), c2pa.hash.bmff.v2 (deprecated), c2pa.hash.bmff.v3 | C2PA | CBOR |\n| [Collection Data Hash](#_collection_data_hash) | c2pa.hash.collection.data | C2PA | CBOR |\n| [Data Hash](#_data_hash) | c2pa.hash.da",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists the standard C2PA assertions in Table 3, grouped by function (content binding and integrity, provenance and workflow, ingredient, content description and referencing, trust and validation adjuncts, policy and disclosure), giving each type's assertion labels, schema and serialization. Examples include c2pa.hash.data, c2pa.hash.bmff.v3 (with c2pa.hash.bmff removed and c2pa.hash.bmff.v2 deprecated), c2pa.actions.v2, c2pa.ingredient.v3, c2pa.metadata (JSON-LD), c2pa.session-keys and c2pa.ai-disclosure.",
        "state": "draft",
