    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s332-16-3-1-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.1.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s332-16-3-1-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.1.1. Description\n\nThe most common way to uniquely verify the integrity of portions of a non-BMFF-based asset is via the [hard bindings](#_hard_bindings) (i.e., cryptographic hash) present in data hash assertions. However, for those formats that are \"box like\" but not compatible with BMFF, the [general box hash](#_general_box_hash) assertion is recommended.\n\nThe `alg` field, if present, shall be a string that is one of the allowed hash algorithms as defined in [Section 12.1, “Hashing”](#_hashing), and that algorithm shall be used to compute the hash. If the `alg` field is not present",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the data hash assertion as the most common hard binding for non-BMFF-based assets, recommending the general box hash assertion for box-like formats not compatible with BMFF. The optional alg field shall name an allowed algorithm (otherwise the Claim's alg applies), the hash goes in the hash field, and excluded ranges shall be listed in exclusions in increasing start order without overlap. Exclusion ranges shall begin and end within one logical unit without overlapping its header or length fields (except freebox or pad data), and the claim generator shall ensure they contain only C2PA Manifest Store content or asset metadata and cannot materially affect interpretation of the asset. The deprecated url field shall not be added and shall be ignored by consumers, and the assertion shall be labelled c2pa.hash.data and shall not appear in a cloud data or external reference assertion nor be used with a compressed manifest.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s333-16-3-1-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.1.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s333-16-3-1-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.1.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `data-hash-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.4.1, “Data Hash”](#cddl_annex_data_hash) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; Also check optionality within the hash-map\n; The data structure used to store the cryptographic hash of some or all of the\n; asset's data\n; and additional information required to compute the hash.\ndata-hash-map = {\n  ; Ranges have monotonically increasing `start` values, and no two ranges may\n  ; overlap.\n  ? \"exclusion",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the CDDL schema for the data hash assertion (the data-hash-map rule, with optional exclusions, alg, pad2, name and deprecated url, and required hash and pad), with the full normative schema in Section G.4.1, and gives a CBOR diagnostic example. Requires exclusion start and length values to use preferred (shortest) serialization normally, but to be written as 32-bit integers when they are not yet known. Requires pad to be present as a zero-filled byte string and pad2, if present, to be zero-filled, with Section 11.7, Multiple Step Processing, describing how to fill in values and adjust padding.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
