    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s337-16-3-1-6-special-considerations-for-riff-based",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.1.6. Special considerations for RIFF-based",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s337-16-3-1-6-special-considerations-for-riff-based.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.1.6. Special considerations for RIFF-based\n\nWhen hashing a RIFF-based asset into which the C2PA Manifest will be embedded, the size field of the top-level `RIFF` chunk (the four bytes at offset 4) should be included in the exclusion ranges. This is to support Update Manifests, which could change the size of the embedded C2PA Manifest Store; because this size field covers the entire file, any change to the size of the C2PA Manifest Store rewrites it.\n\n<a id=\"_bmff_based_hash\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that, when hashing a RIFF-based asset into which the C2PA Manifest will be embedded, the size field of the top-level RIFF chunk (the four bytes at offset 4) be included in the exclusion ranges. Explains that this supports Update Manifests, since this size field covers the whole file and is rewritten whenever the C2PA Manifest Store size changes.",
