    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s339-16-3-2-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.2.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s339-16-3-2-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.2.1. Description\n\nPortion(s) of a BMFF-based asset that a claim generator wishes to uniquely identify with a [hard binding](#_hard_bindings) (i.e., cryptographic hash) shall be described using BMFF-based hash assertions.\n\nA BMFF-based hash assertion shall have a label of `c2pa.hash.bmff.v3`.\n\nAll Merkle trees used in BMFF-based hash assertions shall be balanced binary trees with the minimum depth necessary to accomodate leaf nodes, where NULL padding is applied only to the rightmost positions as needed to maintain the complete binary tree structure. This also requires that each leve",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that portions of a BMFF-based asset to be identified with a hard binding be described using BMFF-based hash assertions labelled c2pa.hash.bmff.v3. All Merkle trees used shall be balanced binary trees of minimum depth, with NULL padding only at the rightmost positions and each level more than half full. Notes that earlier versions documented c2pa.hash.bmff and c2pa.hash.bmff.v2, and requires validators to ignore any c2pa.hash.bmff assertions. The assertion shall not appear in a cloud data or external reference assertion, and the deprecated url field shall not be added by claim generators and shall be ignored by consumers.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
