    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s340-16-3-2-2-hash-computation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.2.2. Hash Computation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s340-16-3-2-2-hash-computation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.2.2. Hash Computation\n\nThe `alg` field, if present, shall be a string that is one of the allowed hash algorithms as defined in [Section 12.1, “Hashing”](#_hashing), and that algorithm shall be used to compute the hash. If the `alg` field is not present, then the hashing algorithm shall be determined by the value of the `alg` field in the Claim.\n\nFor a non-fragmented MP4 asset, the `hash` field, the `merkle` field, or both fields shall be present. For a fragmented MP4 asset validated using a Merkle tree, the `merkle` field shall be present and the `hash` field shall be absent. For li",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies how the BMFF hash is computed: alg selects an allowed algorithm or defaults to the Claim's alg; non-fragmented MP4 needs hash, merkle or both, fragmented MP4 validated by Merkle tree needs only merkle, and live media segments need only hash. All file bytes are hashed except boxes or subsets matching exclusions entries, with box headers following the box's inclusion or exclusion, subset offsets measured from the box start and ordered without overlap, and in v2 and v3 each non-excluded root box contributing its 8-byte big-endian absolute offset concatenated with its data (the offset omitted for Merkle hashes when both hash and merkle are present). Defines exclusion matching by xpath, length, version, flags (with exact) and data, restricts xpath to a strict abbreviated full-path subset of BMFF 4cc nodes, and requires non-leaf nodes to be plain container boxes, with the box holding an embedded manifest always excluded. Requires 'free' boxes to replace or reserve space for excluded boxes, requires post-embed offsets to be hashed, and describes three ways to achieve this: pre-inserted 'free' boxes, a two-pass approach, or placing Update Manifests at the end of the file using box_purpose values original and update.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s341-16-3-2-3-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.2.3. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s341-16-3-2-3-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.2.3. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for the `c2pa.hash.bmff.v2` (deprecated) and `c2pa.hash.bmff.v3` assertions are defined by the `bmff-hash-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.4.2, “BMFF Hash”](#cddl_annex_bmff_hash) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\nbmff-hash-map = {\n  \"exclusions\": [1* exclusions-map],\n\n  ; A string identifying the cryptographic hash algorithm used to compute this\n  ; hash, taken from the C2PA hash algorithm identifier list. If this field is\n  ; absent, the hash algorithm is taken from a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the CDDL schema shared by the c2pa.hash.bmff.v2 (deprecated) and c2pa.hash.bmff.v3 assertions through the bmff-hash-map rule, with the complete normative schema in Section G.4.2, BMFF Hash. The map carries required exclusions plus optional alg, hash, merkle, name, deprecated url and sequenceNumber, with exclusions-map entries defined by xpath and optional length, data, subset, version, flags and exact, and merkle-map entries carrying uniqueId, localId, count, optional alg and initHash, hashes, and optional fixedBlockSize or variableBlockSizes for piecewise mdat validation. Gives CBOR diagnostic examples for a monolithic MP4, for fragmented MP4 files and for non-fragmented MP4 with a Merkle tree, plus pseudo-code for computing the BMFF-based hash and a suggested example of hashing for the Merkle map.",
