      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.3.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s349-16-3-3-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.3.1. Description\n\nA claim generator should use a general box hash assertion to verify the integrity, with a [hard binding](#_hard_bindings) (i.e., cryptographic hash), of assets whose formats use a non-BMFF-based box format such as JPEG 1, PNG, or GIF.\n\nA general box hash assertion shall have a label of `c2pa.hash.boxes`. Such an assertion consists of an array of structures, each one listing one or more boxes (by their name/identifier) and a hash that covers that data of those boxes (and any possible data that may be present in the file between them), along with the algorithm used f",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that claim generators use a general box hash assertion, labelled c2pa.hash.boxes, as a hard binding for non-BMFF box formats such as JPEG 1, PNG or GIF; it is an array of structures each listing one or more boxes and a hash over them (including any data between them). Boxes shall appear in asset order, including the C2PA Manifest box, and unlisted or out-of-order boxes cause rejection during validation. Describes the excluded flag (letting validators ignore a whole box, with an accurate hash or the single byte 00 recommended) and the exclusions byte ranges (with boxIndex, ordered, non-overlapping, confined to one box and to manifest or metadata content), where excluded set to true takes precedence over exclusions. Requires each instance of repeated box types to be listed separately, defines alg fallback from box-hash-map to box-map to Claim, and requires the C2PA Manifest Store box to be listed alone with name C2PA and hash 00 as a single box even when split across JPEG APP11 segments. The optional pad and pad2 shall be zero-filled, and the assertion shall not appear in a Cloud Data or External Reference assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
