      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.3.2. Special handling of multi-part assets\n\nTo support file formats that consist of multiple parts (as described in [Section 16.3.5, “Multi-Asset Hash”](#_multi_asset_hash)), one additional logical box is defined for cases where the data of one or more parts comes after the box-based data of the primary part. This box shall be labelled `c2pa.after` (for arbitrary data beyond the end of the box structure). The `c2pa.after` box, if present, shall be the last box listed, and its hash shall be computed from the byte following the last box until the end of the physical file.\n\nThe hard bi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a logical box labelled c2pa.after for multi-part formats where part data follows the primary part's box-based data; if present it shall be listed last and its hash shall cover from the byte after the last box to the end of the physical file. Requires that only the whole-asset hard binding assertion may include a c2pa.after box, while a hash assertion for an individual part shall cover only that part.",
        "state": "draft",
