      "target": "../sections/s352-16-3-3-3-1-jpeg-1-specific-handling.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.3.3.3.1. JPEG 1-specific Handling\n\nWhen working with JPEG 1, the `APP11` box is used for standards other than C2PA (i.e., JPEG 360). In those situations, all non-C2PA `APP11` boxes shall be included in the list of hashed boxes. The `APP11` boxes containing the C2PA Manifest Store shall be identified by `C2PA`. All other boxes shall be identified by the symbol found in [ISO 10918-1:1994, Table B.1](https://www.iso.org/standard/18902.html).\n\nThe C2PA Manifest Store can be identified by it being a JUMBF superbox with a label of `c2pa` and a JUMBF type UUID of `63327061-0011-0010-8000-00",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies JPEG 1 handling for general box hash: non-C2PA APP11 boxes shall be included in the hashed boxes, APP11 boxes holding the C2PA Manifest Store shall be identified as C2PA, and all other boxes shall use the symbols from ISO 10918-1:1994, Table B.1. Notes that the manifest store is recognizable as a JUMBF superbox labelled c2pa with the given type UUID, and that SOS and RST[n] boxes include their following entropy-coded segments. Explains that CIPA Multi-Picture Format files can be supported by listing all boxes of each Individual Image in sequence, but that if the file is treated as a multi-part asset the c2pa.after box shall be used for parts after the first image's EOI.",
        "state": "draft",
