      "target": "../sections/s355-16-3-3-3-4-gif-specific-handling.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.3.3.3.4. GIF-specific Handling\n\nThe hash of a box containing a 'Packed Fields' attribute will also hash the optional data indicated by that attribute. For example, the Image Descriptor will include the Local Color Table block, and the Logical Screen Descriptor will include the Global Color Table block, if they exist.\n\nFor all boxes containing a block label, the naming convention shall be as follows: \"<Block Label>\".\n\nFor all extension blocks, the naming convention is as follows: \"<Extension Introducer><Extension Label>\".\n\nThe only other blocks that are not described by the above nami",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies GIF handling for general box hash: hashing a box with a Packed Fields attribute also hashes the optional data it indicates, such as Local or Global Color Tables. Requires boxes with a block label to be named \"<Block Label>\" and extension blocks to be named \"<Extension Introducer><Extension Label>\", with the header named \"GIF89a\", Table Based Image Data \"TBID\" and the Logical Screen Descriptor \"LSD\", and gives examples such as \"3B\" for the trailer and \"21FE\" for a Comment Extension.",
