      "target": "../sections/s356-16-3-3-3-5-riff-specific-handling.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.3.3.3.5. RIFF-specific Handling\n\nRIFF file chunks may be nested in a tree structure of arbitrary depth. The root of this structure consists of one or more **L0** chunks, each with the chunk identifier of `RIFF`. These `RIFF` chunks are defined with the following structure:\n\n*   Bytes 0-3: Chunk identifier, always `RIFF`.\n    \n*   Bytes 4-7: Chunk length (minus 8 bytes for the chunk identifier and chunk length fields).\n    \n*   Bytes 8-11: Media type identifier.\n    \n*   Bytes 12-n: Chunk data (all **L1** chunks).\n    \n\nAfter the media type identifier, the `RIFF` chunk may contain one",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the nested RIFF chunk structure of L0 RIFF chunks, L1 sub-chunks and LIST chunks that nest further chunks, and specifies how they map to general box hash boxes. Each L0 chunk shall be a 12-byte box named by its media type identifier, each non-LIST L1 chunk a box named by its chunk identifier, and each LIST L1 chunk a box named by its list type identifier, with L1 boxes spanning from byte 0 through any padding byte. All L2 and deeper chunks shall be hashed as part of their LIST L1 chunk, and padding bytes shall be treated as part of, and hashed with, the preceding chunk.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s357-16-3-3-3-6-font-specific-handling",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.3.3.6. Font-specific Handling",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s357-16-3-3-3-6-font-specific-handling.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.3.3.3.6. Font-specific Handling\n\nThe tables of a font correspond directly to the hash boxes, including the `C2PA` table.\n\nTables are always enumerated in the order they appear in the font’s table directory.\n\nNote that the table directory itself is not part of the hashed content, and therefore not covered by any box.\n\nThe `checkSumAdjustment` value shall be treated as zero (`0`) when computing the hash for the box containing the `head` table.\n\nThe grouping, or lack thereof, of Font tables in the general box hash assertion is up to the claim generator.\n\nNote: Fonts created for wide dis",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that font tables, including the C2PA table, correspond directly to hash boxes enumerated in table directory order, with the table directory itself not hashed and checkSumAdjustment treated as zero when hashing the box containing the head table. Leaves the grouping of tables into boxes to the claim generator, noting that one table per box helps hashes survive re-packaging while combined boxes may not validate after a format transformation. States that, because font consumers shall not react to unrecognized tables, existing infrastructure expects the head table's checkSumAdjustment to incorporate the final content of the C2PA table.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s358-16-3-3-3-7-ogg-specific-handling",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.3.3.7. Ogg-specific Handling",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s358-16-3-3-3-7-ogg-specific-handling.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.3.3.3.7. Ogg-specific Handling\n\nIn an Ogg file, the structure consists of one or more logical bitstreams, and the data for each stream is held in Ogg Pages. For the purpose of hashing, each logical bitstream is treated as a single 'box', which includes every Page, in order, with the same bitstream\\_serial\\_number. The C2PA Manifest Store 'box' is the logical bitstream identified in [Section A.3.7, “Embedding manifests into OGG Vorbis”](#_embedding_manifests_into_ogg_vorbis).\n\nThe box-name for each non-C2PA logical bitstream shall be a string constructed in the format: Stream-\\[bitstr",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that, for hashing an Ogg file, each logical bitstream is treated as a single box comprising all its Pages in order, with the C2PA Manifest Store box being the bitstream identified in Section A.3.7, Embedding manifests into OGG Vorbis. Requires each non-C2PA bitstream's box name to be Stream-[bitstream_serial_number], using the ASCII base-10 value of the serial number read as a 32-bit little-endian unsigned integer, so that serial number \\x01\\x00\\x00\\x00 yields \"Stream-1\".",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s359-16-3-3-4-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
