      "target": "../sections/s359-16-3-3-4-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.3.4. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `box-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.4.4, “Boxes Hash”](#cddl_annex_boxes_hash) for the complete normative schema):\n\nCDDL for Box Hash\n\n```cddl\nbox-map = {\n  \"boxes\": [1* box-hash-map],\n\n  ; A string identifying the cryptographic hash algorithm used to compute the\n  ; hash in this assertion, taken from the C2PA hash algorithm identifier list.\n  ; If this field is absent, the hash algorithm is taken the `alg` value of the\n  ; enclosing structure. If",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the CDDL schema for the general box hash through the box-map rule (boxes and optional alg) and box-hash-map (names, optional alg, hash, optional excluded, exclusions, pad and pad2), with box-exclusions-map entries of start, length and optional boxIndex, and refers to Section G.4.4, Boxes Hash, for the complete normative schema. Gives CBOR diagnostic examples for JPEG 1, PNG, GIF, TTF and JXL. Requires exclusion start and length values to use preferred (shortest) serialization normally, but to be written as 32-bit integers when not yet known.",
