      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.4.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s361-16-3-4-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.4.1. Description\n\nIn workflows where it is known in advance that the C2PA Manifest will refer to a collection of assets, instead of a single asset, the collection data hash assertion shall be used as the method to specify the [hard bindings](#_hard_bindings) (i.e., cryptographic hashes) for the assets in the collection.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> It is possible to describe each folder of the training data set of an AI/ML model by having each folder be a separate ingredient of the complete training data set’s manifest.\n\nA collection data hash assertion shall have a label of `c2pa.hash.collection",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that, when a C2PA Manifest is known in advance to refer to a collection of assets rather than a single asset, the collection data hash assertion be used to specify the hard bindings for the assets in the collection. Notes that each folder of an AI/ML training data set can be described as a separate ingredient of the full data set's manifest. The assertion shall be labelled c2pa.hash.collection.data and shall not appear in a cloud data assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
