      "target": "../sections/s362-16-3-4-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.4.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `collection-data-hash-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.4.5, “Collection Data Hash”](#cddl_annex_collection_data_hash) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; An array of URIs and their associated hashes\n$collection-data-hash-map /= {\n  \"uris\": [1* $uri-hashed-data-map],\n\n  ; A string identifying the cryptographic hash algorithm used to compute the\n  ; hash on each entry of the `uris` array, taken from the C2PA hash algorithm\n  ; identifier li",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the CDDL schema for the collection data hash assertion through the collection-data-hash-map rule, which holds a uris array of hashed URI entries, a required alg and an optional zip_central_directory_hash, and also allows URN-based record identifiers per RFC 8141; the complete normative schema is in Section G.4.5, Collection Data Hash. Gives CBOR diagnostic examples for a list of remote URLs, a list of relative file URIs and relative paths inside an EPUB.",
        "state": "draft",
