      "target": "../sections/s366-16-3-5-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.5.1. Description\n\nThere exist a number of file formats that are composed of multiple parts, where each part is itself a valid file format, such as when multiple individual images are aggregated into a single file. Some examples include:\n\n*   [CIPA Multi-Picture Format (MPF)](https://www.cipa.jp/std/documents/download_e.html?CIPA_DC-007-2025_E)\n    \n*   Android [Ultra HDR](https://developer.android.com/media/platform/hdr-image-format) format (which uses MPF)\n    \n*   [ISO 21496](https://www.iso.org/standard/86775.html) HDR (which uses MPF)\n    \n*   [Android Motion Photo](https://deve",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes file formats composed of multiple parts that are each valid files, such as CIPA Multi-Picture Format, Android Ultra HDR, ISO 21496 HDR and Android Motion Photo. Explains that existing hard binding assertions cannot separately verify each part's integrity or record parts' own C2PA Manifests, and that the multi-asset hash assertion provides this. Also notes the case of an optional part that may be removed by a workflow without a trusted signer while the rest of the file remains verifiable.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
