      "target": "../sections/s372-16-3-6-3-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.6.3. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `segment-hash-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.4.7, “Segment Hash”](#cddl_annex_segment_hash) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; Segment hash assertion for append-only plain-text files.\n; Carries the byte-exact binding between a signed checkpoint manifest\n; and its covered segment, together with a cryptographic digest of the\n; immediately preceding sentinel line so that historical sentinels cannot\n; be rewritten without invalidating the",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the CDDL schema for the segment hash assertion through the segment-hash-map rule, with version 1, optional alg, hash, segmentStart, segmentEnd, optional sentinelLength, optional predecessorSentinel and optional metadata, and a predecessor-sentinel-map whose start, length and hash fields are required together; the full normative schema is in Section G.4.7, Segment Hash. Gives a CBOR diagnostic example using the offsets and hashes of the second checkpoint from Section A.3.17.6, Test vectors.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
