    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s374-16-3-7-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.7.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s374-16-3-7-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.7.1. Description\n\nIf a claim generator will be providing a soft binding for the asset’s content, it shall be described using a soft binding assertion. The types of soft bindings which may be created and stored in such an assertion are described in [Section 16.3.7, “Soft Binding”](#soft_binding_assertion).\n\nA previous version of this specification provided a `url` field to provide a pointer to where the hashed data may be located, but it was never used. This field is now deprecated in favor of the [asset reference assertion](#_asset_reference). Claim generators shall not add this fie",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that a soft binding a claim generator provides for an asset's content be described using a soft binding assertion labelled c2pa.soft-binding. Deprecates the never-used url field in favor of the asset reference assertion, so claim generators shall not add it and consumers shall ignore it. Also deprecates the extent field within scope in favor of the region field, so claim generators shall not add it and consumers should ignore it; in both cases the field still counts as part of the content validated per Section 14.10.4, Assertion Validation.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s375-16-3-7-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.7.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s375-16-3-7-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.7.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `soft-binding-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.12, “Soft Binding”](#cddl_annex_soft_binding) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; Align regions-of-interest object structure in soft-binding assertions with\n; that used for other purposes\n; # include regions-of-interest\n\n; The data structure used to store one or more soft bindings across some or all\n; of the asset's content\nsoft-binding-map = {\n  ; A string identifying the soft binding algo",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies the CDDL schema for the soft binding assertion through the soft-binding-map rule, with alg, blocks, optional pad, pad2, name, alg-params, bindingMetadata, deprecated url and metadata; each soft-binding-block-map has a scope (deprecated extent, timespan in milliseconds or region) and a value, and the full normative schema is in Section G.5.12, Soft Binding. Gives a CBOR diagnostic example using the phash algorithm with two timespan blocks.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s376-16-3-7-3-requirements",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.7.3. Requirements",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s376-16-3-7-3-requirements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.7.3. Requirements\n\nThe soft binding algorithm used shall be present as the value of the `alg` field, and the blocks over which it was applied shall be listed in the `blocks` field. If the algorithm used requires any additional parameters, they should be present as the value of `alg-params`.\n\nThe `scope` field may contain either a `region` or `timespan` field to describe the portion of digital content that the soft binding has been computed over. The `region` field, when present, contains a `region-map` object (as defined in [Section 16.9.2, “Regions of Interest”](#_regions_of_intere",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires the soft binding algorithm to be given in the alg field and the blocks it was applied over to be listed in blocks, and recommends that any extra algorithm parameters be placed in alg-params. Allows the scope field to contain either a region (a region-map from Section 16.9.2, Regions of Interest) or a timespan in milliseconds from the start of the content, and requires pad and pad2, if present, to be zero-filled byte strings.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s377-16-3-7-3-1-bindingmetadata",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.7.3.1. bindingMetadata",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s377-16-3-7-3-1-bindingmetadata.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.3.7.3.1. bindingMetadata\n\nA soft binding assertion may include a `bindingMetadata` key that provides for the specification of some algorithm or workflow-specific information via some pre-defined as well as custom fields (and their associated values). Custom fields shall conform to the same syntax as [entity-specific namespacing](#_namespacing), e.g. `com.litware.someFieldName`.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This is useful for providing extra information that would be useful to a specific workflow or C2PA Manifest Consumer.\n\nA C2PA Validator should not use this information when validating the soft b",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Allows a soft binding assertion to include a bindingMetadata key carrying pre-defined and custom algorithm- or workflow-specific fields, with custom fields required to follow entity-specific namespacing (e.g. com.litware.someFieldName). States that a C2PA Validator should not use this information when validating the soft binding but may use it for logging or informational purposes, since the normative validation information is in the other assertion fields and the algorithm's entry in the Soft Binding Algorithm List.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s378-16-3-7-4-soft-binding-algorithm-list",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.7.4. Soft Binding Algorithm List",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s378-16-3-7-4-soft-binding-algorithm-list.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.7.4. Soft Binding Algorithm List\n\nThe soft binding algorithm list is a machine readable list of recommended values for the `alg` field. The value of the `alg` field should correspond to the `alg` field of an algorithm present in that list. The format of `alg-params` and `value` fields are algorithm specific and described via a human readable information page referenced by `informationalUrl` within the entry for `alg` in the list.\n\nThe list is maintained as a JSON document by the C2PA at the following location: [https://sbal.c2pa.org](https://sbal.c2pa.org)\n\nEntries in the soft bindi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the soft binding algorithm list, a machine-readable JSON document maintained by the C2PA at https://sbal.c2pa.org, as the list of recommended values for the alg field, which should match an entry's alg. Entries marked deprecated shall not be used to create soft binding assertions, and resolving with them is discouraged; validators should not resolve such bindings. Gives the JSON schema for entries and requires each entry's alg to follow namespacing and represent the owner, each algorithm version to have its own entry, type to be watermark or fingerprint, and supported media types to be given as encodedMediaTypes or decodedMediaTypes based on IANA types. Requires entryMetadata with a description and dateEntered, a required contact email and a required informationalUrl to a page describing the algorithm, including the algorithm-specific format of alg-params and value.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s379-16-3-7-5-soft-binding-resolution-api",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.7.5. Soft Binding Resolution API",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s379-16-3-7-5-soft-binding-resolution-api.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.3.7.5. Soft Binding Resolution API\n\nThe soft binding resolution API is a Web API providing a standard way of retrieving C2PA Manifest stores from a soft binding resolution API endpoint given a soft binding value, a manifest identifier, or an asset. The soft binding algorithm list entry may contain a list of URIs of soft binding resolution APIs in the `softBindingResolutionApis` field. If several URIs are given then any may be used for a soft binding resolution.\n\nThe API specification and documentation is available [here](../softbinding/Decoupled.html.md#SBR-API).\n\n<a id=\"_validating_s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the soft binding resolution API as a Web API for retrieving C2PA Manifest stores from an endpoint given a soft binding value, a manifest identifier or an asset. States that a soft binding algorithm list entry may list resolution API URIs in softBindingResolutionApis, any of which may be used, and points to the separate API specification.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
