    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s380-16-3-7-5-1-validating-soft-binding-matches",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.3.7.5.1. Validating Soft Binding Matches",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s380-16-3-7-5-1-validating-soft-binding-matches.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.3.7.5.1. Validating Soft Binding Matches\n\nA common use for soft bindings is to discover the active manifest, from a manifest repository, for an asset whose C2PA Manifest is absent or invalid.\n\nDiscovery of the C2PA Manifest shall be performed using one, or a combination of, algorithms identified by the `alg` field within the C2PA Soft Binding Algorithm List. The list is maintained as a JSON document by the C2PA at the following location: [https://sbal.c2pa.org](https://sbal.c2pa.org)\n\nIf a C2PA Manifest is found in a manifest repository, and that manifest contains one or more soft bi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes using soft bindings to discover the active manifest in a manifest repository for an asset whose C2PA Manifest is absent or invalid, requiring discovery to use one or more algorithms identified in the C2PA Soft Binding Algorithm List. Requires that, if the located manifest contains soft binding assertions, the matcher ensure all of them match the soft bindings used for discovery. A soft binding assertion matches when both its alg and value match those used, with matching performed as the specified algorithm prescribes.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
