    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s388-16-4-1-4-2-reason",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.4.2. Reason",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s388-16-4-1-4-2-reason.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.4.2. Reason\n\nIf present, the `reason` field shall contain one of these standard values, or a custom value which conforms to the same syntax as [entity-specific namespacing](#_namespacing), for the rationale behind the action:\n\n*   `c2pa.PII.present`;\n    \n*   `c2pa.invalid.data`;\n    \n*   `c2pa.trade-secret.present`;\n    \n*   `c2pa.government.confidential`.\n    \n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Although the `reason` field can be used for any actions, only redaction-focused `c2pa` values are defined at this time.\n\nWhen using a `c2pa.redacted` action, the `reason` field shall contain the rationale f",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that the reason field, if present, contain one of the standard values c2pa.PII.present, c2pa.invalid.data, c2pa.trade-secret.present or c2pa.government.confidential, or a custom value following entity-specific namespacing. Notes that only redaction-focused c2pa values are defined so far, and requires that a c2pa.redacted action's reason field contain the rationale for the redaction.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s389-16-4-1-4-3-when",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.4.3. When",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s389-16-4-1-4-3-when.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.4.3. When\n\nAlso present may be the date and time when the action took place in the `when` field. If included, the value of the `when` field shall be compliant with CBOR date/times ([RFC 8949](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949), 3.4.1).\n\nClaim generators should use `when` for a single, exact action time. It shall be interpreted as equivalent to `whenStart` and `whenEnd` both having the same `absolute` value.\n\nA v2 action may instead include `whenStart`, `whenEnd`, or both.\n\n`whenStart` shall use `generator-lower-bound-time-type`, and `whenEnd` shall use `generator-upper-bound",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Allows an action to include a when field for the time of the action, which shall be a CBOR date/time and shall be interpreted as whenStart and whenEnd sharing the same absolute value; claim generators should use when for a single exact time. A v2 action may instead use whenStart (generator-lower-bound-time-type) and whenEnd (generator-upper-bound-time-type) as defined in Section 8.9, with whenStart not later than whenEnd when both are present, and when shall not appear together with either of them. Notes that these are claim-generator-provided timestamps and that UTC-based times should be used.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s390-16-4-1-4-4-softwareagent",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.4.4. SoftwareAgent",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s390-16-4-1-4-4-softwareagent.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.4.4. SoftwareAgent\n\nThe software or hardware used to perform the action can be identified via the `softwareAgent` field. In a v1 action, this is a simple text string. However, for v2, `softwareAgent` uses the richer `generator-info-map` structure as described in [Section 10.2.3.2, “Generator Info Map”](#_generator_info_map). When multiple softwareAgents are used, as described in [Section 16.4.1.6.2, “SoftwareAgents”](#_softwareagents), then the `softwareAgentIndex` field shall be used to reference the softwareAgent by its 0-based index in the `softwareAgents` array. A given actio",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the softwareAgent field identifying the software or hardware that performed an action, a text string in v1 and a generator-info-map in v2. When multiple softwareAgents are used, softwareAgentIndex shall reference the agent by its 0-based index in the softwareAgents array, and an action shall have only one of softwareAgent or softwareAgentIndex. Notes that these fields help when the agent differs from the claim generator and that the earlier actors field was removed in version 2.0.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s391-16-4-1-4-5-digital-source-type",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.4.5. Digital Source Type",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s391-16-4-1-4-5-digital-source-type.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.4.5. Digital Source Type\n\nAn action may include a `digitalSourceType` key, whose value shall be one of the terms [defined by the IPTC](http://cv.iptc.org/newscodes/digitalsourcetype/) or a C2PA specific value from the list below:\n\n`[http://c2pa.org/digitalsourcetype/empty](http://c2pa.org/digitalsourcetype/empty)`\n\nMedia whose [digital content](#_digital_content) is effectively empty, such as a blank canvas or zero-length video.\n\n`[http://c2pa.org/digitalsourcetype/trainedAlgorithmicData](http://c2pa.org/digitalsourcetype/trainedAlgorithmicData)`\n\nData that is the result of algor",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Allows an action to include a digitalSourceType whose value shall be an IPTC-defined term or one of the C2PA values http://c2pa.org/digitalsourcetype/empty (effectively empty content) or http://c2pa.org/digitalsourcetype/trainedAlgorithmicData (model-derived data in a data format rather than a media type). Notes its common use with c2pa.created to indicate how media was created, and states that for trained algorithmic assets one or more ingredients may be added to describe the inputs and referenced from a c2pa.placed or c2pa.created action.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s392-16-4-1-4-6-unique-identifiers-for-actions",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.4.6. Unique Identifiers for Actions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s392-16-4-1-4-6-unique-identifiers-for-actions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.4.6. Unique Identifiers for Actions\n\nWhere a unique identifier for an instance of a specific action is required, it can be either determined implicitly or through explicit declaration. Implicitly, each action can be identified and its unique identifier assembled according to the following recommendation:\n\nUse the [JUMBF URI](#_standard_uris) of that `actions` assertion, which includes the unique manifest ID and a path to the `actions` assertion. For example: `self#jumbf=/c2pa/urn:c2pa:ABCD:joe-ed/c2pa.assertions/c2pa.actions.v2`. If it is also necessary to refer to a specific act",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes how to identify a specific action instance, either implicitly or explicitly. Recommends implicitly using the JUMBF URI of the actions assertion and, for a specific action, appending &cbor= with a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) path such as /actions/1, observing all JSON Pointer rules. Suggests a custom parameters key such as com.fabrikam.actionId for an explicit identifier.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s393-16-4-1-4-7-changes",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.4.7. Changes",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s393-16-4-1-4-7-changes.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.4.7. Changes\n\nThe action may be specific to only a portion of an asset - such as a range of frames in a video or a specific area on an image. In v1, the value was a simple text string. For v2, they are identified using a `changes` field, whose value is an array of `region-map` objects (as defined in [Section 16.9.2, “Regions of Interest”](#_regions_of_interest)).\n\n<a id=\"_parameters\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that an action may apply to only part of an asset, such as a range of video frames or an image area; in v1 this was a text string, while in v2 it is a changes field holding an array of region-map objects from Section 16.9.2, Regions of Interest.",
        "state": "draft",
