    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s394-16-4-1-4-8-parameters",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.4.8. Parameters",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s394-16-4-1-4-8-parameters.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.4.8. Parameters\n\nAn action may include a `parameters` key that provides for the specification of some action-specific information via some pre-defined as well as the open-ended inclusion of any custom fields (and their associated values). Custom fields shall conform to the same syntax as [entity-specific namespacing](#_namespacing), e.g. `com.litware.someFieldName`.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This is useful for providing extra information that would be useful to a specific workflow or C2PA Manifest Consumer.\n\nA claim generator that performs the same action over and over, with the same parame",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the parameters key for action-specific pre-defined and custom fields, with custom fields required to follow entity-specific namespacing, and the optional multipleInstances field, whose absence means it is unknown whether the action was repeated. Requires c2pa.opened and c2pa.placed actions to hold hashed JUMBF URIs to related ingredient assertions in ingredient (v1) or ingredients (v2), allows a c2pa.deleted action to reference a componentOf ingredient whose content it fully removes, and recommends regionOfInterest metadata when only part of an ingredient is relevant. Requires sourceLanguage and targetLanguage in c2pa.translated to be BCP 47 codes and the redacted field of c2pa.redacted to hold the JUMBF URI of the redacted assertion, and allows an optional machine-readable name field that sub-classifies the action. Gives an example c2pa.created action for a Generative AI image referencing two ingredients.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s395-16-4-1-4-9-related-assertions",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.4.9. Related Assertions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s395-16-4-1-4-9-related-assertions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.4.9. Related Assertions\n\nAn action may include a `relatedAssertions` key in the `parameters` object. If present, the value shall be an array of one or more hashed JUMBF URIs identifying assertion(s) that are related to the action.\n\nEach entry in `relatedAssertions` shall reference an assertion in the same C2PA Manifest as the action. The related assertion(s) provide additional information about, or are otherwise related to, the action.\n\nEntries in `relatedAssertions` shall not reference an actions nor an ingredient assertion (i.e., an assertion whose label is `c2pa.actions`, `c2p",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Allows an action's parameters to include relatedAssertions, an array of one or more hashed JUMBF URIs to related assertions in the same C2PA Manifest. Entries shall not reference actions or ingredient assertions (c2pa.actions, c2pa.actions.v2, c2pa.ingredient, c2pa.ingredient.v2 or c2pa.ingredient.v3), and Manifest Consumers may use them to present additional context. Notes that this lets an action reference, for example, an assertion metadata assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s396-16-4-1-5-watermarking",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.5. Watermarking",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s396-16-4-1-5-watermarking.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.1.5. Watermarking\n\nWhen using a `c2pa.watermarked.bound` action, a [soft binding assertion](#soft_binding_assertion) shall also be included in the C2PA Manifest to describe the inserted watermark. The `c2pa.watermarked.bound` action should reference one or more of these corresponding soft binding assertions using the `relatedAssertions` field in the `parameters` object of that action.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The `c2pa.watermarked` action is deprecated in favour of the more specific `c2pa.watermarked.bound` and `c2pa.watermarked.unbound` actions.\n\n<a id=\"_action_templates\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that a c2pa.watermarked.bound action be accompanied by a soft binding assertion describing the inserted watermark, which the action should reference through relatedAssertions in its parameters. Notes that c2pa.watermarked is deprecated in favor of c2pa.watermarked.bound and c2pa.watermarked.unbound.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
