        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.6.2. SoftwareAgents",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s399-16-4-1-6-2-softwareagents.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.6.2. SoftwareAgents\n\nIf multiple softwareAgents were used, they can be listed in the `softwareAgents` field instead. This field is an array of `generator-info-map` objects, each of which describes a different software or hardware which can then be referenced by its index via the `softwareAgentIndex` field of a given action or template.\n\nExample 7. Software Agents example\n\nAn example of specifying multiple agents across multiple actions, in CBOR diagnostic notation ([RFC 8949](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949), clause 8):\n\n```none\n{\n    \"actions\": [\n        {\n            \"ac",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the softwareAgents field, an array of generator-info-map objects that can list multiple software or hardware agents, each referenced by index through the softwareAgentIndex field of an action or template. Gives a CBOR diagnostic example of six actions referencing two agents.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s400-16-4-1-6-3-icons",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.6.3. Icons",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s400-16-4-1-6-3-icons.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.6.3. Icons\n\nA template may also include an icon - an image (raster or vector) that can be used in the C2PA Manifest Consumer’s user experience to provide some graphic representation of the action. Since a Manifest Consumer will know about all the defined actions, such icons shall only be present in templates for entity-specific actions.\n\nThe value of the `icon` field, if present, shall be a [hashed URI](#_hashed_uris). This hashed URI shall be to either a [embedded data assertion](#_embedded_data) or to a [cloud data assertion](#_cloud_data). If a embedded data assertion is used,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Allows a template to include an icon, a raster or vector image the Manifest Consumer can use to represent the action, but requires icons to appear only in templates for entity-specific actions. The icon value, if present, shall be a hashed URI to an embedded data assertion (labelled c2pa.icon and following the multiple-instance label rules) or a cloud data assertion, matching the structure of the icon field in the Claim's Generator Info Map. Recommends that Manifest Consumers also support the data box approach from earlier versions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s401-16-4-1-7-localizations",
