      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.12. Relationship Between Actions and Ingredients",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s406-16-4-1-12-relationship-between-actions-and-ingre.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.1.12. Relationship Between Actions and Ingredients\n\nActions and ingredients are closely related concepts: an actions assertion records _what_ happened to an asset, while an ingredient assertion records the other asset(s) or data involved in that history. The requirements linking the two are described throughout this section and [Section 16.5, “Ingredient”](#ingredient_assertion); this section summarizes them for ease of reference.\n\nIn many cases, adding an ingredient to a C2PA Manifest requires a corresponding entry in the `actions` array, and vice versa. For example, a `c2pa.opened",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Summarises the requirements that link actions assertions, which record what happened to an asset, with ingredient assertions, which record the other assets or data involved, noting that adding one often requires a matching entry in the other and that c2pa.opened and c2pa.placed actions must reference their ingredient assertions. It gives further examples: a c2pa.created action may reference inputTo ingredients such as Generative AI inputs, and a c2pa.deleted action may reference a componentOf ingredient and should be paired with c2pa.redacted when that ingredient assertion is also redacted.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
