      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s407-16-4-1-12-1-digital-source-type.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.4.1.12.1. Digital Source Type\n\nThe `digitalSourceType` of an ingredient can be established in one of two ways, depending on whether the ingredient has an active manifest:\n\n*   If the ingredient has an active manifest, its `digitalSourceType` could be inferred from information provided by that manifest, as described in [Section 16.4.1.4.5, “Digital Source Type”](#_digital_source_type).\n    \n*   If the ingredient does not have an active manifest, the ingredient assertion itself may carry a `digitalSourceType` field, as described in [Section 16.5.12, “Existing manifests”](#_existing_man",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that an ingredient's digitalSourceType can be inferred from its active manifest if it has one, or otherwise carried in the ingredient assertion itself, that an ingredient assertion shall not contain both activeManifest and digitalSourceType, and that an ingredient may declare no digitalSourceType at all.",
        "state": "draft",
