    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s409-16-4-1-14-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.1.14. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s409-16-4-1-14-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.1.14. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for `c2pa.actions` is defined by the `actions-map` rule, and the schema for `c2pa.actions.v2` is defined by the `actions-map-v2` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.1, “Actions”](#cddl_annex_actions) for the complete normative schema):\n\nCDDL for Action choices\n\n```cddl\n; DO NOT EDIT — generated from actions.yaml\n; Run generateActions.sh to regenerate.\n; Structural definitions are in actions.cddl\n\n$action-choice /= \"c2pa.addedText\"\n$action-choice /= \"c2pa.adjustedColor\"\n$action-choice /",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL schemas for the actions assertions, with c2pa.actions defined by the deprecated actions-map rule and c2pa.actions.v2 by actions-map-v2, plus the generated list of predefined action names (c2pa.* and font.* actions, with a pattern allowing custom names). The v2 schema defines a required actions array and allActionsIncluded flag, optional templates, softwareAgents and metadata, and per-action fields such as softwareAgent, description, digitalSourceType, exact or ranged timing (when, or whenStart and whenEnd), changes, related, reason (required for c2pa.redacted) and parameters including redacted, ingredients, relatedAssertions, sourceLanguage, targetLanguage, name and multipleInstances. It also gives a CDDL for font-specific action parameters (Unicode ranges and variable-font instance settings such as weight, width, italic, slant and optical size) and a CBOR diagnostic example of a v2 actions assertion with a filtered and a cropped action.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
