    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s411-16-4-2-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.2.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s411-16-4-2-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.2.1. Description\n\nThere are use cases where storing the data for an assertion remotely, such as in the cloud, is better than embedded inside the asset, especially for those cases where that data may change over time. Additionally, it may be important to reference non-assertion-based data stored externally. To address those needs, a specific type of assertion serves as an external reference to the location of that information. An external reference assertion may use an `unhashed-ext-uri-map` for the `location` field, where the referenced data is advisory and may change over time, or",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the external reference assertion (label c2pa.external-reference), which points to data stored remotely, either advisory and changeable via an unhashed-ext-uri-map or cryptographically bound at signing via a hashed-ext-uri-map, in a required location field with an optional label when the target is a complete assertion; it should appear in gathered_assertions and shall not reference actions, hash, cloud-data, external-reference or ingredient assertions. Referenced data shall be treated as optional and should not be retrieved during manifest validation, unhashed retrieved data shall be treated as advisory unless independently verified, and the size field should be omitted when the referenced data may change.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
