    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s413-16-4-2-3-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.2.3. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s413-16-4-2-3-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.2.3. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `external-reference-map` and `hashed-external-reference-map` rules in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.8, “External Reference”](#cddl_annex_external_reference) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; Assertion that references assertion data stored externally by URI (no hash)\nexternal-reference-map = {\n  ; specifies the location and type of the remote data\n  \"location\": unhashed-ext-uri-map,\n\n  ; label for the referenced assertion, if relevant (e.g., c2p",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for the external reference assertion as two rules, external-reference-map with an unhashed location and hashed-external-reference-map with a hashed location, each also allowing optional label, description and metadata fields. It also defines the unhashed-ext-uri-map (url plus optional dc:format, size and data_types) and the hashed-ext-uri-map, which additionally requires alg and hash. CBOR diagnostic examples show unhashed references to a remote c2pa.metadata assertion, an arbitrary blob and changing JSON data, and hashed references to an audit log and a version history.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
