    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s415-16-4-3-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.3.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s415-16-4-3-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.3.1. Description\n\nMany container formats embed URI references to external resources (for example, scripts and stylesheets in HTML, or texture files in MaterialX scenes) but provide no native mechanism to hash-bind those dependencies. A linked resource integrity assertion provides cryptographic hash coverage for such externally referenced resources, supplying the equivalent of W3C Subresource Integrity ([Subresource Integrity Level 2](https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-sri-2-20260320/)) for formats that do not natively support that concept.\n\nThe `resources` field is an object containing e",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the linked resource integrity assertion (label c2pa.linked-resource-integrity), which provides hash coverage, akin to W3C Subresource Integrity, for external resources referenced by container formats, using a resources field holding either an externalResources array of hashed absolute URLs or a relativeResources array with a shared alg; it shall appear only in created_assertions, and relative URIs shall be resolved against the asset's location, or treated as unresolvable when that location is unknown. The optional allURIsIncluded flag, when true, says every fetched or embedded reference the signer can enumerate at signing time is covered, excluding navigational links, the manifest itself and transitively discovered resources, while an absent value should be read as meaning more references may exist; validators are not required to retrieve resources, so hash checking is optional.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s416-16-4-3-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.3.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s416-16-4-3-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.3.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `linked-resource-integrity-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.15, “Linked Resource Integrity”](#cddl_annex_linked_resource_integrity) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; One or more external resources with cryptographic hashes, used when the\n; container format only supports absolute references to external resources.\nexternal-resources-map = {\n  \"externalResources\": [1* $hashed-ext-uri-map],\n}\n\n; One or more relative resources with cryptog",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for the linked resource integrity assertion, where linked-resource-integrity-map holds resources as either an external-resources-map or a relative-resources-map (with its own alg), plus optional allURIsIncluded and metadata. It also defines the hashed-ext-uri-map and the uri-hashed-data-map, whose relative URI type permits no scheme or authority and leaves rejection of percent-encoded traversal to validation. Two CBOR diagnostic examples show an HTML asset with two fully covered external resources and a MaterialX scene with one relative texture and partial coverage.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
