    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s418-16-4-4-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.4.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s418-16-4-4-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.4.1. Description\n\nThis assertion is used to indicate one or more locations where a copy of the asset may be obtained. Such locations shall each be described using an asset reference assertion. The location shall be expressed via a URI. The URI may be to either a single asset or it may reference a directory. In the latter case, it serves to provide the location for a collection of assets, that would be hashed via a [collection data hash](#_collection_data_hash).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Expressing a `uri` provides flexibility to source the asset from web locations or distributed filesystems su",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the asset reference assertion (label c2pa.asset-ref), which records via URIs one or more locations, a single asset or a directory of collection-hashed assets, where a copy of the asset may be obtained, with the metadata time stamp giving a basis for judging link freshness.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s419-16-4-4-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.4.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s419-16-4-4-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.4.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `asset-ref-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.5, “Asset Reference”](#cddl_annex_asset_ref) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; The asset reference assertion (ARA) describes where a copy of the asset may be\n; obtained.\nasset-ref-map = {\n  \"references\": [1* ara-reference-block-map]\n\n  ; additional information about the assertion\n  ? \"metadata\": $assertion-metadata-map,\n}\n\nara-reference-block-map = {\n  \"reference\": ara-reference-uri-map,\n  ?",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for the asset reference assertion, where asset-ref-map holds a required references array whose entries pair a reference containing a uri with an optional human-readable description, plus optional metadata. A CBOR diagnostic example lists one web location and one IPFS location.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s420-16-4-5-repository-receipt",
