    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s421-16-4-5-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.5.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s421-16-4-5-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.5.1. Description\n\nThere are use cases where a receipt may be desired in order to prove that a C2PA Manifest has been ingested by a C2PA Manifest Repository.\n\nSuch use cases include providing non-repudiation of ingestion, establishing that a manifest was present in a repository at a particular time, or supporting workflows in which an external service attests to registration of the manifest.\n\nSuch a receipt may be recorded via a repository receipt assertion. When recorded, it shall only appear within an [update manifest](#_update_manifests).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Update manifests are used s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the repository receipt assertion (label c2pa.repository-receipt), which may record proof that a C2PA Manifest Repository ingested a manifest and shall appear only in an update manifest, with a body that is a JSON-LD object including @context. Its repository object shall give the repository's base uri and a canonical manifestId, and its anchor object shall give a uri where the proof can be verified and a repository-defined proof object, with optional repository-specific parameters.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s422-16-4-5-2-repository-receipt-assertion-schema-and",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.4.5.2. Repository Receipt Assertion Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s422-16-4-5-2-repository-receipt-assertion-schema-and.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.4.5.2. Repository Receipt Assertion Schema and Example\n\nThe JSON schema for the repository receipt assertion payload is defined in the following:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"$id\": \"https://c2pa.org/schemas/repository-receipt.json\",\n  \"title\": \"C2PA Repository Receipt\",\n  \"description\": \"Receipt showing that a C2PA Manifest Store was ingested by a repository and associated with an external proof of ingestion.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"@context\": {\n      \"type\": [\"object\", \"string\"],",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the JSON Schema for the repository receipt assertion payload, requiring @context, an @type fixed to org.c2pa.repository-receipt, a repository object (uri and manifestId) and an anchor object (uri and proof, with optional parameters). An example JSON object shows a receipt from a repository with an anchor URI, a view parameter and a proof value.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s423-16-5-ingredient",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5. Ingredient",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s423-16-5-ingredient.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### 16.5. Ingredient\n\nThis assertion describes an ingredient - an asset used in the creation of, or otherwise related to, the asset described by the manifest - together with its relationship to that asset and a reference to its own provenance data.\n\n<a id=\"_description_16\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the ingredient assertion, which describes an asset used in creating, or otherwise related to, the asset described by the manifest, together with its relationship to that asset and a reference to its own provenance data.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s424-16-5-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s424-16-5-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.1. Description\n\nWhen assets are composed together, for example placing an image into a layer in an image editing tool or an audio clip into a video in a video editing tool, it is important that information about any claim from the placed asset be recorded into the new asset to provide a way to understand the entire history of the new composed asset. This is also true when an existing asset is used to create a derived asset or asset rendition.\n\nAnother common use for an ingredient is to describe some assets or data that were used as input to a process, such as the training or inferenc",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that ingredients record the provenance of assets composed into, derived from or rendered from other assets, and also describe assets or data used as input to processes such as AI/ML training or inference. It names three versions of the assertion, deprecated c2pa.ingredient and c2pa.ingredient.v2 and the current c2pa.ingredient.v3, which shall be the label used and addresses validating ingredients after redaction, with the usual multiple-instance labelling applying.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s425-16-5-2-establishing-unique-identifiers",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.2. Establishing unique identifiers",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s425-16-5-2-establishing-unique-identifiers.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.2. Establishing unique identifiers\n\nIf the ingredient being added contains a C2PA Manifest, then its unique identifier shall be taken from the [manifest label](#manifest-identifier) of the JUMBF superbox containing the ingredient’s active C2PA Manifest, and it is not necessary to provide the optional `instanceID` field of the ingredient assertion. When the claim generator provides the optional `instanceID` field of the ingredient assertion, then the value of the unique identifier shall be determined as specified by [Section 9.3, “Identifying Non-C2PA Assets”](#_identifying_non_c2pa_a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that an ingredient containing a C2PA Manifest takes its unique identifier from the manifest label of its active manifest, making instanceID unnecessary, while an instanceID supplied by the claim generator shall be determined as specified for non-C2PA assets, and may be supplied even when a manifest exists.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s426-16-5-3-relationship",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.3. Relationship",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s426-16-5-3-relationship.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.3. Relationship\n\nWhen adding an ingredient, its relationship to the current asset shall be described. The possible values of the `relationship` field and their meanings are shown in [Table 6, “Ingredient Relationships”](#ingredient-relationships).\n\n**Table 6. Ingredient Relationships**\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `parentOf` | The current asset is a derived asset or asset rendition of this ingredient. This relationship value is also used with [update manifests](#_update_manifests). |\n| `componentOf` | The current asset is composed of multiple parts, this ingredient being one",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires each ingredient's relationship to be described as parentOf (the asset is derived from or a rendition of it, also used with update manifests), componentOf (it is one part of a composed asset) or inputTo (it was input to a computational process such as an AI/ML model). In Standard Manifests a claim generator adding an ingredient shall ensure a c2pa.actions assertion exists and add c2pa.opened for parentOf or c2pa.placed for componentOf, and a parentOf or componentOf ingredient assertion shall be listed in the same claim field (created_assertions or gathered_assertions) as the actions assertion referring to it.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s427-16-5-4-title",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.4. Title",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s427-16-5-4-title.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.4. Title\n\nIf present, the value of `dc:title` shall be a human-readable name for the ingredient, which may be taken either from the asset’s XMP or the asset’s name in a local or remote (e.g., cloud-based) filesystem. However, claim generators should not set this value if the information is available in the ingredient’s active C2PA Manifest.\n\n<a id=\"_format\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that dc:title, if present, shall be a human-readable ingredient name taken from XMP or a filesystem name, but claim generators should not set it when the information is available in the ingredient's active manifest.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s428-16-5-5-format",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.5. Format",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s428-16-5-5-format.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.5. Format\n\nIf present, the value of `dc:format` shall be the IANA Media Type for the ingredient. It is recommended that a claim generator should provide this field and it shall contain a valid value. When describing a [multi-file ingredient](#_multi_file_ingredients), such as the data set of an AI/ML model, the `dc:format` field shall be set to `multipart/mixed`.\n\n<a id=\"ingredient_schema\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that dc:format, if present, shall be the ingredient's IANA media type, that claim generators should provide it with a valid value, and that multi-file ingredients such as an AI/ML data set shall use multipart/mixed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s429-16-5-6-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.6. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s429-16-5-6-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.6. Schema and Example\n\nThe [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) for this type is shown below (see [Section G.5.4, “Ingredient”](#cddl_annex_ingredient) for the complete normative schema, including all versions):\n\n```cddl\n; Version 3 (v3) of the ingredient assertion\n; Assertion that describes an ingredient used in the asset\ningredient-map-v3 = {\n  ? \"dc:title\": tstr, ; name of the ingredient\n  ? \"dc:format\": format-string, ; Media Type of the ingredient\n\n  ; The relationship of this ingredient to the asset it is an ingredient of.\n  \"relationship\": $relation-choice",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for the ingredient assertion in its current v3 form (ingredient-map-v3) and the deprecated v2 and v1 forms, along with the format-string pattern and the relationship values parentOf, componentOf and inputTo. The v3 map requires only relationship and offers optional fields including dc:title, dc:format, validationResults, instanceID, data, dataTypes, either activeManifest or digitalSourceType but not both, relatedAssertions, claimSignature, thumbnail, description, informationalURI, softBindingsMatched, softBindingAlgorithmsMatched and metadata. A CBOR diagnostic example shows a parentOf ingredient with a thumbnail, related assertion, active manifest, claim signature and validationResults including ingredientDeltas.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s430-16-5-7-description-field",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.7. Description field",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s430-16-5-7-description-field.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.7. Description field\n\nAn ingredient may include a free-text description, in the `description` field, of what an the ingredient is or is used for. If present, the content of this field should be produced by the claim generator, and should not contain user-provided information.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> A user-provided ingredient description can be specified using a custom assertion.\n\n<a id=\"_ingredient_data\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Allows an ingredient to carry a free-text description field about what it is or is used for, which should be produced by the claim generator rather than contain user-provided information, user descriptions instead going in a custom assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
