    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s432-16-5-8-1-standard-usage",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.8.1. Standard Usage",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s432-16-5-8-1-standard-usage.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.5.8.1. Standard Usage\n\nIn certain use cases, such as Generative AI, it may be important to have ingredients where the data of the ingredient is provided - either embedded into the C2PA Manifest or via a URL that references the data. This is accomplished through the `data` field in the ingredient, which uses a `hashed-uri` to point to an [embedded data assertion](#_embedded_data) or a `hashed-ext-uri-map` to point to an external reference.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Previous versions of this specification allowed the `hashed_uri` to point to a [data box](#_data_boxes).\n\nUsing an [embedded data ass",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that an ingredient's own data, important for uses such as Generative AI, can be supplied through the data field, as a hashed-uri to an embedded data assertion or a hashed-ext-uri-map to external data, and that claim generators should weigh size since embedded data is carried into future manifests unless redacted. Where data can be neither embedded nor linked, such as a private AI model, an asset type in data_types can describe it, and examples show prompt, public model and private model ingredients.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s433-16-5-8-2-multi-file-ingredients",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.8.2. Multi-file Ingredients",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s433-16-5-8-2-multi-file-ingredients.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.5.8.2. Multi-file Ingredients\n\nIn some cases, an ingredient may be represented as a set of multiple files, such as the training data set for an AI/ML model. It is recommended that in those instances that the [C2PA Manifest](#_existing_manifests) be included in the ingredient assertion and that the C2PA Manifest for the full data set include an [asset reference assertion](#_asset_reference) that references where to find those files.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This method is well suited for when working with a collection of assets where all of the files are not contained in the same hierarchy.\n\n<a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recommends that an ingredient made of multiple files, such as an AI/ML training data set, include its C2PA Manifest in the ingredient assertion and that the data set's manifest include an asset reference assertion pointing to where the files are found.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s434-16-5-9-informational-uri",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.9. Informational URI",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s434-16-5-9-informational-uri.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.9. Informational URI\n\nWhen it is necessary to provide a URL to a web page with information about the ingredient, such as detailed information about an AI/ML model, it should be placed as the value of the `informationalURI` field of the ingredient assertion.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The `informationalURI` is not an authenticated link to the content of the ingredient itself, but something more generally of interest to a human user.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Older (and deprecated) versions of the ingredient assertion named this field `informational_URI`.\n\n<a id=\"_thumbnails\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that a URL to a web page about an ingredient, such as AI/ML model details, should go in the informationalURI field, which is not an authenticated link to the ingredient's content and was named informational_URI in deprecated versions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s435-16-5-10-thumbnails",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.10. Thumbnails",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s435-16-5-10-thumbnails.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.10. Thumbnails\n\nWhen adding an ingredient, it may be useful to also include a thumbnail of the ingredient to help establish the state of the ingredient at the time of import. For that purpose, a thumbnail shall be added as a [thumbnail assertion](#thumbnail_assertion) and referenced herein via a hashed-uri reference. If a new thumbnail assertion is created in the active manifest, it shall also be added to the [`relatedAssertions`](#ingredient_related_assertions) field.\n\nManifest Consumers should also support the [data box](#_data_boxes) approach recommended by earlier versions of thi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Specifies that a thumbnail recording an ingredient's state at import shall be added as a thumbnail assertion referenced by hashed-uri, and also added to relatedAssertions when newly created in the active manifest, while Manifest Consumers should still support the earlier data box approach.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s436-16-5-11-related-assertions",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.11. Related Assertions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s436-16-5-11-related-assertions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.11. Related Assertions\n\nIn cases where there are other assertions in the active manifest that should be understood as being about an ingredient rather than about the current asset, the claim generator may reference those assertions using the `relatedAssertions` field of the ingredient assertion. The value of this field shall be an array of one or more hashed JUMBF URIs, each referencing an assertion, in the same C2PA Manifest, that is neither an ingredient nor an action assertion.\n\nAn ingredient assertion can contain both an `activeManifest` and a `relatedAssertions` key. However, as",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Allows the claim generator to use the ingredient's relatedAssertions field, an array of hashed JUMBF URIs to non-ingredient, non-action assertions in the same manifest, to mark assertions that are about the ingredient rather than the current asset, though such assertions should appear in the ingredient's own manifest where possible. Each referenced assertion shall have a label ending in .ingredient (for example c2pa.ai-disclosure.ingredient or com.litware.metadata.ingredient) following the usual multiple-instance rules, and an example shows an inputTo ingredient referencing an AI disclosure assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s437-16-5-12-existing-manifests",
