        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s440-16-5-13-1-determining-the-need",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.13.1. Determining the need",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s440-16-5-13-1-determining-the-need.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.5.13.1. Determining the need\n\nTo determine whether or not an existing manifest from the ingredient’s C2PA Manifest Store needs to be copied into the asset’s C2PA Manifest Store, the claim generator shall:\n\n1.  Validate the ingredient per the process described in [Section 16.5.13.4, “Ingredient validation”](#_ingredient_validation). In case of validation failures, the claim generator may skip the rest of these steps if directed to do so (for example, via user input or via configuration).\n    \n2.  For each manifest in the ingredient’s C2PA Manifest Store, compare its [URN identifier](#_",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out the procedure a claim generator shall follow to decide whether to copy each manifest from an ingredient's Manifest Store: validate the ingredient (optionally stopping on failure if so directed), compare manifest URNs with those already in the asset's store, and on a URN match compare manifest box hashes, not copying when they match. When hashes differ only because of redaction it keeps the existing manifest, replaces it, or redacts it to the union of both redaction sets depending on where redactions were applied, and in all other cases it copies the ingredient's manifest, re-labelled with a new URN.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s441-16-5-13-2-examples",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.13.2. Examples",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s441-16-5-13-2-examples.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.5.13.2. Examples\n\n**EXAMPLE:** Consider a claim generator `D` that is importing ingredients. It begins by importing ingredient `B`, which itself has an ingredient Manifest `A`. After validating both manifests, claim generator `D` copies Manifests `B` and `A` into Asset `D` 's C2PA Manifest Store. Then it imports ingredient `C`, which also includes a redacted version of Manifest `A`. After validating Manifest `C` and the redacted Manifest `A`, it compares the hashes of both versions of Manifest `A`. Knowing that the version of Manifest `A` in ingredient `C` was redacted, claim generato",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives two examples of manifest copying in which claim generator D imports ingredient B (carrying manifest A) and then ingredient C carrying a redacted manifest A, which D uses to overwrite its copy of A. In the second, the version of A from C fails validation, so D copies it under a new URN instead, with a note that non-manifest JUMBF boxes need not be copied.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s442-16-5-13-3-adding-manifest-references-to-the-ingr",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.13.3. Adding manifest references to the ingredient assertion",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s442-16-5-13-3-adding-manifest-references-to-the-ingr.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.5.13.3. Adding manifest references to the ingredient assertion\n\nIf the active manifest of the ingredient has been copied into the asset’s C2PA Manifest Store, then a [URI reference](#_uri_references) to the ingredient’s active [C2PA Manifest box](#_serialization) shall be stored as the value of the `activeManifest` field in the ingredient assertion, and an additional [URI reference](#_uri_references) to the active Manifest’s [C2PA Claim Signature box](#_serialization) shall be stored as the value of `claimSignature`.\n\nFor a C2PA Manifest present in the C2PA Manifest Store, ``hashed_ur",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires that when an ingredient's active manifest has been copied into the asset's store, hashed_uri references to its manifest box and claim signature box be stored in the ingredient assertion's activeManifest and claimSignature fields. An ingredient added without a manifest may instead carry a digitalSourceType drawn from the values allowed for actions, an ingredient assertion shall not contain both activeManifest and digitalSourceType, and an example shows a componentOf ingredient marked as trained algorithmic media.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s443-16-5-13-4-ingredient-validation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.13.4. Ingredient validation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s443-16-5-13-4-ingredient-validation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.5.13.4. Ingredient validation\n\n<a id=\"_general_15\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Heading that opens Section 16.5.13.4, Ingredient validation; the block holds no text beyond the heading.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s444-16-5-13-4-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.13.4.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s444-16-5-13-4-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.5.13.4.1. General\n\nIn addition, when the ingredient assertion references a C2PA Manifest, the claim generator shall also act as a validator, performing validation of the ingredient as described in [validation steps](#_validation_process). The result of that validation - all [success codes](#_success_codes), [informational codes](#_informational_codes), and [failure codes](#_failure_codes) - shall be used in populating the ingredient assertion’s `validationResults` or `validationStatus` field as described below. This field is required to be present so that it can be used in future val",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires the claim generator, when an ingredient assertion references a C2PA Manifest, to validate the ingredient and record all success, informational and failure codes in validationResults or validationStatus for use in future validations. A recorded failure is treated as an explicit statement that an actor knowingly chose to proceed despite errors, and claim generators are advised to raise warnings prominently.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s445-16-5-13-4-2-v2-ingredient-assertions-deprecated",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.13.4.2. V2 ingredient assertions (DEPRECATED)",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s445-16-5-13-4-2-v2-ingredient-assertions-deprecated.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.5.13.4.2. V2 ingredient assertions (DEPRECATED)\n\nIn a v2 ingredient assertion with no `c2pa_manifest` field, the `validationStatus` field is optional, but if present may contain an empty array.\n\nIn a v2 ingredient assertion with `c2pa_manifest` field, each object in the `validationStatus` array consists of a `code` field whose value describes the validation status of a specific part of the manifest along with an optional `success` field whose boolean value indicates whether the code reflects success (true) or failure (false). An optional description of the validation status may be pr",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes validationStatus in deprecated v2 ingredient assertions, optional and possibly empty without c2pa_manifest, and otherwise an array of status-map objects each with a code, an optional success boolean, an optional explanation and a url that should point to the failing claim, signature or assertion. Custom status codes are permitted but shall follow entity-specific namespace syntax and include a success boolean.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s446-16-5-13-4-3-v3-ingredient-assertions",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.13.4.3. V3 ingredient assertions",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s446-16-5-13-4-3-v3-ingredient-assertions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.5.13.4.3. V3 ingredient assertions\n\nIn a v3 ingredient assertion with an `activeManifest` field, the `validationResults` field shall be present. It may also be present when an `activeManifest` field is not present — for example, to record that the claim generator was unable to establish the ingredient’s active manifest at all, such as a remote manifest that could not be retrieved (see [Section 14.5.3.1, “By Reference”](#_by_reference)).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The ability for `validationResults` to exist without an `activeManifest` field is a change from previous versions.\n\nWhen present, the",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Requires a v3 ingredient assertion with activeManifest to carry validationResults, which may also appear without it, for example when a remote manifest could not be retrieved, and which shall hold full results for the ingredient's active manifest plus ingredientDeltas giving, for each manifest-bearing ingredient assertion in the ingredient's store, its ingredientAssertionURI and validationDeltas omitting statuses already recorded (compared on type, code and url). Each status-map shall contain a code and may contain a url and explanation, custom codes shall follow entity-specific namespace syntax, and a worked example and a manifest.inaccessible example illustrate usage. The results map may also carry a SemVer specVersion and either the deprecated trustListUri or trustListUris, whose objects shall each give the uri and type (such as c2pa.trustList or c2pa.tsaTrustList) of a trust list where a trust anchor matched, with an optional identifier that for ETSI-formatted lists shall be the list's sequence number.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s447-16-5-14-ingredient-metadata",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.5.14. Ingredient Metadata",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s447-16-5-14-ingredient-metadata.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### 16.5.14. Ingredient Metadata\n\nAs described in [assertion metadata](#_metadata_about_assertions), the `metadata` field of the ingredient assertion may contain metadata about the ingredient, such as the date and time when it was generated or other data that may help Manifest Consumers to make informed decisions about the provenance or veracity of the assertion data.\n\nOne common use for the `metadata` field is when only a portion of an ingredient is used in the creation or editing of an asset. In such cases, the `metadata` field should contain a `regionOfInterest` field (as described in [Sec",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that an ingredient assertion's metadata field may carry information such as generation time to help Manifest Consumers judge provenance. When only part of an ingredient is used, metadata should include a regionOfInterest describing the parts used, as an example with temporal and track regions shows.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
