    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s461-16-6-3-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.3.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s461-16-6-3-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.3.1. Description\n\nThe asset type assertion provides a way to more completely describe an asset, specifically additional context on how to parse or otherwise process it. This assertion allows for specifying an IANA Media Type value and/or additional type information, since many assets have formats that cannot be completely described by a single Media Type value.\n\nThe asset type assertion shall have a label of `c2pa.asset-type.v2`. There shall be at most one asset type assertion in a C2PA Manifest.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Earlier versions of this specification documented a `c2pa.asset-type` as",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The asset type assertion, labelled c2pa.asset-type.v2 and limited to one per manifest, gives extra context on how to parse or process an asset beyond a single Media Type, and replaces the deprecated c2pa.asset-type assertion. Its optional dc:format field holds the IANA Media Type, and its optional types field is an array of asset-type-map entries whose type value comes from the asset type or model type tables or an entity-specific namespace, with an optional version. Table 7 lists asset type values such as c2pa.types.dataset, c2pa.types.generator and serialization formats, and Table 8 lists AI/ML model type values from c2pa.types.model.caffe to c2pa.types.model.xgboost.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s462-16-6-3-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.3.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s462-16-6-3-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.3.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `asset-types` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.6, “Asset Type”](#cddl_annex_asset_type) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; The asset type assertion provides a way to describe the type or format of an\n; asset, specifically additional context on how to parse or otherwise process\n; it. It can also be used to describe externally referenced or related assets\n; such as AI/ML models.\n\nasset-type-map = {\n  \"type\": $asset-type-choice, ; one of the l",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines the asset-types map, with optional dc:format, a types array of asset-type-map entries (each a type choice plus an optional SemVer version) and optional metadata. A CBOR example describes a TensorFlow 2.11.0 model stored in the SavedModel format.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s463-16-6-3-3-details-on-selection-of-a-value-for-typ",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.3.3. Details on selection of a value for `type`",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s463-16-6-3-3-details-on-selection-of-a-value-for-typ.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.3.3. Details on selection of a value for `type`\n\nIf an asset’s exact type is specified in the [IANA registry application type](https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml#application) or [IANA registry text type](https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml#text), including JSON, CSV, and XML types, this information should be included in the asset type assertion `dc:format` field.\n\nFor example, if the asset is a CSV formatted text file, the `dc:format` field would be `text/csv`.\n\nAn asset type assertion may contain both a Dublin Core format and a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "When an asset's exact type is in the IANA application or text registries it should be recorded in dc:format, and an asset type assertion may combine a Dublin Core format with a C2PA standard or custom type. Table 9 lists common dc:format values such as application/json and text/csv, IANA structured suffixes like +json are also supported, and Table 10 adds two non-IANA formats, application/x-hdf5 and application/x-7z-compressed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
