      "content": "##### 16.6.4.1. Description\n\nA Font Information assertion is used to ensure that basic font metadata, such as the name, format, creator attribution, and licensing, are added to the asset in a manner which may be validated cryptographically.\n\nA Font Information assertion shall have a label of `font.info`, and there shall be at most one Font Information assertion per manifest.\n\n<a id=\"_schema_and_example_15\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The Font Information assertion, labelled font.info with at most one per manifest, adds basic font metadata such as name, format, creator attribution and licensing so it can be validated cryptographically.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s466-16-6-4-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.4.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s466-16-6-4-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.4.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `font-info-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.18, “Font Information”](#cddl_annex_font_info) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; Assertion data for font.info assertion.\nfont-info-map = {\n  \"fullName\": tstr, ; The full name of the font.\n  ; A version in the semantic versioning (semver) format.\n  ? \"version\": semver-string, ; The version of the font in SemVer format.\n\n  ; A URL to the release notes associated with this version of the font.",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines font-info-map, with required fields fullName, familyName, style, weight, postScriptName (restricted to a printable ASCII pattern), format (TrueType or OpenType) and copyrightNotice, plus optional version, versionUrl, releaseDate, copyrightHolder, copyrightYears, designers, designFoundry, sourceFoundry and identifier. Supporting rules define the allowed styles, a weight map with a class name and a value from 1 to 1000, an entity map with name and URL, and a designer map with person, foundry, contribution and start and end dates. Two CBOR examples follow, a basic one and an extended one showing the optional fields.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
