        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.5.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s468-16-6-5-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.5.1. Description\n\nA depthmap assertion provides a 3D description of the scene being captured by a camera. A depthmap assertion may contain a pre-computed [depth map](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Depth_map), or data which can later be used to compute a depth map by downstream ingestion or viewing software (e.g., left/right stereo images).\n\nAll depthmap assertions shall have a label that starts with `c2pa.depthmap` and be followed by a third section that identifies the type of depth map.\n\nC2PA depthmap assertions shall be captured optically, not inferred from a single 2D image via, f",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A depthmap assertion gives a 3D description of a captured scene, either as a pre-computed depth map or as data such as stereo images from which one can be computed; its label shall start with c2pa.depthmap followed by a part naming the depth map type, and the depth data shall be captured optically rather than inferred from a single 2D image.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s469-16-6-5-2-gdepth-depthmap",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.5.2. GDepth Depthmap",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s469-16-6-5-2-gdepth-depthmap.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.5.2. GDepth Depthmap\n\nA GDepth depth map assertion leverages the well-established [GDepth format](https://developers.google.com/depthmap-metadata/reference) to encode a pre-computed depth map.\n\nA GDepth depthmap assertion shall have a label of `c2pa.depthmap.GDepth`.\n\nThe schema for the data stored in this assertion shall always mirror the schema at [https://developers.google.com/depthmap-metadata/reference](https://developers.google.com/depthmap-metadata/reference).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> There are no concerns with splitting up the GDepth data when it grows beyond 64KB, as that limit exist",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The GDepth depthmap assertion, labelled c2pa.depthmap.GDepth, encodes a pre-computed depth map using the GDepth format, and its data schema shall always mirror the published GDepth schema, with a note that splitting data beyond 64KB is not a concern.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s470-16-6-5-3-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.5.3. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s470-16-6-5-3-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.5.3. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `depthmap-gdepth-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.16, “Depth Map (GDepth)”](#cddl_annex_depthmap_gdepth) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; Assertion that encodes a GDepth-formatted 3D depth map of the captured scene\ndepthmap-gdepth-map = {\n  ; The format that describes how to convert the depthmap data into a valid\n  ; float-point depthmap. Current valid values are 'RangeInverse' and\n  ; 'RangeLinear'\n  \"GDepth:Format\": format-type,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines depthmap-gdepth-map, with GDepth fields for format (RangeInverse or RangeLinear), near and far values, MIME type and base64 depth data, plus optional units, measure type, confidence image, device manufacturer, model, software and original image width and height. A CBOR example is given, and the block states that GDepth:Format, GDepth:Near, GDepth:Far, GDepth:Mime and GDepth:Data shall be present in every GDepth assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
