    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s472-16-6-6-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.6.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s472-16-6-6-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.6.1. Description\n\nIn previous versions of this specification, a concept of a data box as a special type of JUMBF box was used as a way to enable the arbitrary embedding of data into a C2PA Manifest, such as for thumbnails, icons and `inputTo` ingredients. It was determined that doing this via a new type of box introduced unnecessary complexities and missing functionality - such as the inability to redact data boxes. Accordingly, that concept has been deprecated in favor of a standard assertion which uses a standard JUMBF Embedded File content type box to contain the data.\n\nAn embedd",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The embedded data assertion replaces the deprecated data box concept, which could not be redacted, with a standard assertion holding data in a JUMBF Embedded File box; its label shall start with c2pa.embedded-data, and some other assertions such as c2pa.thumbnail.claim are technically equivalent under their own labels.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s473-16-6-6-2-technical-details",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.6.2. Technical Details",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s473-16-6-6-2-technical-details.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.6.2. Technical Details\n\nSince the embedded data assertion is based on a JUMBF Embedded File content type box, it’s Embedded File Description box shall contain an IANA media type (e.g., `image/png`) as the value of the _MEDIA TYPE_ field, and may contain a file name as the value of the _FILE NAME_ field. It shall not have the `External` toggle bit set.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> IANA structured suffixes ([https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-type-structured-suffix/media-type-structured-suffix.xhtml](https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-type-structured-suffix/media-type-structured-suffix.xhtm",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The Embedded File Description box of an embedded data assertion shall carry an IANA media type (structured suffixes allowed) and may carry a file name, shall not set the External bit, and its Binary Data box shall hold file bytes matching that media type.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
