    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s475-16-6-7-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.7.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s475-16-6-7-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.7.1. Description\n\nA cloud data assertion references a remotely-stored C2PA assertion packaged as JUMBF.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> For other externally stored data, whether assertion or non-assertion, see the [external reference](#external_reference_assertion) assertion.\n\nFor privacy and reliability reasons, data referenced through a cloud data assertion shall be considered optional: their contents should not be retrieved as part of manifest validation. A validator may retrieve the contents later to serve an application-dependent need, such as further exploration of the provenance history. The",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The cloud data assertion, labelled c2pa.cloud-data, references a remotely stored C2PA assertion packaged as JUMBF (media type always application/jumbf) through a hashed URI, so the remote data must be static, and its contents shall be treated as optional and should not be fetched during manifest validation. It shall not refer to actions, hashing, ingredient or other cloud data assertions (a list of labels is given), and its size field shall give the referenced data's size while the size and dc:format fields of the hashed external URI map shall be omitted.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s476-16-6-7-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.7.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s476-16-6-7-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.7.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `cloud-data-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.9, “Cloud Data”](#cddl_annex_cloud_data) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; Assertion that references the actual assertion stored in the cloud\ncloud-data-map = {\n  \"label\": tstr, ; label for the cloud-based assertion (eg.c2pa.actions)\n  \"size\": size-type, ; Number of bytes of data\n\n  ; http(s) URL to where the cloud-hosted assertion can be found\n  \"location\": $hashed-ext-uri-map,\n\n  ; media/",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines cloud-data-map with a label, a size of at least 1, a hashed external URI location, an optional content_type and optional metadata, followed by a CBOR example pointing to a remote c2pa.metadata assertion.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s477-16-6-8-metadata",
