    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s478-16-6-8-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.8.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s478-16-6-8-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.8.1. Description\n\nIn earlier versions of this specification, there were individual assertions for each metadata standard (e.g., IPTC, EXIF). In this version, there now exists a category of assertions that shall be used to represent metadata, in a standardized serialization. Having the metadata in an assertion establishes that the metadata in that assertion is significant, because it has been explicitly included in the C2PA Manifest, and signed by a specific signer - thus enabling cryptographic validation and attribution of the data. In addition, by using a common serialization, it e",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Metadata is now represented by a category of assertions with a standardized serialization, replacing earlier per-standard assertions, so that included metadata is signed, attributable and processed consistently; these assertions may represent existing standards or private specifications.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s479-16-6-8-2-common-requirements",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.8.2. Common Requirements",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s479-16-6-8-2-common-requirements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.8.2. Common Requirements\n\nA metadata assertion shall have either a label which ends in the string `.metadata` or `.metadata.ingredient` and is preceded by either the standard `c2pa` identifier or any other provided that it conforms to the same syntax as [entity-specific namespaces](#_namespacing). For example, a `com.litware.metadata` assertion would be valid.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The `.metadata.ingredient` form supports [related assertions to ingredients](#ingredient_related_assertions).\n\nEach metadata assertion shall contain a single JSON content type box containing the [JSON-LD](https:",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A metadata assertion's label shall end in .metadata or .metadata.ingredient, preceded by c2pa or an entity-specific namespace (for example com.litware.metadata). Each shall hold a single JSON content box with a JSON-LD serialization that includes @context, and the recommended approach is to build an XMP Data Model representation and serialize it to JSON-LD.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s480-16-6-8-3-the-c2pa-metadata-assertion",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.8.3. The `c2pa.metadata` assertion",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s480-16-6-8-3-the-c2pa-metadata-assertion.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.8.3. The `c2pa.metadata` assertion\n\nThis specification defines one metadata assertion, whose label is `c2pa.metadata`, which is used to represent a subset of common metadata schemas that may be used in any C2PA Manifest. Claim generators shall include in this assertion only the specific metadata fields enumerated in [Appendix C, _Implementation Details for `c2pa.metadata`_](#metadata_annex).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Custom labelled metadata assertions can contain any values from any schemas.\n\nExample 15. `c2pa.metadata` assertion for an image\n\nAn example of an `c2pa.metadata` assertion for an",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The block defines the c2pa.metadata assertion for a subset of common metadata schemas and requires claim generators to include only the fields enumerated in Appendix C, while custom-labelled metadata assertions may hold any values. JSON-LD examples show the assertion for an image (Exif, TIFF, IPTC and Photoshop fields including GPS data) and for a PDF.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s481-16-6-8-4-redaction-of-c2pa-metadata",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.6.8.4. Redaction of `c2pa.metadata`",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s481-16-6-8-4-redaction-of-c2pa-metadata.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.6.8.4. Redaction of `c2pa.metadata`\n\nAlthough the redaction process works in such a way that only an entire assertion could be redacted (see [Section 8.8, “Redaction of Assertions”](#_redaction_of_assertions)), the use of an [update manifest](#_update_manifests) enables partial redaction by removing the original and then placing the new, reduced, versions in the update manifest. This new assertion would be presented in a user experience in association with the signer of the update manifest and not with the signer of the C2PA Manifest that has been redacted.\n\nFor example, a metadata as",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Although redaction removes only whole assertions, an update manifest allows partial redaction of c2pa.metadata by removing the original and adding a reduced version, which is then attributed to the update manifest's signer, for example keeping camera information while dropping location data.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
