    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s488-16-7-2-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.7.2.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s488-16-7-2-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.7.2.1. Description\n\nIn some provenance workflows, a standard or update manifest is created offline, where it is not possible to obtain a trusted time stamp (as per [RFC 3161](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3161)) from a TSA at the time of signing. However, in such cases those signing certificates will expire after a certain period of time, thus leading to an invalid C2PA Manifest.\n\nTo prevent that expiration, a trusted time stamp can be added at a later point in time (provided the certificate has not yet expired) providing for a \"proof of existence\" for that C2PA Manifest and (in t",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The time stamp assertion lets a trusted RFC 3161 time stamp be added later to a manifest created offline, before its signing certificate expires, giving proof of existence for the manifest and, for the active manifest, its asset.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s489-16-7-2-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.7.2.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s489-16-7-2-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.7.2.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `time-stamp-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.6.3, “Time Stamp”](#cddl_annex_time_stamp) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; The data structures used to store an array of\n; manifest URNs to time stamp \"blobs\"\n$time-stamp-map /= {\n  * $time-stamp-entry => bstr\n}\n\n$time-stamp-entry /= tstr .regexp \"^urn:c2pa:[\\\\da-zA-Z_-]+$\"\n```\n\nAn example in CBOR diagnostic notation ([RFC 8949](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949), clause 8) is shown be",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines time-stamp-map as a map from C2PA manifest URNs to time stamp byte strings, with a CBOR example.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s490-16-7-2-3-requirements",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.7.2.3. Requirements",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s490-16-7-2-3-requirements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.7.2.3. Requirements\n\nA time stamp assertion shall have a label of `c2pa.time-stamp`, and there shall be at most one time stamp assertion per C2PA Manifest.\n\nThe time stamp assertion consists of a CBOR map (defined as a `time-stamp-map`) which shall contain at least one key-value pair (defined as a `time-stamp-entry`). The key shall be the label of the C2PA Manifest receiving the time stamp, and the value shall be a CBOR byte string whose contents are described in the following paragraph.\n\nThe value for each `time-stamp-entry` shall be the same binary data found in the `timeStampToken`",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A time stamp assertion shall be labelled c2pa.time-stamp, appear at most once per manifest, and contain at least one entry keyed by the label of the manifest being time-stamped. Each value shall be the timeStampToken from an RFC 3161 TSA response obtained in detached mode by the usual process, except that the payload is the signature field of the target manifest's COSE_Sign1_Tagged claim signature.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
