      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.7.3.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s492-16-7-3-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.7.3.1. Description\n\nThis assertion provides the session keys that are used, as part of a live media workflow based on the \"[Section 15.5, “Verifiable Segment Info method”](#verifiable_segment_info)\", to sign the `verifiable-segment-info-map`. Live media workflows that rely solely on the \"[Section 15.4, “Per-segment C2PA Manifest Box method”](#using_c2pa_manifest_box)\" are not required to use this assertion.\n\n<a id=\"_requirements_4\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The session keys assertion provides the keys used to sign the verifiable-segment-info-map in live media workflows based on the Verifiable Segment Info method, and is not required for workflows that rely only on the per-segment C2PA Manifest Box method.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s493-16-7-3-2-requirements",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.7.3.2. Requirements",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s493-16-7-3-2-requirements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.7.3.2. Requirements\n\nA session keys assertion shall have a label of `c2pa.session-keys`, and a C2PA Manifest may contain at most one session keys assertion.\n\nThe session keys assertion consists of a CBOR map (defined as a `session-keys-data`) and shall contain the following fields:\n\n`keys`\n\nAn array of one or more session key objects.\n\nEach session key in the `keys` array is represented as an object containing the following fields:\n\n`key`\n\nA COSE key that shall include a `kid` (key identifier) to ensure that the keys can be uniquely identified.\n\n`minSequenceNumber`\n\nAn unsigned intege",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A session keys assertion shall be labelled c2pa.session-keys, at most one per manifest, and holds a keys array whose entries contain a COSE key with a kid, minSequenceNumber, createdAt, validityPeriod and a signerBinding signature over the signer's end-entity certificate. Keys shall be used only within their validity period, and new keys supplied in a later manifest may overlap earlier ones but their minSequenceNumber shall be at least the current sequence number, supporting key rotation and preventing replay.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s494-16-7-3-3-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.7.3.3. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s494-16-7-3-3-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.7.3.3. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `session-keys-data` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.6.2, “Session Keys”](#cddl_annex_session_keys) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; Data structure to supply session keys used for live-media validation\nsession-keys-data = {\n    \"keys\" => [1* session-key], ; one or more session keys\n}\n\nsession-key = {\n    ; session key used to sign the `verifiable-segment-info-map`, note:\n    ; semantics need to require kid in COSE_Key\n    \"key\" => COSE_Key,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines session-keys-data as an array of one or more session-key maps, each with a COSE key, minSequenceNumber, createdAt timestamp, validityPeriod in seconds and a COSE_Sign1_Tagged signerBinding. A CBOR example shows a c2pa.session-keys assertion with two P-256 keys.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
