        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.8.1.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s497-16-8-1-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.8.1.1. Description\n\nThe environmental sustainability assertion is used to convey machine-generated sustainability data associated with the creation or modification of an asset. The information carried by this assertion is intended to support transparency and auditing of environmental costs (for example, energy consumption, greenhouse gas emissions, and water use) across a content supply chain, including workflows that use Generative AI.\n\nA C2PA Manifest may contain one or more environmental sustainability assertions. Each environmental sustainability assertion describes a set of susta",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The c2pa.environmental-sustainability assertion conveys machine-generated data on the environmental costs of creating or modifying an asset, a manifest may hold several, and their data may be aggregated, including recursively across ingredients. An action may reference one through relatedAssertions, and any such reference shall be a hashed JUMBF URI to an assertion in the same manifest. The optional energy_kwh, carbon_kgco2e (gross emissions, excluding offsets) and water_litres fields shall each hold a non-negative value in their named unit, and any measurementMethod shall be a reverse-DNS namespaced custom value.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
