    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s500-16-8-2-1-summary",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.8.2.1. Summary",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s500-16-8-2-1-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.8.2.1. Summary\n\nAs part of an ongoing effort to enhance AI transparency and accountability, a new AI Disclosure assertion is introduced to provide a means for a Claim Generator to provide machine-readable AI transparency information. This assertion enables verifiable AI transparency, automated compliance verification, and trustworthy AI content at scale.\n\n<a id=\"_details_3\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The AI Disclosure assertion is introduced so claim generators can provide machine-readable, verifiable AI transparency information supporting automated compliance checks.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s501-16-8-2-2-details",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.8.2.2. Details",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s501-16-8-2-2-details.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.8.2.2. Details\n\nThe AI Disclosure assertion shall have a label of `c2pa.ai-disclosure`.\n\nThe value of the `modelType` field is an enumeration of AI model types defined in [Table 8, “Model type values”](#model-types) and it shall be present in the `ai-model-disclosure-map` object. If present, the value of the `scientificDomain` field shall conform to the [arXiv taxonomy](https://arxiv.org/category_taxonomy), e.g., \"cs.AI\", \"physics.optics\". All other fields are optional, but if present, they shall conform to the types specified in the CDDL schema defined below.\n\n<a id=\"_relationship_be",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The AI Disclosure assertion shall be labelled c2pa.ai-disclosure and shall include modelType from the model type table, any scientificDomain shall follow the arXiv taxonomy, and other optional fields shall conform to the CDDL types.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s502-16-8-2-3-relationship-between-digitalsourcetype-",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.8.2.3. Relationship Between `digitalSourceType` and `humanOversightLevel`",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s502-16-8-2-3-relationship-between-digitalsourcetype-.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.8.2.3. Relationship Between `digitalSourceType` and `humanOversightLevel`\n\nThe `c2pa.ai-disclosure` assertion is designed to complement existing C2PA signals rather than replace them. In particular, `c2pa.actions` and `digitalSourceType` already provide a strong foundation for recording how an asset was created or modified. What this assertion introduces are three critical provenance primitives not previously captured in the ecosystem: model provenance — full disclosure of the AI models used for maximum transparency; scientific routing metadata — surfacing the discipline and sensitivi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The c2pa.ai-disclosure assertion complements c2pa.actions and digitalSourceType by adding model provenance, scientific domain metadata and a human oversight level. A table shows how digitalSourceType and humanOversightLevel combine, from fully autonomous AI generation to human-validated composites, and notes the assertion is not attached for digitalCreation with no trained model.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s503-16-8-2-4-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.8.2.4. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s503-16-8-2-4-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.8.2.4. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `ai-model-disclosure-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.5.14, “AI Disclosure”](#cddl_annex_ai_disclosure) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; CDDL Schema for AI Model Disclosure Metadata\nai-model-disclosure-map = {\n  \"modelType\": $model-type-choice, ; this is an enumeration of AI model types\n  ? \"modelName\": tstr, ; human-readable name of the AI model used\n\n  ; unique identifier of the AI model used (e.g., a URI, PURL, etc.)\n  ? \"modelIdent",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines ai-model-disclosure-map with a required modelType, optional modelName, modelIdentifier, scientificDomain list and metadata, and a contentProfile holding humanOversightLevel with the values fully_autonomous, prompt_guided or human_validated; further fields are listed as pending. A CBOR example discloses a Hugging Face Transformers model, though its caption describes a TensorFlow model, which does not match the example shown.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s504-16-9-assertion-supporting-structures",
