    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s506-16-9-1-1-description",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.1. Description",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s506-16-9-1-1-description.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.1. Description\n\nIn many cases, it is useful or even necessary to provide additional information about an assertion, such as the date and time when it was generated or other data that may help Manifest Consumers to make informed decisions about the provenance or veracity of the assertion data.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> A Manifest Consumer is not required to read any portion of assertion metadata. It can choose which, if any, fields it wishes to consume, perhaps even varying based on the assertion type to which it is applied.\n\n<a id=\"_custom_values\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Assertion metadata provides additional information about an assertion, such as when it was generated, to help Manifest Consumers judge its provenance, and consumers are not required to read any of it.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s507-16-9-1-2-custom-values",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.2. Custom Values",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s507-16-9-1-2-custom-values.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.2. Custom Values\n\nThe assertion metadata structure may include custom key/value pairs, in addition to the standard fields defined below. Such custom map keys shall be namespaced using the same [entity-specific namespaces](#_namespacing) approach as described in [Section 8.2.1, “Namespacing”](#_namespacing). This ensures that there are no collisions between different organizations adding their own custom data.\n\n<a id=\"_schema_and_example_23\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The assertion metadata structure may include custom key/value pairs, whose keys shall use entity-specific namespaces to avoid collisions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s508-16-9-1-3-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.3. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s508-16-9-1-3-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.3. Schema and Example\n\nBelow shows the core schemas used inside other assertions.\n\nThe [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) for the `assertion-metadata-map` rule is in the following listing (see [Section G.7.1, “Assertion Metadata Common Types”](#cddl_annex_assertion_metadata_common) for the complete normative schema):\n\nCDDL for Assertion Metadata\n\n```cddl\n; Describes additional information about an assertion, including a hashed-uri\n; reference to it. We use a socket/plug here to allow hashed-uri-map to be used\n; in individual files without having the map defi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines the assertion-metadata-map with optional dateTime, reviewRatings, reference, the deprecated dataSource (which claim generators shall not include), localizations, regionOfInterest, processStart, processEnd and custom fields. Supporting rules define bounded time maps with absolute, lowerBound or upperBound types, a source-map with a type and details, a rating-map with a value from 1 to 5, a code and explanation, and localization entries, followed by a CBOR example. Assertion metadata usually sits in another assertion's metadata field but can be stored separately in an assertion labelled c2pa.assertion.metadata, for example for non-JSON or non-CBOR assertions such as thumbnails.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s509-16-9-1-4-datetime",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.4. DateTime",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s509-16-9-1-4-datetime.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.4. DateTime\n\nIf a `dateTime` field is present, its value shall be a date time string that complies with CBOR date/times ([RFC 8949](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949), 3.4.1). This field is used to indicate the date and time when the assertion was generated.\n\n<a id=\"_region_of_interest\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "If present, dateTime shall be a CBOR-compliant date time string indicating when the assertion was generated.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s510-16-9-1-5-region-of-interest",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.5. Region of Interest",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s510-16-9-1-5-region-of-interest.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.5. Region of Interest\n\nThe assertion may be specific to only a portion of an asset - such as a range of frames in a video or a specific area on an image. Such a portion may be identified using a `regionOfInterest` field, whose value is a `region-map` object (as defined in [Section 16.9.2, “Regions of Interest”](#_regions_of_interest)).\n\n<a id=\"_data_source\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "An assertion that applies to only part of an asset, such as a range of video frames or an image area, may identify that part with a regionOfInterest field holding a region-map object.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s511-16-9-1-6-data-source",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.6. Data Source",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s511-16-9-1-6-data-source.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.6. Data Source\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The `dataSource` field is deprecated. See [Section H.1, “`dataSource` Field in Assertion Metadata”](#_datasource_field).\n\n<a id=\"_review_ratings\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Note stating that the dataSource field is deprecated, with a pointer to Section H.1.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s512-16-9-1-7-review-ratings",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.7. Review Ratings",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s512-16-9-1-7-review-ratings.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.7. Review Ratings\n\nWhen present, the `reviewRatings` array provides a place for the claim generator to provide one or more `rating` objects on the quality (or lack thereof) of an assertion. A `reviewRatings` shall not be present if a `dataSource` object is present with a `type` field whose value is either `humanEntry.anonymous` or `humanEntry.credentialed`.\n\nThe `value` field of the `rating` object shall be present with any integer value from _1_ (worst) through _5_ (best). If present, the `explanation` field shall contain a human-consumable string description of the type of ratin",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The optional reviewRatings array lets a claim generator attach one or more rating objects judging the quality of an assertion, and it shall not be present when a dataSource of type humanEntry.anonymous or humanEntry.credentialed is present. Each rating shall carry an integer value from 1 (worst) to 5 (best), with an optional human-readable explanation and an optional machine-readable code, drawn either from Table 11 (such as actions.unknownActionsPerformed, ingredient.notVisible or thumbnail.primaryMismatch) or from entity-specific namespaces.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s513-16-9-1-8-references",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.8. References",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s513-16-9-1-8-references.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.8. References\n\nBecause the `reference` field of the assertion metadata assertion is a standard [hashed\\_uri](#_uri_references), it is also possible to have an [assertion metadata assertion](#_metadata_about_assertions) refer to assertions in other manifests than the active one. For example, the active manifest may include an `assertion metadata` assertion that validates the `c2pa.metadata` assertion present in an ingredient’s manifest.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Since the claim is a special type of assertion, this same method can be used to refer to claims in other manifests.\n\n<a id=\"_process",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Because the reference field of an assertion metadata assertion is a standard hashed_uri, it can point to assertions, and likewise claims, in manifests other than the active one, such as a c2pa.metadata assertion in an ingredient's manifest.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s514-16-9-1-9-process-time",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.9. Process time",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s514-16-9-1-9-process-time.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.9. Process time\n\nThe optional `processStart` and `processEnd` fields describe the overall process represented by the enclosing assertion. As defined in [Section 8.9, “Specifications of time in assertions”](#_specifications_of_time_in_assertions), `processStart` shall use `generator-lower-bound-time-type`, and `processEnd` shall use `generator-upper-bound-time-type`.\n\nWhen both fields are present, the time value represented by `processStart` shall be less than or equal to the time value represented by `processEnd`.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The `processStart` and `processEnd` fields are claim",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The optional processStart and processEnd fields describe the time span of the overall process behind the enclosing assertion, using generator lower-bound and upper-bound time types respectively, with processStart required to be no later than processEnd; a note says these are claim-generator timestamps, not trusted ones.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s515-16-9-1-10-localization",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.10. Localization",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s515-16-9-1-10-localization.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### 16.9.1.10. Localization\n\n<a id=\"_general_17\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Heading that opens Section 16.9.1.10, Localization; the block holds no text beyond the heading.",
