    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s516-16-9-1-10-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "16.9.1.10.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s516-16-9-1-10-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### 16.9.1.10.1. General\n\nIt is important that consumers of C2PA manifests be able to understand the information in their native language, when possible. To this end, it is possible to add localization information for an assertion with a dictionary that is included in the assertion’s metadata.\n\n<a id=\"_localization_dictionary\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The general localization text explains that, so consumers can read manifest information in their own language, localization information for an assertion can be added as a dictionary in the assertion's metadata.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
