      "target": "../sections/s537-a-3-4-embedding-manifests-into-ttml.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.3.4. Embedding manifests into TTML\n\n[TTML2](https://www.w3.org/TR/ttml2/) (Timed Text Markup Language) is an XML-based format for timed text (subtitles and captions) defined by the W3C. This section applies only to standalone TTML files with the media type `application/ttml+xml`. When TTML is carried as a timed-text track inside a BMFF-based container (e.g., MP4 or IMF), the C2PA Manifest Store shall be embedded in the outer BMFF container as described in [Section A.5, “Embedding manifests into BMFF-based assets”](#_embedding_manifests_into_bmff_based_assets); the rules in this section",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "For standalone TTML files (application/ttml+xml) the C2PA Manifest Store shall be Base64-encoded in a c2pa:manifest element at /tt:tt/tt:head/tt:metadata/c2pa:manifest with the c2pa namespace declared on the root element, whereas TTML carried inside a BMFF container uses the BMFF embedding instead, and an external manifest is preferred where toolchains drop foreign-namespace elements. Implementations shall not treat this element as a conformance error even in constrained profiles such as IMSC or EBU-TT-D, and the claim generator shall include a c2pa.hash.data assertion whose single exclusion range covers the c2pa:manifest element from opening to closing tag.",
