      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.3.8. Embedding manifests into TIFF-based assets\n\nThe [DNG](https://helpx.adobe.com/content/dam/help/en/camera-raw/digital-negative/jcr_content/root/content/flex/items/position/position-par/download_section_733958301/download-1/DNG_Spec_1_7_1_0.pdf) format provides camera manufacturers to provide their camera raw formats in a standardized manner. DNG is based on which is based on [TIFF/EP](https://www.iso.org/standard/29377.html) (which is, itself, based on [TIFF v6](https://www.itu.int/itudoc/itu-t/com16/tiff-fx/docs/tiff6.pdf)). An Exif uncompressed file ([Exif](https://www.cipa.jp/std",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "For TIFF-based files, including Exif uncompressed, TIFF/EP, DNG and other TIFF-based RAW formats, the C2PA Manifest Store shall be embedded as the data of tag 52545 (0xCD41) with tag type 7, and the TIFF ByteOrder does not govern its endianness. There shall be only one store per asset, placed in the last IFD of the main chain (in the single main IFD or a new IFD after it, otherwise as the only entry in its IFD), and it should sit at the end of the file to support update manifests without disturbing other offsets.",
