      "content": "#### A.3.9. Embedding manifests into RIFF-based assets\n\nThe [RIFF](https://www.loc.gov/preservation/digital/formats/fdd/fdd000025.shtml) format provides a generic container format for storing data in tagged chunks. It is primarily used to store multimedia such as images, sound and video. It serves as the container format for [WAV](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WAV), [BWF, Broadcast Wave](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broadcast_Wave_Format), [AVI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audio_Video_Interleave) and [WebP](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebP).\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> RIFF is based on an older format",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "In RIFF-based files such as WAV, BWF, AVI and WebP, the C2PA Manifest Store shall be embedded as the data of a chunk with identifier C2PA that is the last sub-chunk of the first RIFF header chunk.",
        "state": "draft",
