      "target": "../sections/s558-a-3-14-embedding-manifests-into-parquet.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.3.14. Embedding manifests into Parquet\n\n[Apache Parquet File Format](https://parquet.apache.org/docs/file-format/) is a columnar storage format widely used for structured and semi-structured data, such as analytics and machine-learning datasets. A Parquet file consists of one or more row groups of column-chunk data followed by a footer containing a Thrift-encoded `FileMetaData` structure that describes the file’s schema, row groups, and an optional `key_value_metadata` list of arbitrary key/value pairs. The file ends with a 4-byte, little-endian length of the footer followed by the 4-by",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The section introduces Apache Parquet, describing its row groups and Thrift-encoded FileMetaData footer with optional key_value_metadata and trailing length and PAR1 magic number, and notes that manifests can only be embedded in non-encrypted Parquet files.",
