    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s561-a-3-14-3-writing-a-manifest-store",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.3.14.3. Writing a Manifest Store",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s561-a-3-14-3-writing-a-manifest-store.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.3.14.3. Writing a Manifest Store\n\nTo embed a C2PA Manifest Store:\n\n1.  Reserve a `c2pa:manifest` `KeyValue` entry in `key_value_metadata`, sized to hold the placeholder, Base64-encoded C2PA Manifest Store.\n    \n2.  Serialize the footer and compute the data hash over the complete file with the placeholder region excluded.\n    \n3.  Sign the manifest using the computed data hash.\n    \n4.  Replace the placeholder value with the Base64-encoded, signed manifest, keeping the same encoded byte length, and rewrite the footer.\n    \n    > **NOTE:**\n    > Because the encoded byte length of the val",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Writing a manifest into Parquet reserves a placeholder c2pa:manifest entry, hashes the file with the placeholder excluded, signs, and replaces the value with the same-length encoded manifest, so the footer length stays valid. Since Parquet libraries usually rewrite footers wholesale, claim generators should check that their writer preserves the entry's exact byte length and the order of key_value_metadata entries.",
        "state": "draft",
