      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.3.17.1. Applicability\n\nThis section applies to files that are written only by appending complete lines to the end of the file, and whose earlier bytes are never rewritten, specifically:\n\n*   Plain-text files with no structural record grammar, such as application logs and event logs (`text/plain`).\n    \n*   JSON Lines (JSONL) streams, in which each line of the file is an independent JSON value.\n    \n\nFormats with a defined record schema that cannot accommodate an additional record, such as `text/csv` and `text/tab-separated-values`, shall not use this method. Such formats shall use an [",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The method applies only to files written by appending complete lines and never rewriting earlier bytes, namely plain-text logs (text/plain) and JSON Lines streams; CSV and TSV shall instead use an external manifest, and structured text such as source code, configuration, Markdown and YAML shall use the structured text embedding method. A file with checkpoints shall not also carry a structured text manifest block, and the two methods are told apart by the sentinel delimiters (BEGIN C2PA CHECKPOINT versus BEGIN C2PA MANIFEST).",
        "state": "draft",
