      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.3.17.5.1. External URI form",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s576-a-3-17-5-1-external-uri-form.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### A.3.17.5.1. External URI form\n\nBefore writing, the claim generator shall choose the URI at which this checkpoint’s manifest will be stored. The URI need not resolve until after signing.\n\n1.  Record _S_ = the current byte offset of the end of the file (the start of the new segment, and the value of `segmentStart`).\n    \n2.  Append the new segment content to the file.\n    \n3.  Record _E_ = the current byte offset of the end of the file (the start of the sentinel, and the value of `segmentEnd`).\n    \n4.  If this is not the first checkpoint, record _P_ = the byte offset of the first byte of",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "To write a checkpoint with an external URI, the claim generator chooses the manifest URI in advance, records the segment start and end offsets, hashes the preceding sentinel line for predecessorSentinel if there is one, then appends the formatted sentinel line in a single write and records its length as sentinelLength. It then builds the c2pa.hash.segment assertion from these values and signs and stores the Manifest Store at the chosen URI, so the sentinel append is the only file write, which suits WORM and append-only storage.",
        "state": "draft",
