        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.3.17.5.2. Inline form",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s577-a-3-17-5-2-inline-form.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### A.3.17.5.2. Inline form\n\n1.  Record _S_ = the current byte offset of the end of the file (the start of the new segment, and the value of `segmentStart`).\n    \n2.  Append the new segment content to the file.\n    \n3.  Record _E_ = the current byte offset of the end of the file (the start of the sentinel, and the value of `segmentEnd`).\n    \n4.  If this is not the first checkpoint, record _P_ = the byte offset of the first byte of the preceding checkpoint’s sentinel line and _PL_ = the byte length of that line including its terminating line ending, then read the bytes `[P, P + PL)` and com",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The inline-form procedure records segment offsets and the predecessor sentinel hash as in the external form, but builds the c2pa.hash.segment assertion without a sentinelLength field (which shall not be present), signs the Manifest Store, and appends a sentinel embedding the Base64-encoded store in one write. Omitting sentinelLength removes the circular dependency between the manifest and the sentinel's length, keeping the procedure compatible with WORM and append-only storage.",
        "state": "draft",
