      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.4.2.1. Adding the Manifest to a PDF",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s585-a-4-2-1-adding-the-manifest-to-a-pdf.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.4.2.1. Adding the Manifest to a PDF\n\nWhen adding a C2PA Manifest to the entire PDF, the document catalog dictionary shall contain an `AF` entry. One of the entries in the array value of `AF` shall be an indirect reference to the embedded file specification consisting of the C2PA Manifest Store containing the active manifest. Only that C2PA Manifest Store shall be listed there; earlier C2PA Manifest Stores may remain embedded in the PDF consistent with [Special Considerations for PDF](#locating_active_manifest_pdf_special). That embedded file specification shall also be referenced, via",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "For a document-level manifest, the PDF catalog shall have an AF entry referencing only the embedded file specification holding the active manifest's store, also referenced from the EmbeddedFiles name tree or a FileAttachment annotation, with the annotation route required when a certifying signature exists so DocMDP restrictions are not broken. Because incremental updates allow multiple stores, the earliest store is the initial manifest and the latest the active one, and consumers shall process all manifests in all stores as if they were one store.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
