      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.4.2.2. Compatibility with PDF Signatures",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s586-a-4-2-2-compatibility-with-pdf-signatures.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.4.2.2. Compatibility with PDF Signatures\n\nIt is necessary to know, when adding a new C2PA Manifest Store, if a PDF signature (certifying or approval) will also be applied. Since the PDF signature will change the data of the PDF after the C2PA Manifest is signed, the size and location of the PDF signature dictionary’s `Contents` key shall be determined before C2PA signing. That range of bytes shall be added to the list of exclusions in the `c2pa.hash.data` assertion, so that the C2PA signature is not invalidated by the addition of the PDF signature. The PDF signature shall be over the e",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "When a PDF signature will also be applied, the size and location of its Contents key shall be fixed before C2PA signing and added as an exclusion in the c2pa.hash.data assertion, and the PDF signature shall cover the whole PDF including the Manifest Store.",
        "state": "draft",
