    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s590-a-5-1-the-uuid-box-for-c2pa",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.1. The `'uuid'` Box for C2PA",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s590-a-5-1-the-uuid-box-for-c2pa.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.5.1. The `'uuid'` Box for C2PA\n\nAll BMFF-based C2PA assets, whether they are timed (e.g., videos with or without audio tracks), untimed (e.g., still photos) or mixed (e.g., live or animated photos) audiovisual media, shall use a `'uuid'` box that adheres to the following syntax and semantics defined below.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The reason that a `'uuid'` box instead of a `'c2pa'` box is being used is that browsers based on Chromium will immediately fail playback when they encounter any unknown top-level boxes.\n\nSome file formats that are BMFF-based and would be supported via this method includ",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "All BMFF-based assets, timed, untimed or mixed, shall use a 'uuid' box for C2PA, chosen over a 'c2pa' box because Chromium-based browsers fail on unknown top-level boxes; supported formats include MP4, fragmented MP4, M4A, HEIF and AVIF.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s591-a-5-1-1-definition",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.1.1. Definition",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s591-a-5-1-1-definition.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.5.1.1. Definition\n\n```none\nBox Type: 'uuid'\nExtended Box Type: 0xD8, 0xFE, 0xC3, 0xD6, 0x1B, 0x0E, 0x48, 0x3C, 0x92, 0x97, 0x58, 0x28, 0x87, 0x7E, 0xC4, 0x81\nVersion: 0\nFlags: 0\nContainer: File\nMandatory: No\nQuantity: Zero or more\n```\n\nC2PA’s `'uuid'` box embeds provenance into BMFF. One such box contains a C2PA Manifest Store, and there may be one or more auxiliary boxes containing additional information required for validation.\n\n<a id=\"_syntax_2\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the box definition for the C2PA 'uuid' box (its extended type, version 0, file container, zero or more allowed) and notes that one such box holds the Manifest Store while auxiliary boxes may hold extra validation data.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
