    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s595-a-5-3-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.3.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s595-a-5-3-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.5.3.1. General\n\nSome files have one or more very large `'mdat'` boxes (e.g., large video or image files which may be downloaded and rendered progressively) or large numbers of independent `'mdat'` boxes (e.g., fMP4 where each fragment can be downloaded independently).\n\nIn these cases, it is unreasonable to require a client to completely download all `'mdat'` box(es) before validating any portion of the asset. Avoiding that necessity is resolved by using multiple hashes.\n\nFor each large `'mdat'` box, subsets of the box have individual hashes that can be validated independently; how to d",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that large or fragmented BMFF assets use multiple hashes so parts can be validated without downloading every 'mdat', and that Merkle trees (one per 'mdat' in non-fragmented files, one per track in fragmented ones) keep the manifest small, with the manifest storing one tree row and an auxiliary box per subset giving its leaf position and the extra hashes needed. The choice of row trades manifest size against auxiliary box size and is left to the implementation, but the BMFF Hash portion of the manifest shall include the merkle field.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s596-a-5-3-1-1-non-fragmented-asset-that-can-be-valid",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.3.1.1. Non-fragmented asset that can be validated piecewise",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s596-a-5-3-1-1-non-fragmented-asset-that-can-be-valid.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### A.5.3.1.1. Non-fragmented asset that can be validated piecewise\n\nIf the manifest contains a non-leaf row of the merkle tree, two or more `ContentProvenanceBox` with `box_purpose` set to `'merkle'` as described below shall be included in the file. They are not required to be included in the file if the manifest contains the leaf row of the merkle tree. If they exist, they shall follow the last `'mdat'` box in the file.\n\nThe hash used for a given leaf node in the merkle tree shall be computed from the subset of payload of the `'mdat'`. The `'mdat'` is divided into sizes defined by `'fixed",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "For a non-fragmented asset, two or more merkle boxes shall follow the last 'mdat' when the manifest holds a non-leaf row, with leaf hashes computed over 'mdat' payload subsets sized by fixedBlockSize or variableBlockSizes. The boxes shall follow subset order, be grouped contiguously per tree, and carry location values counting up from 0.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s597-a-5-3-1-2-fragmented-asset",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.3.1.2. Fragmented asset",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s597-a-5-3-1-2-fragmented-asset.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### A.5.3.1.2. Fragmented asset\n\nFor fMP4 assets which are split across multiple files:\n\n*   One `ContentProvenanceBox` box with `box_purpose` set to `'merkle'` as described below shall be included in each fragment file immediately preceding the `'moof'` box.\n    \n*   The hash used for a given leaf node in the Merkle tree shall be over all data in its containing single fragment file except data excluded by the exclusion list.\n    \n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This specification does not enable support for fMP4 assets which are split across multiple files where individual fragment files contain more than",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "For fMP4 split across files, one merkle box shall precede the 'moof' in each fragment file and each leaf hash covers the whole fragment file minus exclusions, while for a single flat fMP4 file a merkle box shall precede each 'moof' and each leaf hash covers that 'moof' up to the next one. Concatenating split files does not yield a compliant file, so producing both forms shall treat the first as a parentOf ingredient with a c2pa.repackaged action.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s598-a-5-3-1-3-live-media-fragmented-asset",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.3.1.3. Live media fragmented asset",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s598-a-5-3-1-3-live-media-fragmented-asset.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### A.5.3.1.3. Live media fragmented asset\n\nFor fMP4 assets which are live media transmissions, follow the instructions [here](#live-media).\n\nAs described [above](#exception-fmp4-manifest-init-seg), for fragmented MP4 (fMP4) streams that are live media transmissions in a 'push' streaming scenario (e.g., over-the-air broadcast television without a pull mechanism), the manifest box is only required to be included in a portion of initialization segments.\n\n<a id=\"_box_containing_the_merkle_auxiliary\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Points to the live media instructions for live fMP4 transmissions and restates that in push streaming the manifest box is required only in a portion of initialisation segments.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s599-a-5-3-1-4-box-containing-the-merkle-auxiliary",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.3.1.4. Box containing the merkle auxiliary",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s599-a-5-3-1-4-box-containing-the-merkle-auxiliary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### A.5.3.1.4. Box containing the merkle auxiliary\n\nRegardless of how the asset is structured, the fields in the corresponding box described above shall be set as follows.\n\nbox\\_purpose\n\nFor an auxiliary `'uuid'` C2PA box, this value shall be `merkle`.\n\ndata\n\nWhen `box_purpose` is `merkle`, this value shall contain raw CBOR bytes indicating how to validate a portion of the asset as defined as follows. If there are multiple auxiliary `'uuid'` C2PA boxes with `box_purpose` `merkle` for a given Merkle tree in a single file, each shall be followed by sufficient padding bytes (zero or more) to m",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "For auxiliary merkle boxes, box_purpose shall be merkle and the data shall be raw CBOR describing how to validate part of the asset, padded so that all such boxes for one Merkle tree in a file are a fixed size.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s600-a-5-3-1-5-regarding-unique-ids",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.3.1.5. Regarding unique IDs",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s600-a-5-3-1-5-regarding-unique-ids.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "###### A.5.3.1.5. Regarding unique IDs\n\nThere are cases, where the ID for a subset of the asset, such as the track\\_id field of the `'tkhd'` box, is only locally unique to a subset of the overall asset rather than globally unique to the asset.\n\nBecause a globally unique ID is needed to determine what to hash, a unique ID is included. This unique ID does not equal any value from the original asset; each value is instead defined when the manifest is created. The unique ID is then combined with an associated local ID to form an ID that’s globally unique to the entire asset.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> When th",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Because some IDs such as the 'tkhd' track_id are only locally unique, a unique ID defined at manifest creation is combined with the local ID to make a globally unique identifier. A note explains that fixed-size merkle boxes let a progressively downloading client compute the offset of the box it needs and fetch only that box.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s601-a-5-3-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.3.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s601-a-5-3-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.5.3.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `bmff-merkle-map` rule in the following [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) (see [Section G.4.3, “BMFF Merkle Hash”](#cddl_annex_bmff_merkle) for the complete normative schema):\n\n```cddl\n; The data structure used to store sufficient information to validate a single\n; 'mdat' box or\n; a portion of an 'mdat' box when a Merkle tree is used\",\nbmff-merkle-map = {\n  \"uniqueId\": int, ; A unique integer used to differentiate local ids\n  \"localId\": int, ; A local id indicating Merkle tree.\n\n  ; Zero-based",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for bmff-merkle-map, with fields uniqueId, localId, location (zero-based leaf index) and an optional hashes array of the additional hashes needed to reach the manifest's Merkle row, plus a CBOR example. For non-fragmented assets localId shall be the zero-based index of the 'mdat', and for fragmented assets it shall be the track_id of the relevant 'tkhd' box.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s602-a-5-4-dynamic-stream-generation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.4. Dynamic stream generation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s602-a-5-4-dynamic-stream-generation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.5.4. Dynamic stream generation\n\nMany adaptive bitrate streaming (ABR) implementations store a single version of an asset, e.g., as a flat MP4 or in another intermediate format, and generate individual asset streams using various codecs, bitrates, etc. at consumption time. As a result, such a server shall either hash said streams and create a C2PA Manifest each time the content is consumed or, if generation is deterministic, create and cache the hashes and C2PA Manifests once and then embed them at consumption time.\n\n<a id=\"_exclusion_list_requirements\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Servers that generate adaptive bitrate streams at consumption time shall either hash streams and create a manifest per consumption or, if generation is deterministic, cache the hashes and manifests and embed them on delivery.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s603-a-5-5-exclusion-list-requirements",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.5. Exclusion List Requirements",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s603-a-5-5-exclusion-list-requirements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.5.5. Exclusion List Requirements\n\nFor all `c2pa.hash.bmff.v2` (deprecated) and `c2pa.hash.bmff.v3` assertions, the entries in [Example 20, “Always excluded boxes”](#always-excluded-boxes) shall always appear on the exclusion list. Other entries are allowed but not required.\n\nThe entire `'uuid'` C2PA box shall be excluded. (The `'data'` field is ensuring that other `'uuid'` boxes are not excluded.)\n\nExample 20. Always excluded boxes\n\n```none\nxpath = \"/uuid\"\ndata = [ { offset = 8, data = b64'2P7D1hsOSDySl1goh37EgQ==' } ]\n```\n\nThe entire `'mfra'` box shall be excluded. The `'ftyp'` box sho",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "For c2pa.hash.bmff.v2 and v3 assertions, the whole C2PA 'uuid' box and the 'mfra' box shall always be excluded and 'ftyp' should not be, with earlier mandatory exclusions dropped as insecure. When both hash and merkle fields are present, an 'mdat' subset exclusion at offset 16 with length 0 shall also appear, and bytes beyond a box's end shall never be hashed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s604-a-5-6-timed-media-streams-that-are-neither-audio",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.6. Timed-media streams that are neither audio nor video",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s604-a-5-6-timed-media-streams-that-are-neither-audio.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.5.6. Timed-media streams that are neither audio nor video\n\nTimed-media streams that are neither audio nor video, such as text streams for captions, that the claim generator wishes to make tamper evident shall be handled the same way as audio and video streams.\n\n<a id=\"_external_references\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Non-audio, non-video timed-media streams, such as caption text, that are to be made tamper evident shall be handled like audio and video streams.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s605-a-5-7-external-references",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.7. External references",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s605-a-5-7-external-references.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.5.7. External references\n\nExternally referenced content declared inside BMFF boxes, such as in a `'dref'`, `'url'`, or `'urn'` box, that the claim generator wishes to make tamper evident shall **not** exclude the referencing box and shall include a separate [cloud data assertion](#_cloud_data) for each external reference to be hashed.\n\n<a id=\"_size_requirements\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Externally referenced content in BMFF boxes such as 'dref', 'url' or 'urn' that is to be tamper evident shall not have its referencing box excluded and shall have a separate cloud data assertion for each reference.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s606-a-5-8-size-requirements",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.5.8. Size requirements",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s606-a-5-8-size-requirements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.5.8. Size requirements\n\nIf a BMFF-based asset uses 32-bit sizes or offsets in any box(es), e.g. the `'stco'` box, and adding boxes to conform to this specification will push the file size over 4 gigabytes, it is the responsibility of the manifest creator to edit the file to use appropriate sizes and offsets, e.g. by replacing the `'stco'` box with a `'co64'` box, before creating the manifest.\n\n<a id=\"_embedding_manifests_into_zip_based_formats\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "If adding C2PA boxes pushes a BMFF file using 32-bit sizes or offsets past 4 gigabytes, the manifest creator is responsible for converting to suitable sizes and offsets, such as replacing 'stco' with 'co64', before creating the manifest.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s607-a-6-embedding-manifests-into-zip-based-formats",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
