      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.6.2.2. Hashing the ZIP Central Directory",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s611-a-6-2-2-hashing-the-zip-central-directory.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.6.2.2. Hashing the ZIP Central Directory\n\nAs described in 4.3.12 of the ZIP AppNote, the Central Directory is an array of central directory headers - one per entry in the ZIP archive. It is stored at the end of the ZIP archive and used to locate the entries in the ZIP archive and necessary information/metadata about them. It is immediately followed by the End of Central Directory record (ZIP AppNote, 4.3.16), which contains information about the ZIP archive itself.\n\nIn order to prevent tampering with the ZIP Central Directory, such as adding new entries or modifying information about t",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Each central directory header and the end of central directory record shall be hashed in sequence, skipping the crc-32 field of the manifest's header, with the result stored in zip_central_directory_hash of the collection-data-hash-map, whose CDDL (uris, alg and the optional central directory hash) is given. A two-pass approach shall be used, first writing a zero-filled content_credential.c2pa and hashing the central directory, then completing and writing the manifest, and that file shall be stored uncompressed, unencrypted and with a general purpose bit flag of 0.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s612-a-6-3-placement-of-the-manifest-store",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.6.3. Placement of the Manifest Store",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s612-a-6-3-placement-of-the-manifest-store.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.6.3. Placement of the Manifest Store\n\nThe C2PA Manifest Store shall be stored in the `META-INF` directory of the ZIP archive with a filename of `content_credential.c2pa` and a media type as recommended for [external manifests](#_external_manifests). The file shall be stored (compression method 0) and not encrypted.\n\nWhen the ZIP-based format is an Open Packaging Conventions (OPC) package, such as Office Open XML or OpenXPS, OPC requires every part of the package to have a content type declared in the package’s `[Content_Types].xml` part. A claim generator embedding a C2PA Manifest Store",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The Manifest Store shall be stored uncompressed and unencrypted as META-INF/content_credential.c2pa in the ZIP archive. In OPC packages such as Office Open XML and OpenXPS, the claim generator shall declare application/c2pa for it in [Content_Types].xml, through a Default or Override element, before computing the collection data hash.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
