    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s617-a-7-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.7.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s617-a-7-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.7.1. General\n\n[HTML](https://www.w3.org/TR/html/) supports two methods for associating a C2PA Manifest Store with a document: an embedded `script` element for inline manifests and a `link` element for referencing external manifests. Both use the IANA Media type `application/c2pa`. While this section describes both approaches, the use of an [external manifest](#_external_manifests) via the `link` element is preferred.\n\nThere shall be at most one C2PA Manifest Store association per HTML document. Both methods place their element in the `head`, so the `head` element shall not contain more",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "HTML can associate a Manifest Store through an inline script element or, preferably, an external link element, both using application/c2pa in the head. There shall be at most one association per document, elements outside the head shall be ignored, and multiple manifest elements in the head shall cause the asset to be treated as having no manifests.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s618-a-7-1-1-embedded-inline-manifests",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.7.1.1. Embedded (inline) manifests",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s618-a-7-1-1-embedded-inline-manifests.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.7.1.1. Embedded (inline) manifests\n\nWhen embedding the C2PA Manifest Store into the HTML document, it shall be embedded as the Base64-encoded (per [RFC 4648](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4648), Section 4) content of a `script` element with `type=\"application/c2pa\"` placed in the `head` of the HTML document. When performing validation, the validator shall strip leading and trailing whitespace from the `script` element’s text content before Base64 decoding.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Browsers ignore `script` elements with unrecognized types, and this approach follows the established HTML patter",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "An embedded HTML manifest store must be placed, Base64-encoded, in a script element of type application/c2pa in the document head, and validators must strip surrounding whitespace before decoding, with an example document shown.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s619-a-7-1-2-external-referenced-manifests",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.7.1.2. External (referenced) manifests",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s619-a-7-1-2-external-referenced-manifests.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.7.1.2. External (referenced) manifests\n\nWhen referencing the C2PA Manifest Store, a `link` element with an attribute of `rel=\"c2pa-manifest\"`, placed in the `head` of the HTML document, shall be used to reference an external C2PA Manifest Store via its `href` attribute. The `type=\"application/c2pa\"` attribute should be included but is not required for discovery; the validator shall match on the `rel` attribute alone. The `c2pa-manifest` link relation is registered in the [IANA Link Relations registry](https://www.iana.org/assignments/link-relations/). The external manifest store shall",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A referenced HTML manifest store must be linked from the document head by a link element with rel=\"c2pa-manifest\" and an href, which validators match on alone (type=\"application/c2pa\" is recommended), and the external store must carry a content binding, with an example document shown.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s620-a-7-1-3-hard-binding",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.7.1.3. Hard Binding",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s620-a-7-1-3-hard-binding.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.7.1.3. Hard Binding\n\nA claim generator embedding a C2PA Manifest Store in an HTML document shall include a [`c2pa.hash.data`](#_data_hash) assertion.\n\nFor an embedded `script` element, the data hash assertion shall include a single exclusion range covering the entire element from the opening `<script` tag through the closing `</script>` tag, inclusive. The hash shall be computed over the document content with the exclusion range removed.\n\nFor an external `link` element, the manifest is not embedded in the document. The data hash assertion shall have no exclusion range; the hash shall b",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A claim generator embedding a manifest store in HTML must include a c2pa.hash.data assertion, whose single exclusion range covers the whole script element when the manifest is embedded, and which has no exclusion range when the manifest is referenced by a link element. A note explains that the hash covers the stored bytes, so any re-serialisation of the HTML invalidates the binding by design, and advises embedding after final serialisation or using an external manifest.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s621-a-7-1-4-validator-behaviour",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.7.1.4. Validator Behaviour",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s621-a-7-1-4-validator-behaviour.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.7.1.4. Validator Behaviour\n\nA validator encountering an HTML document (`text/html`) shall perform the following steps:\n\n1.  Treating the file as a series of bytes (vs. text), the validator shall parse the `head` element, searching for a `script` element with `type=\"application/c2pa\"` or a `link` element with `rel=\"c2pa-manifest\"`.\n    \n2.  If multiple matching elements are found, the document shall be treated as if no manifests were located.\n    \n3.  If no matching element is found, the document does not contain an HTML-embedded manifest.\n    \n4.  If a `script` element is found, Base64",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Validators of text/html documents must parse the head as bytes for an application/c2pa script element or a c2pa-manifest link element, treat multiple matches as no manifest, and Base64-decode a script element's content. Resolving a link's external URI is optional, and any obtained manifest store is then validated through the normal validation process.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
