      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.8.3.1. Byte-to-Variation-Selector Conversion",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s629-a-8-3-1-byte-to-variation-selector-conversion.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.8.3.1. Byte-to-Variation-Selector Conversion\n\nEach byte of the wrapped manifest shall be converted to a Unicode variation selector using the following algorithm:\n\n```python\nfunction byteToVariationSelector(byte b) {\n    if (b >= 0 && b <= 15) {\n        return U+FE00 + b;\n    } else if (b >= 16 && b <= 255) {\n        return U+E0100 + (b - 16);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n<a id=\"_variation_selector_to_byte_conversion\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Each wrapper byte must be converted to a variation selector, with bytes 0 to 15 mapping to U+FE00 onward and bytes 16 to 255 mapping to U+E0100 onward, as shown in pseudocode.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s630-a-8-3-2-variation-selector-to-byte-conversion",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.8.3.2. Variation-Selector-to-Byte Conversion",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s630-a-8-3-2-variation-selector-to-byte-conversion.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.8.3.2. Variation-Selector-to-Byte Conversion\n\nTo decode variation selectors back to bytes:\n\n```python\nfunction variationSelectorToByte(codepoint vs) {\n    if (vs >= U+FE00 && vs <= U+FE0F) {\n        return vs - U+FE00;\n    } else if (vs >= U+E0100 && vs <= U+E01EF) {\n        return (vs - U+E0100) + 16;\n    } else {\n        return INVALID;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n<a id=\"_encoding_example\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the pseudocode for decoding variation selectors back to bytes, inverting the two ranges U+FE00 to U+FE0F and U+E0100 to U+E01EF and returning INVALID for any other code point.",
        "state": "draft",
