      "title": "A.8.4.1. Placement Rules",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s633-a-8-4-1-placement-rules.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.8.4.1. Placement Rules\n\nThe `C2PATextManifestWrapper` shall be embedded according to the following rules:\n\n1.  The wrapper shall be embedded as a single, contiguous block of variation selectors.\n    \n2.  The wrapper shall be immediately preceded by a single Zero-Width No-Break Space (U+FEFF), which marks the start of the wrapper for detection (see [Section A.8.4.2, “Detection Algorithm”](#text_manifest_detection_algorithm)). This marker is part of the wrapper for the purpose of content binding, so the `c2pa.hash.data` exclusion range covers the marker together with the variation-select",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The wrapper must be a single contiguous, unsplit run of variation selectors immediately preceded by a U+FEFF marker, which counts as part of the wrapper for the c2pa.hash.data exclusion, and should be placed at the end of the visible text. A claim generator should embed at most one wrapper, and a validator finding more than one valid wrapper must treat the asset as having no manifests.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
