      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.8.5. Deterministic Wrapper Padding",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s635-a-8-5-deterministic-wrapper-padding.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.8.5. Deterministic Wrapper Padding\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> The UTF-8 byte length of a `C2PATextManifestWrapper` depends on the byte distribution of the encoded manifest. Bytes in the range 0x00-0x0F map to base Variation Selectors (U+FE00-U+FE0F), which encode to 3 UTF-8 bytes. Bytes in the range 0x10-0xFF map to supplementary Variation Selectors (U+E0100-U+E01EF), which encode to 4 UTF-8 bytes. Because the `c2pa.hash.data` exclusion must specify the wrapper’s byte range, and the hash value influences the manifest bytes, a circular dependency exists between the exclusion length and the wrapper b",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A note explains that a wrapper's UTF-8 length depends on how many bytes map to 3-byte versus 4-byte variation selectors, creating a circular dependency between the c2pa.hash.data exclusion length and the manifest bytes, which deterministic padding resolves by deriving the length from the manifest byte count alone.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
