    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s636-a-8-5-1-worst-case-encoding-formula",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.8.5.1. Worst-Case Encoding Formula",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s636-a-8-5-1-worst-case-encoding-formula.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.8.5.1. Worst-Case Encoding Formula\n\nFor a manifest of _M_ bytes, the deterministic target wrapper byte length is:\n\n```python\nHEADER_SIZE = 8 + 1 + 4    // magic + version + manifestLength (13)\nE_target = 3 + (HEADER_SIZE + M) * 4 + 6\n```\n\nWhere:\n\n*   `3` = UTF-8 byte length of the ZWNBSP prefix (U+FEFF)\n    \n*   `HEADER_SIZE` = 8 (magic) + 1 (version) + 4 (manifestLength) = 13 bytes\n    \n*   `4` = maximum UTF-8 byte length per Variation Selector character\n    \n*   `6` = padding margin to guarantee the gap between the target and the actual unpadded wrapper length is always expressible a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines the deterministic target wrapper byte length for an M-byte manifest as 3 + (13 + M) * 4 + 6, covering the U+FEFF prefix, the 13-byte header, the worst case of 4 bytes per selector, and a margin of 6. Notes explain that the margin guarantees the gap to the actual length can always be expressed as a combination of 3s and 4s, aided by the low-range bytes always present in the header.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s637-a-8-5-2-claim-generator-procedure",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
