      "target": "../sections/s637-a-8-5-2-claim-generator-procedure.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.8.5.2. Claim Generator Procedure\n\nA claim generator embedding a `C2PATextManifestWrapper` should use the following procedure to produce a deterministic exclusion length:\n\n1.  Build the C2PA Manifest Store with `exclusion_length` set to 0 (placeholder).\n    \n2.  Compute `E = 3 + (HEADER_SIZE + M) * 4 + 6`, where _M_ is the manifest byte count and `HEADER_SIZE` is 13.\n    \n3.  Rebuild the Manifest Store with `exclusion_length = E` in the `c2pa.hash.data` assertion.\n    \n4.  If the manifest byte count changed (due to CBOR integer width change), recompute `E` and repeat step 3. This conver",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A claim generator should build the manifest store with a placeholder exclusion_length, compute the target length E, rebuild with exclusion_length set to E (repeating once if the CBOR integer width changes), and encode the wrapper. It then fills the gap between E and the actual length with a fixed number of 0x00 and 0x10 padding bytes, so that compliant generators produce byte-identical wrappers.",
