      "target": "../sections/s641-a-8-6-3-exclusion-handling.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "##### A.8.6.3. Exclusion Handling\n\nThe `exclusions` field in the `c2pa.hash.data` assertion uses byte offsets in the UTF-8 encoded text as stored, before NFC normalization is applied. Normalization is performed on the text that remains after the excluded bytes have been removed, as specified in [Section 14.12.1.3.1, “Validating a text data hash”](#validating_a_text_data_hash). Implementations shall be careful to:\n\n1.  Calculate offsets against the text as stored, not against its normalized form\n    \n2.  Work with byte offsets, not character offsets\n    \n3.  Validate that excluded regions encom",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The c2pa.hash.data exclusions use byte offsets into the stored UTF-8 text before NFC normalisation, and implementations must compute byte (not character) offsets against the stored text and ensure the exclusion covers the whole wrapper, including the U+FEFF marker and any padding.",
        "state": "draft",
