    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s661-a-10-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.10.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s661-a-10-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.10.1. General\n\nThe Web ARChive (WARC) format ([ISO 28500:2017](https://www.iso.org/standard/68004.html)) is used by national libraries, legal deposit systems, and digital preservation institutions to archive web content. A WARC file is a sequential concatenation of records, each containing a captured resource (such as an HTTP response) along with metadata about the capture. The format supports incremental appending of new records.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> This section applies to WARC 1.1 files as defined by [ISO 28500:2017](https://www.iso.org/standard/68004.html). WARC 1.0 files use the same rec",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines how to embed a C2PA Manifest Store in WARC files (application/warc), the archive format of concatenated capture records, applying to WARC 1.1 and optionally WARC 1.0. Notes say this in-band provenance complements existing fixity practices and contrast its signing model with WACZ, PREMIS and BagIt.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s662-a-10-2-placement-of-the-manifest-store",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.10.2. Placement of the Manifest Store",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s662-a-10-2-placement-of-the-manifest-store.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.10.2. Placement of the Manifest Store\n\nThe C2PA Manifest Store shall be stored as the block of a WARC record of a dedicated record type with the following header fields:\n\n*   `WARC-Type`: `c2pa-provenance`\n    \n*   `Content-Type`: `application/c2pa`\n    \n*   `WARC-Date`: the time at which the manifest was created\n    \n*   `Content-Length`: the byte length of the C2PA Manifest Store\n    \n\nThe remaining required and optional header fields (including `WARC-Record-ID`) shall conform to [ISO 28500:2017](https://www.iso.org/standard/68004.html). The C2PA manifest record shall not carry a `WAR",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The manifest store must be the block of a dedicated WARC record with WARC-Type c2pa-provenance, Content-Type application/c2pa, the manifest creation time and its length, without a WARC-Target-URI, and validators identify it by those two type values. That record must be the last in the file and the only one of its kind, and updates must remove it and append a replacement, leaving other records' bytes and hashes unchanged.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s663-a-10-3-hashing",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.10.3. Hashing",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s663-a-10-3-hashing.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.10.3. Hashing\n\nA WARC file shall be hashed using a [collection data hash](#_collection_data_hash). Every WARC record in the file other than the C2PA manifest record shall be included as a member of the collection. The hash algorithm used shall be specified in the `alg` field of the collection data hash structure. The hash of each record shall be computed over the uncompressed bytes of that record, from the first byte of the version line through and including the two CRLF sequences that terminate the record, as defined by the `warc-record` production in [ISO 28500:2017](https://www.iso.o",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A WARC file must be hashed with a collection data hash covering every record except the manifest record, each hashed over its full uncompressed bytes including headers, and each entry's uri must be the record's WARC-Record-ID, which generators must check is unique. Continuation records are hashed individually and revisit records as they appear, without dereferencing.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s664-a-10-4-update-manifests-and-compressed-manifests",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.10.4. Update manifests and compressed manifests",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s664-a-10-4-update-manifests-and-compressed-manifests.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.10.4. Update manifests and compressed manifests\n\nThe block of the C2PA manifest record is a C2PA Manifest Store, so it may contain [update manifests](#_update_manifests), and any manifest it contains may be a [compressed manifest](#_compressed_manifests).\n\nAn update manifest is added to a WARC file by the update procedure in [Section A.10.2, “Placement of the Manifest Store”](#warc_placement): the existing C2PA manifest record is removed and the replacement, containing the update manifest, is appended as the new last record. Because the C2PA manifest record is not a member of the collec",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The WARC manifest record may contain update manifests and compressed manifests, and an update is added by removing and re-appending the manifest record, leaving the existing collection data hash binding valid since update manifests carry no content binding. Because records are identified by WARC-Record-ID rather than offset, the manifest record's offset and length may change, and manifest compression is independent of WARC record compression.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s665-a-10-5-compressed-warc-files",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.10.5. Compressed WARC files",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s665-a-10-5-compressed-warc-files.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.10.5. Compressed WARC files\n\nWARC files are commonly stored with per-record gzip compression, and other schemes such as WARC-zstd are also in use. Because each record’s hash is computed over its uncompressed bytes (see [Section A.10.3, “Hashing”](#warc_hashing)), the compression scheme does not affect the collection data hash. A record may be stored uncompressed, per-record compressed, or recompressed under a different scheme without invalidating its hash, provided its uncompressed content is unchanged. This applies equally to per-record gzip, whole-file gzip, and WARC-zstd, including i",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Because record hashes are computed over uncompressed bytes, records may be stored uncompressed or recompressed under per-record gzip, whole-file gzip or WARC-zstd without invalidating the collection data hash.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s666-a-10-6-concatenation-and-splitting",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.10.6. Concatenation and splitting",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s666-a-10-6-concatenation-and-splitting.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.10.6. Concatenation and splitting\n\nWhen WARC files are concatenated or split, the collection data hash of a pre-existing C2PA Manifest Store will no longer cover the correct set of records. A claim generator producing a combined WARC file shall remove any pre-existing C2PA manifest records from constituent files and append a new C2PA manifest record covering all other records in the resulting file. The pre-existing manifests may be referenced as ingredients.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n> Recompressing a record does not change its hash, because the hash covers uncompressed bytes. Any change to a record",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "When WARC files are concatenated or split, a claim generator must remove pre-existing manifest records and append a new one covering all remaining records, optionally citing the earlier manifests as ingredients, since any change to record content or the record set requires a new manifest store.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s667-a-10-7-validation-behaviour",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A.10.7. Validation Behaviour",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s667-a-10-7-validation-behaviour.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### A.10.7. Validation Behaviour\n\nRefer to the Validation clause for the normative procedures: [Special Considerations for WARC](#locating_active_manifest_warc) for locating the C2PA Manifest Store, and [Hashing of WARC files](#validating_a_warc_collection_hash) for validating the collection data hash.\n\n<a id=\"_user_experience\"></a>",
