      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Table 20 defines the validation failure codes, each with its meaning and the structure its url refers to, starting with algorithm.unsupported and a large set of assertion-level codes. These cover malformed or mismatched hard binding assertions (data, BMFF, boxes, collection, multi-asset and segment hash), action and ingredient reference problems, cloud data and external reference errors, linked resource integrity problems, missing, undeclared or wrongly redacted assertions, and multiple hard bindings. Claim and signature failures include claim.missing, claim.multiple, claim.hardBindings.missing, claim.actions.missing, claimSignature.mismatch and claimSignature.outsideValidity, alongside hashed URI and ingredient manifest or signature mismatches. Further codes address live video sessions, segments, initialization and session keys (with enumerated conditions for BMFF/CMAF and Enhanced RTMP), manifest-level problems such as inaccessible, encrypted or malformed manifest stores, multiple parents and invalid update manifests, and signing credential problems such as revocation or absence from trust lists, plus a catch-all general.error.",
