        "text": "Defines three status values for constructs whose status has changed: DEPRECATED (claim generators are required not to produce it while validators are encouraged to accept it), UNDEFINED (validators are required to ignore it), and blank for fully supported. Table 21 then gives the status of each manifest type, label, timestamp, assertion, field, digital source type, action, status code and claim field across versions 1.3 to 2.5, for example showing c2pa.claim, older ingredient and BMFF hash versions, stds.iptc and stds.exif as deprecated, with c2pa.hash.segment becoming defined only in 2.5. In 2.5 it newly deprecates templateParameters in action-template-map-v2, the string label x5chain COSE header, trustListUri and the c2pa.removed action.",
