        "text": "Summarizes version 2.1 (September 2024) as improving the security and reliability of Content Credentials, saying all publicly disclosed vulnerabilities were addressed. It lists definitions of well-formed, valid and trusted manifests and valid assets, deprecation and versioning processes, the c2pa URN namespace, the ingredients v3 and c2pa.hash.bmff.v3 assertions, time-stamp manifests and sigTst2 with a TSA trust list, detailed validation requirements and new status codes, hashing improvements, a separate embedding annex with JPEG-XL, action assertion changes, and editorial work towards ISO standardization.",
