      "target": "../sections/s705-f-6-2-0-january-2024.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### F.6. 2.0 - January 2024\n\nThis version represents a significant departure from previous versions. It reduces reliance on the term \"actor\" within the trust and validation model, shifting the basis for trust decisions away from identifying individual humans or organisations and toward the hardware and software components identified by X.509 certificates. In addition to validator-configured trust lists, it also introduces a new default trust list, the \"C2PA Trust List\", which is intended to cover certificates issued to hardware and software. This philosophical change led to the following funct",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Summarizes version 2.0 (January 2024) as shifting trust decisions away from identifying humans or organizations toward hardware and software identified by X.509 certificates, adding a default C2PA Trust List and allowing only X.509 certificates for signing. It lists the well-formed and valid manifest concepts, the reworked c2pa.metadata approach replacing the Exif, IPTC and Schema.org assertions, removal of W3C Verifiable Credentials, actors, training and data mining and endorsement assertions, a v2 claim with created_assertions and gathered_assertions and a single claim generator, and other changes such as removing c2pa.hash.bmff and adding c2pa.watermarked.",
        "state": "draft",
