    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s717-g-3-1-hashed-uri",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "G.3.1. Hashed URI",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s717-g-3-1-hashed-uri.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### G.3.1. Hashed URI\n\n```cddl\n; The data structure used to store a reference to a URL within the same JUMBF\n; and its hash. We use a socket/plug here to allow hashed-uri-map to be used in\n; individual files without having the map defined in the same file\n$hashed-uri-map /= {\n  \"url\": jumbf-uri-type, ; JUMBF URI reference\n\n  ; A string identifying the cryptographic hash algorithm used to compute all\n  ; hashes in this claim, taken from the C2PA hash algorithm identifier list. If\n  ; this field is absent, the hash algorithm is taken from an enclosing\n  ; structure as defined by that structure.",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for $hashed-uri-map, a reference to a location within the same JUMBF holding a url, an optional alg and a required hash, where alg falls back to an enclosing structure and the structure is invalid if no algorithm is found anywhere. It also defines jumbf-uri-type as a self#jumbf= string pattern, noting that &cbor= extensions were added in 2.5.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
