    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s718-g-3-2-hashed-external-uri",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "G.3.2. Hashed External URI",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s718-g-3-2-hashed-external-uri.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### G.3.2. Hashed External URI\n\n```cddl\n; The data structure used to store a reference to an external URL and its hash.\n; We use a socket/plug here to allow hashed-ext-uri-map to be used in individual\n; files without having the map defined in the same file\n$hashed-ext-uri-map /= {\n  \"url\": ext-url-type, ; http/https URL\n\n  ; A string identifying the cryptographic hash algorithm used to compute the\n  ; hash on this URI's data, taken from the C2PA hash algorithm identifier list.\n  ; Unlike alg fields in other types, this field is mandatory here.\n  \"alg\": tstr .size (1..max-tstr-length),\n  \"hash",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for $hashed-ext-uri-map, which references an external http or https URL with a mandatory alg and hash plus optional dc:format, size and data_types. It also defines ext-url-type as a regular expression for http and https URLs.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s719-g-3-3-unhashed-external-uri",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "G.3.3. Unhashed External URI",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s719-g-3-3-unhashed-external-uri.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### G.3.3. Unhashed External URI\n\n```cddl\n; The data structure used to store a reference to an external URI WITHOUT a\n; hash. This might include, for example, http/https reference or URI reference\n; to a smart contract under CAIP-10 convention\nunhashed-ext-uri-map = {\n  \"url\": tstr, ; URI reference\n  ? \"dc:format\": format-string, ; IANA media type of the data\n  ? \"size\": size-type, ; Number of bytes of data\n\n  ; additional information about the data's type\n  ? \"data_types\": [1* asset-type-map],\n}\n```\n\n<a id=\"cddl_annex_uri_hashed_data\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for unhashed-ext-uri-map, a reference to an external URI without a hash (for example an http link or a CAIP-10 smart contract reference) with optional dc:format, size and data_types.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s720-g-3-4-uri-hashed-data",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "G.3.4. URI Hashed Data",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s720-g-3-4-uri-hashed-data.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### G.3.4. URI Hashed Data\n\n```cddl\n; The data structure used to store a reference to a URI and its hash.\n$uri-hashed-data-map /= {\n  \"uri\": relative-url-type, ; relative URI reference\n  \"hash\": bstr, ; byte string containing the hash value\n  ? \"size\": size-type, ; Number of bytes of data\n  ? \"dc:format\": format-string, ; IANA media type of the data\n\n  ; additional information about the data's type\n  ? \"data_types\": [1* asset-type-map],\n}\n\n; An RFC 3986 relative-reference with no scheme and no authority: excludes\n; \":\" (which would indicate a scheme) entirely, and permits at most one\n; leadin",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the CDDL for $uri-hashed-data-map, which pairs a relative uri with a hash and optional size, dc:format and data_types. It defines relative-url-type as an RFC 3986 relative reference with no scheme or authority, noting that percent-encoded traversal sequences are syntactically allowed and that rejecting them is left to validation rather than the schema.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
