      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "G.4.7. Segment Hash",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s728-g-4-7-segment-hash.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### G.4.7. Segment Hash\n\n```cddl\n; Segment hash assertion for append-only plain-text files.\n; Carries the byte-exact binding between a signed checkpoint manifest\n; and its covered segment, together with a cryptographic digest of the\n; immediately preceding sentinel line so that historical sentinels cannot\n; be rewritten without invalidating the chain.\n\nsegment-hash-map = {\n  ; Version of this assertion format. Always 1 for this version of the specification.\n  \"version\": 1,\n\n  ; A string identifying the cryptographic hash algorithm used to compute both\n  ; \"hash\" and predecessorSentinel.hash,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines segment-hash-map, a segment hash assertion for append-only plain-text files that binds a signed checkpoint manifest byte-exactly to its covered segment, with version fixed at 1, an optional alg resolved as in other hash structures, the hash of bytes from segmentStart to segmentEnd, an optional sentinelLength (present only when the sentinel references an external URI) and optional metadata. Every checkpoint after the first must carry predecessorSentinel, whose start, length and hash fields must all appear together and authenticate the immediately preceding sentinel line, so that earlier sentinels cannot be rewritten without breaking the chain.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
