      "target": "../sections/s730-g-5-1-actions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### G.5.1. Actions\n\n```cddl\n; Structural definitions for actions assertions.\n; Pre-defined action names are in action-choices.cddl (generated from actions.yaml).\n\naction-time-exact-group = (\n  ? \"when\": tdate ; exact action time\n)\n\naction-time-range-group = (\n  ? \"whenStart\": generator-lower-bound-time-type, ; exact action start or lower bound\n  ? \"whenEnd\": generator-upper-bound-time-type ; exact action end or upper bound\n)\n\n; Version 2 (v2) of the actions assertion\n\n$action-reason /= \"c2pa.PII.present\"\n$action-reason /= \"c2pa.invalid.data\"\n$action-reason /= \"c2pa.trade-secret.present\"\n$acti",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines version 2 of the actions assertion, actions-map-v2, with a required actions list and allActionsIncluded flag (previously optional) plus optional templates, softwareAgents and metadata, and it lists reason values such as c2pa.PII.present and c2pa.trade-secret.present. Each action item names the action, may carry a software agent or index, description and digitalSourceType, either an exact when time or a whenStart/whenEnd range (mutually exclusive), changed regions, related actions, and parameters such as redacted, ingredients, relatedAssertions, source and target languages for translation, name and multipleInstances, with reason and redacted required for c2pa.redacted. Action templates may use the \"*\" wildcard, an icon and parameters, with the older templateParameters deprecated and to be merged as if it were parameters, and the block also gives the deprecated version 1 actions-map, whose items use a string softwareAgent, a semicolon-delimited changed field, instanceID and a single ingredient parameter.",
