      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "G.5.10. Regions of Interest",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s739-g-5-10-regions-of-interest.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### G.5.10. Regions of Interest\n\n```cddl\nregion-map = {\n    ; definition of the range, one or more ranges\n    \"region\":        [1* range-map],\n\n    ; a free-text string representing a human-readable name for the region which\n    ; could be used in a user interface.\n    ? \"name\": tstr .size (1..max-tstr-length),\n\n    ; a free-text string representing a machine-readable, unique to this\n    ; assertion, identifier for the region.\n    ? \"identifier\": tstr .size (1..max-tstr-length),\n    ? \"type\":     tstr .size (1..max-tstr-length), ; from a controlled list\n    ? \"role\":     $role-choice, ; DEPRE",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines region-map, which describes a region of interest through one or more ranges together with optional name, identifier, type, description and metadata fields, and a role field that is marked deprecated. Each range has a type of spatial, temporal, frame, textual or identified, with matching shape, time, frame, text or item details, where a shape is a rectangle, circle or polygon measured in pixels or percent from an origin, with an optional inside flag. Times are either NPT or wall-clock (start inclusive, end exclusive unless endInclusivity says inclusive), frames cover video frames or document pages, text ranges use fragment-based selectors modelled on W3C Web Annotation, and identified ranges pair a container-specific identifier such as track_id with a value.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
