      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines depthmap-gdepth-map, an assertion holding a GDepth-format 3D depth map of the captured scene, which requires GDepth:Format (RangeInverse by default, or RangeLinear), GDepth:Near, GDepth:Far, GDepth:Mime and base64 GDepth:Data. Optional fields cover units (m or mm), measurement type (OpticalAxis or OpticRay), a confidence image and its type, the device manufacturer, model and software, and the original colour image's width and height, which apps must update when scaling, cropping or rotating that image.",
