      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### H.1. `dataSource` Field in Assertion Metadata\n\n> **IMPORTANT:**\n> The `dataSource` field in assertion metadata is deprecated. Claim generators shall not include a `dataSource` field in assertion metadata. Validators shall continue to accept the field for backwards compatibility.\n\nA previous version of this specification defined a `dataSource` field in the assertion metadata structure to convey the origin of assertion data. No known implementations used this field, and the distinctions it expressed are better addressed through the conformance and attestation mechanisms defined elsewhere in",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The dataSource field in assertion metadata is deprecated: claim generators shall not include it, while validators shall still accept it, because no known implementations used it. The block describes its former structure, a type drawn from a table of values such as signer, claimGenerator.REE, localProvider.TEE, remoteProvider, remoteProvider.external and humanEntry (or an entity-specific namespace), and a human-readable details string.",
