      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s765-h-2-string-label-x5chain.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### H.2. String Label `x5chain`\n\n> **IMPORTANT:**\n> Use of the string label `x5chain` for the X.509 certificate chain COSE header is deprecated. Claim generators shall use the integer label `33` instead, as described in [Section 13.5, “X.509 Certificates”](#x509_certificates).\n\nA previous version of this specification required claim generators to write the string label `x5chain` for the certificate chain header parameter, to avoid a dependency on the integer label `33` being standardised. Integer label `33` has since been standardised by [RFC 9360](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9360), and",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The string label x5chain for the X.509 certificate chain COSE header is deprecated, so claim generators shall use integer label 33, now standardised by RFC 9360, while validators shall still accept the string label.",
