      "target": "../sections/s766-h-3-data-boxes.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### H.3. Data Boxes\n\n> **IMPORTANT:**\n> This section is retained for historical purposes. The concept of a data box has been deprecated in favour of a standard assertion that uses a standard JUMBF Embedded File content type box to contain the data. For more information, see [Section 16.6.6, “Embedded Data”](#_embedded_data).\n\n<a id=\"_general_25\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The note says data boxes are deprecated and kept only for historical reference, replaced by a standard assertion that holds data in a JUMBF Embedded File content type box.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s767-h-3-1-general",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "H.3.1. General",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s767-h-3-1-general.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### H.3.1. General\n\nData boxes provide a way to include arbitrary data into the C2PA Manifest that is referenced from an assertion, instead of embedding it directly into a field of the assertion as a binary string. These data boxes are placed in the [Data Box Store](#_data_box_store) and each one will be a single CBOR Content Type box (`cbor`).\n\nThe data of a data box is provided directly as the value of the `data` field, which is a `bstr`, so any binary data can be provided. The type of the data shall be identified using the `dc:format` field, with a standard IANA media type.\n\n> **NOTE:**\n>",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Data boxes let arbitrary data referenced from an assertion be placed in the Data Box Store as single CBOR content type boxes, with the binary data in the data field, its type identified by an IANA media type in dc:format (structured suffixes such as +json are allowed), and optional asset types in data_types. A data box shall have the label c2pa.data and follows the usual assertion label rules for multiple instances.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s768-h-3-2-schema-and-example",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "H.3.2. Schema and Example",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s768-h-3-2-schema-and-example.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### H.3.2. Schema and Example\n\nThe schema for this type is defined by the `data-box-map` rule in the [CDDL Definition](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610) in [CDDL for data box](#cddl_for_data_box).:\n\nCDDL for data box\n\n```cddl\n; box allowing for the storage of arbitrary data\n\ndata-box-map = {\n  \"dc:format\": format-string, ; IANA media type of the data\n  \"data\" : bstr, ; arbitrary text/binary data\n\n  ; additional information about the data's type\n  ? \"data_types\": [1* asset-type-map],\n}\n```\n\n<a id=\"_data_box_store\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The CDDL defines data-box-map, which holds an IANA media type in dc:format, arbitrary data as a byte string and optional data_types.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s769-h-4-data-box-store",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "H.4. Data Box Store",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s769-h-4-data-box-store.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### H.4. Data Box Store\n\n> **IMPORTANT:**\n> This section is retained for historical purposes. The concept of a data box has been deprecated in favor of a standard assertion that uses a standard JUMBF Embedded File content type box to contain the data. For more information about the embedded data assertion, see [Section 16.6.6, “Embedded Data”](#_embedded_data).\n\nA C2PA Data Box Store is a JUMBF superbox that shall contain only one or more CBOR Content Type boxes (`cbor`). It shall not contain any other type of JUMBF box or superbox. It shall have a label of `c2pa.databoxes` and a JUMBF type UU",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The deprecated, historical Data Box Store is a JUMBF superbox that shall contain only CBOR content type boxes labelled c2pa.data, and shall itself have the label c2pa.databoxes and the c2db type UUID, and the block also includes a figure of a manifest store with data boxes.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s770-h-5-action-c2pa-removed",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "H.5. Action `c2pa.removed`",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s770-h-5-action-c2pa-removed.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### H.5. Action `c2pa.removed`\n\nA previous version of this specification allowed claim generators to write the action `c2pa.removed` for `componentOf` ingredients that have been removed. This action has since been deprecated in favour of using the `ingredient` field of the `c2pa.deleted` action. Claim generators shall not use the `c2pa.removed` action.\n\nValidators should continue to accept the `c2pa.removed` action for backwards compatibility.\n\n<a id=\"_validation_rule\"></a>",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The c2pa.removed action, formerly used for removed componentOf ingredients, is deprecated in favour of the ingredient field of c2pa.deleted, so claim generators shall not use it, though validators should still accept it.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/c2pa-2026-specification-2-5/blocks/prose-s771-h-5-1-validation-rule",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "H.5.1. Validation rule",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s771-h-5-1-validation-rule.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "#### H.5.1. Validation rule\n\nCheck that the `ingredients` field (or `ingredient` field for `c2pa.actions`) contains one or more valid hashed URIs, each of which can be resolved to an ingredient assertion in another manifest whose `relationship` field is `componentOf`. If not, then the claim shall be rejected with a failure code of `assertion.action.ingredientMismatch`.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The validation rule requires that the ingredients (or, for c2pa.actions, ingredient) field hold one or more valid hashed URIs, each resolving to an ingredient assertion in another manifest whose relationship is componentOf, and otherwise the claim shall be rejected with assertion.action.ingredientMismatch.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
